{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-001", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Six-digit numbers with digit sum 27", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4926, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 771, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 44, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1952, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "55252", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "55252"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdada8442-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdaa9fe3a-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T22:55:07-0500", "answer": "I need to find the number of integers n with 1 \u2264 n \u2264 999999 whose decimal digits sum to exactly 27.\n\nSince 999999 has 6 digits, I need to count numbers from 1 to 999999 with digit sum 27. This is equivalent to counting 6-digit strings (allowing leading zeros) where digits sum to 27, then subtracting the case where all digits are 0 (which gives sum 0, not 27, so no adjustment needed for that).\n\nActually, let me be more careful. Numbers from 1 to 999999 can be represented as 6-digit strings with leading zeros allowed (from 000001 to 999999). The number 000000 = 0 is excluded, but it has digit sum 0, not 27, so it doesn't affect our count.\n\nSo I need: number of solutions to d\u2081 + d\u2082 + d\u2083 + d\u2084 + d\u2085 + d\u2086 = 27 where 0 \u2264 d\u1d62 \u2264 9 for each i.\n\nUsing inclusion-exclusion. First, count non-negative integer solutions without the upper bound: C(27+6-1, 6-1) = C(32, 5).\n\nThen subtract cases where some d\u1d62 \u2265 10. If d\u1d62 \u2265 10, let d\u1d62' = d\u1d62 - 10, so d\u1d62' \u2265 0. Then sum = 17, giving C(17+6-1, 5) = C(22, 5) solutions for each choice of which digit exceeds 9. There are C(6,1) = 6 such choices.\n\nAdd back cases where two digits \u2265 10: sum becomes 27-20 = 7, giving C(7+6-1, 5) = C(12, 5) for each pair. There are C(6,2) = 15 pairs.\n\nSubtract cases where three digits \u2265 10: sum becomes 27-30 = -3 < 0, so 0 solutions.\n\nSo the answer is:\nC(32,5) - 6\u00b7C(22,5) + 15\u00b7C(12,5)\n\nLet me compute:\n- C(32,5) = 32!/(5!\u00b727!) = (32\u00b731\u00b730\u00b729\u00b728)/(5\u00b74\u00b73\u00b72\u00b71) = (32\u00b731\u00b730\u00b729\u00b728)/120\n\n32\u00b731 = 992\n992\u00b730 = 29760\n29760\u00b729 = 863040\n863040\u00b728 = 24165120\n24165120/120 = 201376\n\n- C(22,5) = (22\u00b721\u00b720\u00b719\u00b718)/120 = (22\u00b721\u00b720\u00b719\u00b718)/120\n22\u00b721 = 462\n462\u00b720 = 9240\n9240\u00b719 = 175560\n175560\u00b718 = 3160080\n3160080/120 = 26334\n\n- C(12,5) = (12\u00b711\u00b710\u00b79\u00b78)/120 = 95040/120 = 792\n\nSo:\n201376 - 6\u00b726334 + 15\u00b7792\n= 201376 - 158004 + 11880\n= 201376 - 158004 = 43372\n43372 + 11880 = 55252\n\nLet me verify: 6\u00b726334 = 158004 \u2713\n15\u00b7792 = 11880 \u2713\n201376 - 158004 = 43372 \u2713\n43372 + 11880 = 55252 \u2713\n\nANSWER: 55252"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-005", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Divisible by exactly two of 4, 6 and 9", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4788, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 378, "reasoning_tokens": 76, "input_tokens": 56, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 723, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "83334", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "83334"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdb461770-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdaaa4c5c-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T22:55:07-0500", "answer": "Count integers divisible by each pair, but not by the third number:\n\n- **4 and 6, but not 9:** Their least common multiple is 12. Exclude multiples of 36:\n  \\[\n  \\left\\lfloor\\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{12}\\right\\rfloor-\n  \\left\\lfloor\\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{36}\\right\\rfloor\n  =83{,}333-27{,}777=55{,}556.\n  \\]\n\n- **6 and 9, but not 4:** Their least common multiple is 18. Again exclude multiples of 36:\n  \\[\n  \\left\\lfloor\\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{18}\\right\\rfloor-\n  \\left\\lfloor\\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{36}\\right\\rfloor\n  =55{,}555-27{,}777=27{,}778.\n  \\]\n\n- **4 and 9, but not 6:** Impossible, since every multiple of \\(\\operatorname{lcm}(4,9)=36\\) is also divisible by 6.\n\nThus the total is \\(55{,}556+27{,}778=83{,}334\\).\n\nANSWER: 83334"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-001", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Six-digit numbers with digit sum 27", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5447, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 289, "reasoning_tokens": 95, "input_tokens": 45, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 602, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "55252", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "55252"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdada8441-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdaa9fe3a-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T22:55:08-0500", "answer": "Write each integer as a six-digit string, allowing leading zeros. We must count solutions to\n\\[\nd_1+\\cdots+d_6=27,\\qquad 0\\le d_i\\le9.\n\\]\n(The all-zero string does not qualify, so including it causes no issue.)\n\nWithout the upper bounds, stars and bars gives \\(\\binom{32}{5}\\) solutions. By inclusion\u2013exclusion, subtract solutions with a digit at least \\(10\\), then add back those with two such digits. Three such digits would sum to at least \\(30\\), so no further terms are needed.\n\nThus the count is\n\\[\n\\binom{32}{5}-6\\binom{22}{5}+\\binom62\\binom{12}{5}\n=201376-158004+11880\n=55252.\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 55252"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-005", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Divisible by exactly two of 4, 6 and 9", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4912, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 910, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 55, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 2264, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "83334", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "83334"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdb461772-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdaaa4c5c-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T22:55:08-0500", "answer": "I need to find integers n in [1, 1,000,000] divisible by exactly two of {4, 6, 9}.\n\nFirst, let me find the LCMs:\n- lcm(4, 6) = 12\n- lcm(4, 9) = 36\n- lcm(6, 9) = 18\n- lcm(4, 6, 9) = 36\n\nFor \"exactly two,\" I need to use inclusion-exclusion carefully.\n\nLet me define:\n- A = divisible by 4 and 6 (i.e., by 12), but NOT by 9\n- B = divisible by 4 and 9 (i.e., by 36), but NOT by 6... wait, if divisible by 4 and 9, then divisible by 36, and 36 is divisible by 6? No, 36/6 = 6, so yes, 36 is divisible by 6.\n\nLet me check: if n is divisible by 4 and 9, then n is divisible by lcm(4,9) = 36. Is 36 divisible by 6? Yes. So any number divisible by 4 and 9 is automatically divisible by 6.\n\nSo \"divisible by 4 and 9 but not 6\" is impossible!\n\nLet me verify: divisible by 4 and 9 means divisible by 36. And 36 = 6 \u00d7 6, so yes, divisible by 6.\n\nSo the pairs:\n- Divisible by 4 and 6, not by 9: divisible by 12, not by 9\n- Divisible by 4 and 9, not by 6: impossible (empty set)\n- Divisible by 6 and 9, not by 4: divisible by 18, not by 4\n\nWait, let me check: divisible by 6 and 9 means divisible by lcm(6,9) = 18. Is every multiple of 18 divisible by 4? No, e.g., 18 is not divisible by 4.\n\nSo I need:\n- Count of multiples of 12 that are NOT multiples of 9 (i.e., not multiples of 36)\n- Count of multiples of 18 that are NOT multiples of 4 (i.e., not multiples of 36)\n\nNote: multiples of 36 are divisible by all three, so they're excluded from both.\n\n**Case 1: Divisible by 4 and 6, not by 9**\nMultiples of 12: \u230a1,000,000/12\u230b = 83,333\nMultiples of 36 (divisible by all three): \u230a1,000,000/36\u230b = 27,777\nCount = 83,333 - 27,777 = 55,556\n\n**Case 2: Divisible by 6 and 9, not by 4**\nMultiples of 18: \u230a1,000,000/18\u230b = 55,555\nMultiples of 36 (divisible by all three): \u230a1,000,000/36\u230b = 27,777\nCount = 55,555 - 27,777 = 27,778\n\n**Case 3: Divisible by 4 and 9, not by 6**\nAs established, this is impossible since lcm(4,9) = 36 and 36 is divisible by 6.\nCount = 0\n\nTotal = 55,556 + 27,778 + 0 = 83,334\n\nLet me double-check my calculations:\n- 1,000,000 / 12 = 83,333.333... \u2192 83,333 \u2713\n- 1,000,000 / 36 = 27,777.777... \u2192 27,777 \u2713\n- 1,000,000 / 18 = 55,555.555... \u2192 55,555 \u2713\n\nCase 1: 83,333 - 27,777 = 55,556 \u2713\nCase 2: 55,555 - 27,777 = 27,778 \u2713\n\nTotal: 55,556 + 27,778 = 83,334\n\nANSWER: 83334"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-006", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Four dice: max is twice the min", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4175, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 296, "reasoning_tokens": 81, "input_tokens": 61, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 531, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "29/216", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "29/216"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdbc4965d-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdaaa736d-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T22:55:08-0500", "answer": "Let the smallest value be \\(m\\). The largest must be \\(2m\\), so \\(m\\) can only be \\(1,2,\\) or \\(3\\).\n\nFor each case, count ordered rolls with all values in \\([m,2m]\\), including both endpoints. By inclusion-exclusion:\n\n- Minimum \\(1\\), maximum \\(2\\): \\(2^4-2(1^4)=14\\).\n- Minimum \\(2\\), maximum \\(4\\): \\(3^4-2(2^4)+1^4=50\\).\n- Minimum \\(3\\), maximum \\(6\\): \\(4^4-2(3^4)+2^4=110\\).\n\nThese cases are disjoint, giving \\(14+50+110=174\\) favorable rolls out of \\(6^4=1296\\). Thus\n\\[\nP=\\frac{174}{1296}=\\frac{29}{216}.\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 29/216"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-005", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Divisible by exactly two of 4, 6 and 9", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5339, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 419, "reasoning_tokens": 148, "input_tokens": 56, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 614, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "83334", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "83334"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdb461771-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdaaa4c5c-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T22:55:08-0500", "answer": "An integer divisible by both 4 and 9 is divisible by 36, hence also by 6. So it cannot qualify.\n\nThe qualifying integers are:\n- Multiples of 12 but not 36 (divisible by 4 and 6 only):\n  \\[\n  \\left\\lfloor\\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{12}\\right\\rfloor-\n  \\left\\lfloor\\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{36}\\right\\rfloor\n  =83{,}333-27{,}777=55{,}556.\n  \\]\n- Multiples of 18 but not 36 (divisible by 6 and 9 only):\n  \\[\n  \\left\\lfloor\\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{18}\\right\\rfloor-\n  \\left\\lfloor\\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{36}\\right\\rfloor\n  =55{,}555-27{,}777=27{,}778.\n  \\]\n\nThese cases are disjoint, giving \\(55{,}556+27{,}778=83{,}334\\).\n\nANSWER: 83334"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-008", "category": "reasoning", "title": "SLA deadline over the holidays", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2244, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 413, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 119, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1117, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "2026-12-30 12:30", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "2026-12-30 12:30"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdd71503d-d027-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdaaa736f-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T22:55:09-0500", "answer": "I need to find the deadline 20 business hours after Thursday, December 24, 2026 at 16:30.\n\nFirst, let me establish the business hours: Monday-Friday, 09:00-17:00 (8 hours per day).\nHolidays: December 25, 2026 (Friday) and January 1, 2027 (Friday).\n\nStarting point: Thursday, December 24, 2026 at 16:30.\n\n**Thursday, December 24, 2026:**\n- From 16:30 to 17:00 = 0.5 hours remaining\n- Hours used: 0.5\n- Hours remaining needed: 20 - 0.5 = 19.5\n\n**Friday, December 25, 2026:** Holiday - no business hours\n\n**Saturday, December 26, 2026:** Weekend - no business hours\n\n**Sunday, December 27, 2026:** Weekend - no business hours\n\n**Monday, December 28, 2026:**\n- Full day: 8 hours (09:00-17:00)\n- Hours used: 8\n- Hours remaining needed: 19.5 - 8 = 11.5\n\n**Tuesday, December 29, 2026:**\n- Full day: 8 hours\n- Hours used: 8\n- Hours remaining needed: 11.5 - 8 = 3.5\n\n**Wednesday, December 30, 2026:**\n- Need 3.5 hours\n- Start at 09:00, add 3.5 hours = 12:30\n- Hours used: 3.5\n- Hours remaining needed: 0\n\nLet me verify: 0.5 + 8 + 8 + 3.5 = 20 \u2713\n\nThe deadline is Wednesday, December 30, 2026 at 12:30.\n\nANSWER: 2026-12-30 12:30"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-001", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Six-digit numbers with digit sum 27", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6783, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 383, "reasoning_tokens": 187, "input_tokens": 45, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 588, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "55252", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "55252"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdada8444-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdaa9fe3a-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T22:55:09-0500", "answer": "Write each integer using six digits, allowing leading zeros. We need to count solutions to\n\\[\nd_1+\\cdots+d_6=27,\\qquad 0\\le d_i\\le9.\n\\]\nThe all-zero string is not counted, so the lower bound \\(n\\ge1\\) causes no issue.\n\nWithout the upper bounds, stars and bars gives \\(\\binom{32}{5}\\) solutions. By inclusion\u2013exclusion, subtract those with a digit at least \\(10\\), then add back those with two such digits. Three are impossible since their sum would be at least \\(30\\).\n\nThus the count is\n\\[\n\\binom{32}{5}-6\\binom{22}{5}+\\binom62\\binom{12}{5}\n=201376-158004+11880\n=55252.\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 55252"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-008", "category": "reasoning", "title": "SLA deadline over the holidays", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2615, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 160, "reasoning_tokens": 35, "input_tokens": 121, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 334, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "2026-12-30 12:30", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "2026-12-30 12:30"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdd71503c-d027-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdaaa736f-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T22:55:09-0500", "answer": "- Thursday, December 24: 16:30\u201317:00 counts as **0.5 hours**, leaving 19.5 hours.\n- December 25 is a holiday, followed by the weekend.\n- Monday, December 28: **8 hours**, leaving 11.5 hours.\n- Tuesday, December 29: **8 hours**, leaving 3.5 hours.\n- Wednesday, December 30: 3.5 hours after 09:00 is **12:30**.\n\nANSWER: 2026-12-30 12:30"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-002", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Seven-seat row logic puzzle", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6622, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 349, "reasoning_tokens": 205, "input_tokens": 172, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 433, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "Eli, Cai, Ben, Ana, Fay, Dev, Gus", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "Eli, Cai, Ben, Ana, Fay, Dev, Gus"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdbb0db68-d027-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdaa9fe38-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T22:55:10-0500", "answer": "The seating order is **Eli, Cai, Ben, Ana, Fay, Dev, Gus**.\n\nChecking the clues:\n- Ben (3) and Dev (6) have exactly two people between them.\n- Eli (1) and Gus (7) are not adjacent, and Gus is to Eli\u2019s right.\n- Cai (2) sits to the left of Fay (5), who sits to the left of Dev (6).\n- Ana (4) and Eli (1) have exactly two people between them.\n- Ana (4) sits immediately to the left of Fay (5).\n\nANSWER: Eli, Cai, Ben, Ana, Fay, Dev, Gus"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-003", "category": "reasoning", "title": "String rotate-and-shift trace", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 8065, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 568, "reasoning_tokens": 345, "input_tokens": 124, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 548, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "kywasurrz", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "kywasurrz"}, "workflow_id": "0sfjdacb1ae1-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjdaa9fe39-d027-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T22:55:10-0500", "answer": "Each iteration first rearranges `s`, then shifts the letters at even indices (`0, 2, 4, 6, 8`) forward by `i`, wrapping around the alphabet.\n\nStarting with `s = \"conductor\"`:\n\n| `i` | After `s[i:] + s[:i][::-1]` | After shifting even-indexed letters |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `onductorc` | `pneudtprd` |\n| 2 | `eudtpr dnp` (without the space: `eudtprdnp`) | `guftrrfnr` |\n| 3 | `trrfnrfug` | `wrufqriuj` |\n| 4 | `qriujfurw` | `urmunfyra` |\n| 5 | `fyranumru` | `kywasurrz` |\n\nThus `print(s)` prints `kywasurrz`, followed by a newline.\n\nANSWER: kywasurrz"}
