gaps are _ B _ C _ B _ C _, so 5 gaps. We need to place 4 A's in these 5 gaps, at most one per gap (to avoid AA adjacent). Number of ways: C(5,4) = 5.\n\nSimilarly for CBCB: 5 ways.\n\nSo for (A=4, B=2, C=2): 2 \u00d7 5 = 10 arrangements?\n\nWait, I need to check: can we put A's in a way that creates adjacency? No, since we put at most one A per gap, and gaps are separated by B or C, so A's are never adjacent. And B's and C's are already non-adjacent to themselves. So yes, 10 arrangements.\n\nBut wait - I need to verify I haven't missed arrangements where A's separate B's and C's differently. Actually, my approach assumes B's and C's are placed first with no two adjacent equal, then A's inserted. But what if the original arrangement has, say, B A C A B A C A? Here B's and C's aren't adjacent to each other in the \"skeleton.\"\n\nLet me reconsider. The skeleton approach: if I remove all A's, I get a sequence of B's and C's. For no two adjacent equal in the full string, we need:\n- No two "}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-004", "category": "coding", "title": "Next run time for a cron expression", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 14285, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1249, "reasoning_tokens": 173, "input_tokens": 377, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 4663, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj52058990-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db5859-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:05:46-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport calendar\nimport re\nfrom bisect import bisect_right\nfrom datetime import date, datetime, timedelta\n\n\ndef next_run(expr: str, after: str) -> str:\n    def parse_field(text: str, low: int, high: int) -> set[int]:\n        values = set()\n        for item in text.split(\",\"):\n            match = re.fullmatch(\n                r\"(\\*|[0-9]+(?:-[0-9]+)?)(?:/([0-9]+))?\", item\n            )\n            if match is None:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid cron item: {item!r}\")\n\n            base, step_text = match.groups()\n            # Strip leading zeroes before conversion to avoid Python's\n            # integer-string length limit for otherwise valid small values.\n            def number(s: str, maximum: int) -> int:\n                s = s.lstrip(\"0\") or \"0\"\n                bound = str(maximum)\n                if len(s) > len(bound) or (\n                    len(s) == len(bound) and s > bound\n                ):\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Value out of range: {item!r}\")\n                return int(s)\n\n            if base == \"*\":\n                start, end = low, high\n            elif \"-\" in base:\n                a, b = base.split(\"-\")\n                start = number(a, high)\n                end = number(b, high)\n            else:\n                if step_text is not None:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Steps on single numbers are invalid\")\n                start = end = number(base, high)\n\n            if not low <= start <= end <= high:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid range: {item!r}\")\n\n            step = 1\n            if step_text is not None:\n                normalized = step_text.lstrip(\"0\")\n                if not normalized:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Step must be positive\")\n                # Any step larger than the range produces only its start.\n                if len(normalized) > len(str(high - low + 1)):\n                    step = high - low + 1\n                else:\n                    step = min(int(normalized), high - low + 1)\n\n            values.update(range(start, end + 1, step))\n        return values\n\n    if not isinstance(expr, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"Expression must be a string\")\n\n    fields = expr.split()\n    if len(fields) != 5:\n        raise ValueError(\"Expected exactly five cron fields\")\n\n    minutes, hours, month_days, months, week_days = [\n        parse_field(field, low, high)\n        for field, (low, high) in zip(\n            fields, [(0, 59), (0, 23), (1, 31), (1, 12), (0, 6)]\n        )\n    ]\n\n    if not isinstance(after, str) or re.fullmatch(\n        r\"[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2} [0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}\", after\n    ) is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid timestamp\")\n    try:\n        start = datetime.fromisoformat(after)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid timestamp\") from exc\n\n    # Five calendar years, clamping February 29 to February 28 if needed.\n    # Searches near year 9999 stop at the representable datetime boundary.\n    if start.year <= 9994:\n        year = start.year + 5\n        day = min(start.day, calendar.monthrange(year, start.month)[1])\n        limit = start.replace(year=year, day=day)\n    else:\n        limit = datetime(9999, 12, 31, 23, 59)\n\n    dom_restricted = fields[2] != \"*\"\n    dow_restricted = fields[4] != \"*\"\n    times = sorted(hour * 60 + minute for hour in hours for minute in minutes)\n\n    current = start.date()\n    last_date = limit.date()\n\n    while current <= last_date:\n        if current.month in months:\n            dom_matches = current.day in month_days\n            dow_matches = (current.weekday() + 1) % 7 in week_days\n\n            if dom_restricted and dow_restricted:\n                day_matches = dom_matches or dow_matches\n            elif dom_restricted:\n                day_matches = dom_matches\n            elif dow_restricted:\n                day_matches = dow_matches\n            else:\n                day_matches = True\n\n            if day_matches:\n                index = (\n                  "}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-004", "category": "coding", "title": "Next run time for a cron expression", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.7647, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 15783, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1554, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 387, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 6887, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.7647, "total": 17, "failures": [{"test": "assert next_run(\"0 9 * * 1-5\", \"2026-10-24 10:00\") == \"2026-10-26 09:00\"", "line": 11, "error": "AssertionError: "}, {"test": "assert next_run(\"0 12 13 * 5\", \"2026-10-24 00:00\") == \"2026-10-30 12:00\"", "line": 14, "error": "AssertionError: "}, {"test": "assert next_run(\"5 4 * * 0\", \"2026-10-24 23:59\") == \"2026-10-25 04:05\"", "line": 15, "error": "AssertionError: "}, {"test": "assert next_run(\"0 0 * 2 1\", \"2026-10-24 00:00\") == \"2027-02-01 00:00\"", "line": 20, "error": "AssertionError: "}], "pass": false, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj52058992-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db5859-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:05:48-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\ndef next_run(expr: str, after: str) -> str:\n    # Parse the after time\n    try:\n        after_dt = datetime.strptime(after, \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\")\n    except ValueError:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid after time format\")\n\n    # Parse the cron expression\n    parts = expr.split()\n    if len(parts) != 5:\n        raise ValueError(\"Cron expression must have exactly 5 fields\")\n\n    minute_field, hour_field, day_of_month_field, month_field, day_of_week_field = parts\n\n    # Validate and parse each field\n    def parse_field(field: str, min_val: int, max_val: int) -> list:\n        if not field:\n            raise ValueError(\"Empty field\")\n\n        items = field.split(',')\n        result = []\n\n        for item in items:\n            if not item:\n                raise ValueError(\"Empty item in field\")\n\n            # Handle step patterns\n            step_match = re.fullmatch(r'^(?:\\*|(\\d+)-(\\d+))(/(\\d+))?$', item)\n            if step_match:\n                start, end, _, step = step_match.groups()\n                if step is not None:\n                    try:\n                        step = int(step)\n                    except ValueError:\n                        raise ValueError(\"Invalid step value\")\n                    if step < 1:\n                        raise ValueError(\"Step must be >= 1\")\n                else:\n                    step = 1\n\n                if start is None:  # It's '*'\n                    if step == 1:\n                        result.append((min_val, max_val, 1))\n                    else:\n                        result.append((min_val, max_val, step))\n                else:\n                    try:\n                        start = int(start)\n                        end = int(end)\n                    except ValueError:\n                        raise ValueError(\"Invalid range values\")\n                    if start > end:\n                        raise ValueError(\"Descending range\")\n                    if start < min_val or end > max_val:\n                        raise ValueError(\"Value out of range\")\n                    result.append((start, end, step))\n                continue\n\n            # Handle single number\n            try:\n                num = int(item)\n                if num < min_val or num > max_val:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Value out of range\")\n                result.append((num, num, 1))\n                continue\n            except ValueError:\n                pass\n\n            # Handle range without step\n            range_match = re.fullmatch(r'^(\\d+)-(\\d+)$', item)\n            if range_match:\n                start, end = range_match.groups()\n                try:\n                    start = int(start)\n                    end = int(end)\n                except ValueError:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Invalid range values\")\n                if start > end:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Descending range\")\n                if start < min_val or end > max_val:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Value out of range\")\n                result.append((start, end, 1))\n                continue\n\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid item in field: {item}\")\n\n        return result\n\n    try:\n        minute_ranges = parse_field(minute_field, 0, 59)\n        hour_ranges = parse_field(hour_field, 0, 23)\n        day_of_month_ranges = parse_field(day_of_month_field, 1, 31)\n        month_ranges = parse_field(month_field, 1, 12)\n        day_of_week_ranges = parse_field(day_of_week_field, 0, 6)\n    except ValueError as e:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid cron expression: {e}\")\n\n    # Check if day fields are unrestricted\n    day_of_month_unrestricted = (day_of_month_field == '*')\n    day_of_week_unrestricted = (day_of_week_field == '*')\n\n    # Find the next matching time\n    current = after_dt + timedelta(minutes=1)\n    max_time = after_dt + timedelta(days=5*365)  # 5 years\n\n    while current <= max_time:\n        # Check month\n        month_matches = Fals"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-002", "category": "coding", "title": "Semantic version range check", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.6316, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 15447, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1538, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 534, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 5320, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.6316, "total": 19, "failures": [{"test": "assert satisfies(\"1.2.3\", \"^1.0.0\")", "line": 10, "error": "TypeError: expected string or bytes-like object, got 'tuple'"}, {"test": "assert not satisfies(\"2.0.0\", \"^1.0.0\")", "line": 11, "error": "TypeError: expected string or bytes-like object, got 'tuple'"}, {"test": "assert satisfies(\"0.2.9\", \"^0.2.3\")", "line": 12, "error": "TypeError: expected string or bytes-like object, got 'tuple'"}, {"test": "assert not satisfies(\"0.3.0\", \"^0.2.3\")", "line": 13, "error": "TypeError: expected string or bytes-like object, got 'tuple'"}, {"test": "assert not satisfies(\"0.0.4\", \"^0.0.3\")", "line": 14, "error": "TypeError: expected string or bytes-like object, got 'tuple'"}], "pass": false, "load_error": null, "passed": 12}, "workflow_id": "0sfj52ca19ea-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db5857-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:05:48-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Optional\n\ndef satisfies(version: str, range_expr: str) -> bool:\n    if not range_expr.strip():\n        raise ValueError(\"empty range expression\")\n\n    # Parse the version\n    v = _parse_version(version)\n\n    # Split into comparator sets\n    sets = [s.strip() for s in range_expr.split('||')]\n    if not sets:\n        raise ValueError(\"empty range expression\")\n    for s in sets:\n        if not s:\n            raise ValueError(\"empty comparator set\")\n\n    # Check if any set is satisfied\n    for set_expr in sets:\n        comparators = []\n        for comp in re.split(r'\\s+', set_expr.strip()):\n            if not comp:\n                continue\n            comparators.append(_parse_comparator(comp))\n        if not comparators:\n            raise ValueError(\"empty comparator set\")\n        if all(_compare(v, op, _parse_version(ver)) for op, ver in comparators):\n            return True\n    return False\n\ndef _parse_version(version: str) -> Tuple[int, int, int, Optional[List[str]], Optional[List[str]]]:\n    # Regex for semantic version\n    pattern = r'^(\\d+)\\.(\\d+)\\.(\\d+)(?:-([0-9A-Za-z-]+(?:\\.[0-9A-Za-z-]+)*))?(?:\\+([0-9A-Za-z-]+(?:\\.[0-9A-Za-z-]+)*))?$'\n    match = re.fullmatch(pattern, version)\n    if not match:\n        raise ValueError(f\"malformed version: {version}\")\n\n    major = int(match.group(1))\n    minor = int(match.group(2))\n    patch = int(match.group(3))\n    prerelease = match.group(4).split('.') if match.group(4) else None\n    build = match.group(5).split('.') if match.group(5) else None\n\n    # Validate no leading zeros\n    if (len(match.group(1)) > 1 and match.group(1)[0] == '0') or \\\n       (len(match.group(2)) > 1 and match.group(2)[0] == '0') or \\\n       (len(match.group(3)) > 1 and match.group(3)[0] == '0'):\n        raise ValueError(f\"malformed version: {version}\")\n\n    return (major, minor, patch, prerelease, build)\n\ndef _parse_comparator(comp: str) -> Tuple[str, str]:\n    if comp == '*':\n        return ('>=', '0.0.0')\n\n    # Regex for comparator\n    pattern = r'^([=<>~^]*)(.+)$'\n    match = re.fullmatch(pattern, comp)\n    if not match:\n        raise ValueError(f\"malformed comparator: {comp}\")\n\n    op = match.group(1)\n    ver = match.group(2)\n\n    if not op:\n        op = '='\n\n    if op not in {'=', '>', '>=', '<', '<=', '^', '~'}:\n        raise ValueError(f\"unknown operator: {op}\")\n\n    if op in {'^', '~'}:\n        # Expand ^ and ~ operators\n        v = _parse_version(ver)\n        major, minor, patch, _, _ = v\n        if op == '^':\n            if major > 0:\n                upper = f\"{major + 1}.0.0\"\n            elif minor > 0:\n                upper = f\"0.{minor + 1}.0\"\n            else:\n                upper = f\"0.0.{patch + 1}\"\n            return ('>=', ver), ('<', upper)\n        elif op == '~':\n            upper = f\"{major}.{minor + 1}.0\"\n            return ('>=', ver), ('<', upper)\n    else:\n        return (op, ver)\n\ndef _compare(v1: Tuple[int, int, int, Optional[List[str]], Optional[List[str]]],\n             op: str,\n             v2: Tuple[int, int, int, Optional[List[str]], Optional[List[str]]]) -> bool:\n    # Compare two versions according to semver rules\n    major1, minor1, patch1, pre1, _ = v1\n    major2, minor2, patch2, pre2, _ = v2\n\n    # Compare main version\n    if major1 != major2:\n        return _compare_num(major1, op, major2)\n    if minor1 != minor2:\n        return _compare_num(minor1, op, minor2)\n    if patch1 != patch2:\n        return _compare_num(patch1, op, patch2)\n\n    # Compare prerelease\n    if pre1 is None and pre2 is None:\n        return _compare_num(0, op, 0)  # equal\n    elif pre1 is None:\n        return op in {'>', '>='}  # v1 is greater\n    elif pre2 is None:\n        return op in {'<', '<='}  # v1 is less\n    else:\n        # Compare prerelease identifiers\n        for id1, id2 in zip(pre1, pre2):\n            if id1 == id2:\n                continue\n            # Check if numeric\n            num1 = _is_numeric(id1)\n            num2 = _is_numeric("}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-018", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Two pipes, a drain and a 3/4 tank", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 19626, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 2084, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 109, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 5949, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "540", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "540"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj525445e8-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db0a32-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:05:52-0500", "answer": "Alright, let's tackle this problem step by step. I'll try to break it down to understand how the tank fills over time with the different pipes and the drain.\n\n### Understanding the Problem\n\nWe have a tank that's initially empty. There are three pipes involved:\n\n1. **Pipe A**: Fills the tank alone in 6 hours.\n2. **Pipe B**: Fills the tank alone in 9 hours.\n3. **Drain C**: Empties the tank alone in 12 hours.\n\nThe sequence of events is:\n\n1. Pipes A and B are opened together for the first 2 hours.\n2. After 2 hours, Pipe A is shut off, and Drain C is opened, while Pipe B continues to run.\n3. We need to find out how many minutes after the start the tank is exactly 3/4 full.\n\n### Calculating Rates\n\nFirst, let's determine the rates at which each pipe fills or empties the tank.\n\n- **Pipe A's filling rate**: If it fills the tank in 6 hours, then in 1 hour, it fills 1/6 of the tank.\n- **Pipe B's filling rate**: If it fills the tank in 9 hours, then in 1 hour, it fills 1/9 of the tank.\n- **Drain C's emptying rate**: If it empties the tank in 12 hours, then in 1 hour, it removes 1/12 of the tank.\n\n### Phase 1: First 2 Hours (Pipes A and B Open)\n\nDuring the first 2 hours, both Pipe A and Pipe B are open. So, their combined filling rate is:\n\nCombined rate = Rate of A + Rate of B = (1/6) + (1/9)\n\nTo add these, let's find a common denominator. The least common multiple of 6 and 9 is 18.\n\n- 1/6 = 3/18\n- 1/9 = 2/18\n\nSo, combined rate = 3/18 + 2/18 = 5/18 of the tank per hour.\n\nIn 2 hours, the amount filled is:\n\nAmount filled = Rate \u00d7 Time = (5/18) \u00d7 2 = 10/18 = 5/9 of the tank.\n\nSo, after 2 hours, the tank is 5/9 full.\n\n### Phase 2: After 2 Hours (Pipe B and Drain C Open, Pipe A Closed)\n\nAfter 2 hours, Pipe A is shut off, and Drain C is opened. Now, Pipe B is still running, and Drain C is emptying the tank.\n\nSo, the net rate is:\n\nNet rate = Rate of B - Rate of C = (1/9) - (1/12)\n\nAgain, find a common denominator. The least common multiple of 9 and 12 is 36.\n\n- 1/9 = 4/36\n- 1/12 = 3/36\n\nSo, net rate = 4/36 - 3/36 = 1/36 of the tank per hour.\n\nThis means that after the first 2 hours, the tank is filling at a rate of 1/36 per hour.\n\n### Determining When the Tank is 3/4 Full\n\nAt the end of 2 hours, the tank is 5/9 full. We want to find out how much more time is needed to reach 3/4 full.\n\nLet's see how much more we need to fill:\n\nDesired fill level = 3/4\nCurrent fill level = 5/9\n\nAmount needed = 3/4 - 5/9\n\nFind a common denominator for 4 and 9, which is 36.\n\n- 3/4 = 27/36\n- 5/9 = 20/36\n\nAmount needed = 27/36 - 20/36 = 7/36 of the tank.\n\nNow, the net filling rate in this phase is 1/36 per hour. So, the time needed to fill an additional 7/36 is:\n\nTime = Amount needed / Rate = (7/36) / (1/36) = 7 hours.\n\nWait a minute, that seems like a lot. Did I make a mistake here?\n\nLet me think again.\n\nIf the net rate is 1/36 per hour, then to fill 7/36, it would indeed take 7 hours. But that would mean the total time is 2 hours (first phase) + 7 hours (second phase) = 9 hours, which seems too long for the tank to be only 3/4 full.\n\nMaybe the issue is in interpreting the net rate. Let me re-examine the net rate after 2 hours.\n\nAfter 2 hours:\n- Pipe B is adding 1/9 per hour.\n- Drain C is removing 1/12 per hour.\nSo, net rate is 1/9 - 1/12 = (4 - 3)/36 = 1/36 per hour.\n\nThat seems correct. So, to go from 5/9 to 3/4, which is an increase of 7/36, at a rate of 1/36 per hour, it would take 7 hours.\n\nBut let's check the total fill after 9 hours:\n\nFirst 2 hours: 5/9\nNext 7 hours: 7 * (1/36) = 7/36\nTotal: 5/9 + 7/36 = 20/36 + 7/36 = 27/36 = 3/4\n\nThat checks out. So, the total time is 9 hours, which is 540 minutes.\n\nBut the answer seems too large. Maybe the issue is in the initial assumption about the net rate.\n\nWait, is the net rate positive or negative? If the net rate is positive, the tank is filling; if negative, it's emptying.\n\nHere, 1/9 (filling) - 1/12 (emptying) = 1/36, which is positive, so the tank is still filling, just very slowly.\n\nGiven that, the calculation see"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-001", "category": "coding", "title": "ISO 8601 duration to seconds", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 23939, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1422, "reasoning_tokens": 982, "input_tokens": 375, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1308, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj52a37772-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db3145-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:05:57-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\n\n_DURATION_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"P\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)Y)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)M)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)W)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)D)?\"\n    r\"(?:T\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)H)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)M)?\"\n    r\"(?:([0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)S)?\"\n    r\")?\"\n)\n\n\ndef parse_duration(s: str) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Convert an ISO 8601 duration to seconds using fixed unit lengths.\"\"\"\n    match = _DURATION_RE.fullmatch(s)\n    if match is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid duration format\")\n\n    values = match.groups()\n    if not any(value is not None for value in values):\n        raise ValueError(\"At least one component is required\")\n\n    if \"T\" in s and all(value is None for value in values[4:]):\n        raise ValueError(\"T must be followed by a time component\")\n\n    scales = (365 * 86400, 30 * 86400, 7 * 86400, 86400, 3600, 60, 1)\n    components = [\n        (value, scale)\n        for value, scale in zip(values, scales)\n        if value is not None\n    ]\n\n    if any(\".\" in value or \",\" in value for value, _ in components[:-1]):\n        raise ValueError(\"Only the last component may have a fractional part\")\n\n    return sum(\n        float(value.replace(\",\", \".\")) * scale\n        for value, scale in components\n    )\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-004", "category": "coding", "title": "Next run time for a cron expression", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 28410, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 5825, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 376, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 23066, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj5205627e-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db5859-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:06:01-0500", "answer": "Here's the complete solution:\n\n```python\nimport re\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\ndef next_run(expr: str, after: str) -> str:\n    # Parse the after time\n    try:\n        after_dt = datetime.strptime(after, \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\")\n    except ValueError:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid after format\")\n\n    # Parse and validate the cron expression\n    fields = expr.split()\n    if len(fields) != 5:\n        raise ValueError(\"Expression must have exactly 5 fields\")\n\n    minute_field, hour_field, dom_field, month_field, dow_field = fields\n\n    # Parse each field into a set of allowed values\n    def parse_field(field: str, min_val: int, max_val: int, field_name: str) -> set:\n        if not field:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Empty field: {field_name}\")\n\n        allowed = set()\n        items = field.split(',')\n\n        for item in items:\n            if not item:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Empty item in {field_name}\")\n\n            # Check for step\n            step = 1\n            base = item\n            if '/' in item:\n                parts = item.split('/')\n                if len(parts) != 2:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Invalid step format in {field_name}: {item}\")\n                base = parts[0]\n                step_str = parts[1]\n                if not step_str.isdigit():\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Invalid step in {field_name}: {item}\")\n                step = int(step_str)\n                if step < 1:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Step must be >= 1 in {field_name}: {item}\")\n\n            # Parse base\n            if base == '*':\n                start, end = min_val, max_val\n            elif '-' in base:\n                range_parts = base.split('-')\n                if len(range_parts) != 2:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Invalid range in {field_name}: {item}\")\n                start_str, end_str = range_parts\n                if not start_str.isdigit() or not end_str.isdigit():\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Invalid range in {field_name}: {item}\")\n                start = int(start_str)\n                end = int(end_str)\n                if start > end:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Descending range in {field_name}: {item}\")\n                if start < min_val or end > max_val:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Range out of bounds in {field_name}: {item}\")\n            else:\n                # Single number\n                if not base.isdigit():\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Invalid number in {field_name}: {item}\")\n                start = int(base)\n                end = start\n                if start < min_val or start > max_val:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Value out of bounds in {field_name}: {item}\")\n                # Step on single number is invalid (like 5/15)\n                if '/' in item:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Step on single number invalid in {field_name}: {item}\")\n\n            # Generate values\n            for v in range(start, end + 1, step):\n                allowed.add(v)\n\n        return allowed\n\n    minutes = parse_field(minute_field, 0, 59, \"minute\")\n    hours = parse_field(hour_field, 0, 23, \"hour\")\n    doms = parse_field(dom_field, 1, 31, \"day of month\")\n    months = parse_field(month_field, 1, 12, \"month\")\n    dows = parse_field(dow_field, 0, 6, \"day of week\")\n\n    # Check if fields are unrestricted (exactly \"*\")\n    dom_restricted = dom_field != '*'\n    dow_restricted = dow_field != '*'\n\n    # Search for next matching time\n    # Start from the minute after 'after'\n    current = after_dt + timedelta(minutes=1)\n    # Round down to minute (already at minute precision)\n\n    max_time = after_dt + timedelta(days=5 * 365 + 2)  # 5 years + leap days buffer\n\n    while current <= max_time:\n        # Check month\n        if current.month not in months:\n            # Move to first day of next month\n            if current.month == 12:\n                current = current.replace(year=current.year + 1, month=1, day=1, hour=0, minute"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-001", "category": "coding", "title": "ISO 8601 duration to seconds", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 29270, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 4995, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 372, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 19393, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj52a3776f-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db3145-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:06:02-0500", "answer": "Here's the complete function:\n\n```python\nimport re\n\ndef parse_duration(s: str) -> float:\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a string\")\n\n    # Pattern for the entire duration\n    # P followed by optional date components, then optional T with time components\n    pattern = re.compile(\n        r'^P'\n        r'(?:(\\d+(?:[.,]\\d+)?)Y)?'      # years\n        r'(?:(\\d+(?:[.,]\\d+)?)M)?'      # months\n        r'(?:(\\d+(?:[.,]\\d+)?)W)?'      # weeks\n        r'(?:(\\d+(?:[.,]\\d+)?)D)?'      # days\n        r'(?:T'\n        r'(?:(\\d+(?:[.,]\\d+)?)H)?'      # hours\n        r'(?:(\\d+(?:[.,]\\d+)?)M)?'      # minutes\n        r'(?:(\\d+(?:[.,]\\d+)?)S)?'      # seconds\n        r')?$'\n    )\n\n    match = pattern.match(s)\n    if not match:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid duration format: {s!r}\")\n\n    years, months, weeks, days, hours, minutes, seconds = match.groups()\n\n    # Check that at least one component is present\n    if all(g is None for g in match.groups()):\n        raise ValueError(\"Duration must have at least one component\")\n\n    # Check that if T is present, at least one time component follows\n    # The regex already ensures this structurally, but we need to verify\n    # that T isn't present with no time components\n    if 'T' in s:\n        # Find position of T\n        t_pos = s.index('T')\n        # Check if anything follows T\n        if t_pos == len(s) - 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"T must be followed by at least one time component\")\n        # Check that at least one of H, M, S is present after T\n        time_part = s[t_pos + 1:]\n        if not re.search(r'[HMS]', time_part):\n            raise ValueError(\"T must be followed by at least one of H, M, S\")\n\n    # Check for fractional parts on non-last components\n    # Find all components with their positions\n    components = []\n    for i, (name, group) in enumerate([\n        ('Y', years), ('M', months), ('W', weeks), ('D', days),\n        ('H', hours), ('M', minutes), ('S', seconds)\n    ]):\n        if group is not None:\n            components.append((name, group, i))\n\n    # Check that only the last component has a fractional part\n    for idx, (name, value, _) in enumerate(components):\n        has_fraction = '.' in value or ',' in value\n        if has_fraction and idx != len(components) - 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Fractional part only allowed on last component, found on {name}\")\n\n    # Parse values and convert to seconds\n    total = 0.0\n\n    def parse_num(val_str):\n        # Replace comma with dot for float parsing\n        return float(val_str.replace(',', '.'))\n\n    if years is not None:\n        total += parse_num(years) * 365 * 86400\n    if months is not None:\n        total += parse_num(months) * 30 * 86400\n    if weeks is not None:\n        total += parse_num(weeks) * 7 * 86400\n    if days is not None:\n        total += parse_num(days) * 86400\n    if hours is not None:\n        total += parse_num(hours) * 3600\n    if minutes is not None:\n        total += parse_num(minutes) * 60\n    if seconds is not None:\n        total += parse_num(seconds)\n\n    return total\n```\n\nWait, I need to reconsider the regex approach. The regex allows `PT` with no components after it, which should be invalid. Let me also handle the case where `T` appears but no time components follow. Let me revise with a more careful approach:\n\n```python\nimport re\n\ndef parse_duration(s: str) -> float:\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a string\")\n\n    if len(s) == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Empty string\")\n\n    if s[0] != 'P':\n        raise ValueError(\"Must start with P\")\n\n    # Check for lowercase letters\n    if any(c.islower() for c in s):\n        raise ValueError(\"Lowercase letters not allowed\")\n\n    # Check for whitespace\n    if any(c.isspace() for c in s):\n        raise ValueError(\"Whitespace not allowed\")\n\n    # Check for signs\n    if '+' in s or '-' in s:\n        raise ValueError(\"Signs not allowed\")\n\n    # Parse the structure manually for better c"}
