{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-002", "category": "coding", "title": "Semantic version range check", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 38250, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 2669, "reasoning_tokens": 1847, "input_tokens": 524, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3306, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 19, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 19}, "workflow_id": "0sfj52ca19e8-d029-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db5857-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:06:12-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\n\n\n_VERSION_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.\"\n    r\"(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.\"\n    r\"(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\"\n    r\"(?:-([A-Za-z0-9-]+(?:\\.[A-Za-z0-9-]+)*))?\"\n    r\"(?:\\+([A-Za-z0-9-]+(?:\\.[A-Za-z0-9-]+)*))?\"\n)\n_COMPARATOR_RE = re.compile(r\"(>=|<=|[=<>^~])?(.+)\")\n\n\ndef _precedence_key(core, prerelease=None):\n    # Length/string pairs compare arbitrary-size integers without int().\n    core_key = tuple((len(part), part) for part in core)\n    prerelease_key = []\n\n    if prerelease is not None:\n        for identifier in prerelease.split(\".\"):\n            if identifier.isdigit():\n                number = identifier.lstrip(\"0\") or \"0\"\n                prerelease_key.append((0, len(number), number))\n            else:\n                prerelease_key.append((1, 0, identifier))\n\n    return core_key, prerelease is None, tuple(prerelease_key)\n\n\ndef _parse_version(text: str):\n    match = _VERSION_RE.fullmatch(text)\n    if match is None:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Malformed version: {text!r}\")\n\n    core = match.group(1, 2, 3)\n    return core, _precedence_key(core, match.group(4))\n\n\ndef _increment_decimal(number: str) -> str:\n    digits = list(number)\n    for index in range(len(digits) - 1, -1, -1):\n        if digits[index] != \"9\":\n            digits[index] = chr(ord(digits[index]) + 1)\n            return \"\".join(digits)\n        digits[index] = \"0\"\n    return \"1\" + \"\".join(digits)\n\n\ndef satisfies(version: str, range_expr: str) -> bool:\n    _, candidate = _parse_version(version)\n    range_matches = False\n\n    for comparator_set in range_expr.split(\"||\"):\n        comparators = comparator_set.split()\n        if not comparators:\n            raise ValueError(\"Range contains an empty comparator set\")\n\n        set_matches = True\n\n        for comparator in comparators:\n            if comparator == \"*\":\n                continue\n\n            match = _COMPARATOR_RE.fullmatch(comparator)\n            if match is None:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Malformed comparator: {comparator!r}\")\n\n            operator = match.group(1) or \"=\"\n            core, target = _parse_version(match.group(2))\n\n            if operator in (\"^\", \"~\"):\n                major, minor, patch = core\n\n                if operator == \"~\":\n                    upper_core = (major, _increment_decimal(minor), \"0\")\n                elif major != \"0\":\n                    upper_core = (_increment_decimal(major), \"0\", \"0\")\n                elif minor != \"0\":\n                    upper_core = (\"0\", _increment_decimal(minor), \"0\")\n                else:\n                    upper_core = (\"0\", \"0\", _increment_decimal(patch))\n\n                upper = _precedence_key(upper_core)\n                matches = target <= candidate < upper\n            elif operator == \"=\":\n                matches = candidate == target\n            elif operator == \">\":\n                matches = candidate > target\n            elif operator == \">=\":\n                matches = candidate >= target\n            elif operator == \"<\":\n                matches = candidate < target\n            else:  # <=\n                matches = candidate <= target\n\n            set_matches = set_matches and matches\n\n        # Do not return early: every comparator must be validated.\n        range_matches = range_matches or set_matches\n\n    return range_matches\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-004", "category": "coding", "title": "Next run time for a cron expression", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 76467, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 4613, "reasoning_tokens": 3585, "input_tokens": 377, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 4234, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj52058991-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db5859-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:06:49-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom bisect import bisect_right\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\n\ndef next_run(expr: str, after: str) -> str:\n    if not isinstance(expr, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"expr must be a string\")\n\n    fields = expr.split()\n    if len(fields) != 5:\n        raise ValueError(\"Cron expression must contain exactly five fields\")\n\n    item_pattern = re.compile(\n        r\"(\\*|[0-9]+(?:-[0-9]+)?)(?:/([0-9]+))?\"\n    )\n\n    def capped_uint(text: str, cap: int) -> int:\n        # Avoid integer-conversion limits for arbitrarily long digit strings.\n        text = text.lstrip(\"0\") or \"0\"\n        bound = str(cap)\n        if (len(text), text) > (len(bound), bound):\n            return cap + 1\n        return int(text)\n\n    def parse_field(field: str, lower: int, upper: int) -> set[int]:\n        values: set[int] = set()\n\n        for item in field.split(\",\"):\n            match = item_pattern.fullmatch(item)\n            if match is None:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid cron item: {item!r}\")\n\n            base, step_text = match.groups()\n\n            if base == \"*\":\n                first, last = lower, upper\n            elif \"-\" in base:\n                left, right = base.split(\"-\")\n                first = capped_uint(left, upper)\n                last = capped_uint(right, upper)\n            else:\n                if step_text is not None:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Steps require '*' or a range\")\n                first = last = capped_uint(base, upper)\n\n            if not lower <= first <= last <= upper:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid cron range: {base!r}\")\n\n            # Steps larger than the field's width select only the first value.\n            step = (\n                1\n                if step_text is None\n                else capped_uint(step_text, upper - lower + 1)\n            )\n            if step == 0:\n                raise ValueError(\"Cron steps must be positive\")\n\n            values.update(range(first, last + 1, step))\n\n        return values\n\n    bounds = ((0, 59), (0, 23), (1, 31), (1, 12), (0, 6))\n    minutes, hours, month_days, months, week_days = [\n        parse_field(field, lower, upper)\n        for field, (lower, upper) in zip(fields, bounds)\n    ]\n\n    if not isinstance(after, str) or re.fullmatch(\n        r\"[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2} [0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}\", after\n    ) is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"after must have format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM\")\n\n    start = datetime.fromisoformat(after)\n\n    # Use five calendar years, clamping February 29 to February 28.\n    if start.year + 5 > 9999:\n        deadline = datetime.max\n    else:\n        try:\n            deadline = start.replace(year=start.year + 5)\n        except ValueError:\n            deadline = start.replace(year=start.year + 5, day=28)\n\n    dom_unrestricted = fields[2] == \"*\"\n    dow_unrestricted = fields[4] == \"*\"\n    times = sorted(hour * 60 + minute for hour in hours for minute in minutes)\n\n    start_day = start.date()\n    last_day = deadline.date()\n    start_minute = start.hour * 60 + start.minute\n    day = start_day\n\n    while day <= last_day:\n        if day.month in months:\n            cron_weekday = (day.weekday() + 1) % 7\n\n            if dom_unrestricted:\n                day_matches = cron_weekday in week_days\n            elif dow_unrestricted:\n                day_matches = day.day in month_days\n            else:\n                day_matches = (\n                    day.day in month_days or cron_weekday in week_days\n                )\n\n            if day_matches:\n                index = (\n                    bisect_right(times, start_minute)\n                    if day == start_day\n                    else 0\n                )\n                if index < len(times):\n                    hour, minute = divmod(times[index], 60)\n                    candidate = datetime(\n                        day.year, day.month, day.day, hour, minute\n                    )\n                    if candidate <= deadline:\n                        retur"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-019", "category": "reasoning", "title": "ABC strings with no repeats, each letter twice", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 133200, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 21396, "reasoning_tokens": 21101, "input_tokens": 58, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 978, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 64017, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "294", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "294"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj52946f4a-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db0a34-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:07:46-0500", "answer": "Total strings with no adjacent equal letters:\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 2^7 = 384\n\\]\n\nCount strings that fail the condition, i.e. some letter appears at most once.\n\nFix letter A:\n- If A appears 0 times, only B and C are used, so the string must alternate: \\(2\\) ways.\n- If A appears exactly once, choose its position: \\(8\\) ways. The remaining positions split into left/right blocks of B/C. A block of length \\(L\\) has \\(1\\) filling if \\(L=0\\), and \\(2\\) fillings if \\(L>0\\).\n  - A at an end: \\(2\\) ways for the other block.\n  - A in one of the 6 interior positions: \\(2 \\cdot 2 = 4\\) ways.\n  So exactly once: \\(2\\cdot 2 + 6\\cdot 4 = 28\\) ways.\n\nThus for a fixed letter, bad strings: \\(2 + 28 = 30\\).\n\nNo two letters can both appear at most once, because then the third would appear at least 6 times, impossible in a length-8 string with no adjacent equal letters (max 4 occurrences of any letter).\n\nSo total bad strings:\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 30 = 90\n\\]\n\nValid strings:\n\\[\n384 - 90 = 294\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 294"}
