{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-018", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Two pipes, a drain and a 3/4 tank", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3505, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 225, "reasoning_tokens": 45, "input_tokens": 107, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 465, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "540", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "540"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj525445e6-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db0a32-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:10:41-0500", "answer": "With A and B running together, the filling rate is\n\\[\n\\frac16+\\frac19=\\frac5{18}\n\\]\ntank per hour. After 2 hours, the tank is \\(2\\cdot\\frac5{18}=\\frac59\\) full.\n\nWith A off and B and C open, the net filling rate is\n\\[\n\\frac19-\\frac1{12}=\\frac1{36}\n\\]\ntank per hour.\n\nThe remaining amount needed to reach \\(\\frac34\\) is\n\\[\n\\frac34-\\frac59=\\frac7{36},\n\\]\nwhich takes \\(\\frac7{36}\\div\\frac1{36}=7\\) hours.\n\nTotal time: \\(2+7=9\\) hours, or \\(540\\) minutes.\n\nANSWER: 540"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-020", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Smallest number above 10,000 from remainders", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4610, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 916, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 73, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1929, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "10223", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "10223"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj52dbecb1-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db3146-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:10:43-0500", "answer": "I need to find the smallest integer n > 10,000 satisfying:\n- n \u2261 3 (mod 7)\n- n \u2261 4 (mod 11)\n- n \u2261 5 (mod 13)\n- n \u2261 2 (mod 3)\n\nI'll use the Chinese Remainder Theorem. First, let me check that the moduli are coprime: 7, 11, 13, 3 are all prime, so they're pairwise coprime.\n\nLet me solve step by step. I'll combine congruences two at a time.\n\n**Step 1: Combine n \u2261 3 (mod 7) and n \u2261 4 (mod 11)**\n\nFrom n \u2261 3 (mod 7): n = 7k + 3 for some integer k.\n\nSubstituting into n \u2261 4 (mod 11):\n7k + 3 \u2261 4 (mod 11)\n7k \u2261 1 (mod 11)\n\nI need the inverse of 7 mod 11. Since 7 \u00d7 8 = 56 = 55 + 1 \u2261 1 (mod 11), the inverse is 8.\n\nSo k \u2261 8 (mod 11), meaning k = 11m + 8.\n\nThus n = 7(11m + 8) + 3 = 77m + 56 + 3 = 77m + 59.\n\nSo n \u2261 59 (mod 77).\n\n**Step 2: Combine n \u2261 59 (mod 77) and n \u2261 5 (mod 13)**\n\nn = 77m + 59. Need 77m + 59 \u2261 5 (mod 13).\n\nFirst reduce: 77 = 5\u00d713 + 12, so 77 \u2261 12 \u2261 -1 (mod 13).\nAnd 59 = 4\u00d713 + 7, so 59 \u2261 7 (mod 13).\n\nSo: -m + 7 \u2261 5 (mod 13)\n-m \u2261 -2 (mod 13)\nm \u2261 2 (mod 13)\n\nSo m = 13p + 2.\n\nThus n = 77(13p + 2) + 59 = 1001p + 154 + 59 = 1001p + 213.\n\nSo n \u2261 213 (mod 1001).\n\n**Step 3: Combine n \u2261 213 (mod 1001) and n \u2261 2 (mod 3)**\n\nn = 1001p + 213. Need 1001p + 213 \u2261 2 (mod 3).\n\n1001 = 333\u00d73 + 2, so 1001 \u2261 2 (mod 3).\n213 = 71\u00d73, so 213 \u2261 0 (mod 3).\n\nSo: 2p + 0 \u2261 2 (mod 3)\n2p \u2261 2 (mod 3)\np \u2261 1 (mod 3)\n\nSo p = 3q + 1.\n\nThus n = 1001(3q + 1) + 213 = 3003q + 1001 + 213 = 3003q + 1214.\n\nSo n \u2261 1214 (mod 3003).\n\n**Step 4: Find smallest n > 10,000**\n\nWe need 3003q + 1214 > 10000.\n\nFor q = 0: n = 1214 (too small)\nFor q = 1: n = 3003 + 1214 = 4217 (too small)\nFor q = 2: n = 6006 + 1214 = 7220 (too small)\nFor q = 3: n = 9009 + 1214 = 10223 (this is > 10000) \u2713\n\nLet me verify n = 10223:\n- 10223 \u00f7 7 = 1460 remainder 3 \u2713 (7 \u00d7 1460 = 10220)\n- 10223 \u00f7 11 = 929 remainder 4 \u2713 (11 \u00d7 929 = 10219)\n- 10223 \u00f7 13 = 786 remainder 5 \u2713 (13 \u00d7 786 = 10218)\n- 10223 \u00f7 3 = 3407 remainder 2 \u2713 (3 \u00d7 3407 = 10221)\n\nAll checks pass!\n\nANSWER: 10223"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-020", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Smallest number above 10,000 from remainders", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6271, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 410, "reasoning_tokens": 142, "input_tokens": 74, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 563, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "10223", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "10223"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj52dc13c2-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db3146-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:10:45-0500", "answer": "From \\(n\\equiv3\\pmod7\\), write \\(n=7a+3\\). Then\n\\[\n7a+3\\equiv4\\pmod{11}\n\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad a\\equiv8\\pmod{11},\n\\]\nso \\(n=59+77b\\).\n\nApplying the condition modulo \\(13\\),\n\\[\n59+77b\\equiv5\\pmod{13}\n\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad 7-b\\equiv5\\pmod{13},\n\\]\nso \\(b=2+13c\\) and \\(n=213+1001c\\).\n\nFinally, modulo \\(3\\),\n\\[\n213+1001c\\equiv2c\\equiv2\\pmod3,\n\\]\ngiving \\(c=1+3t\\). Thus all solutions are\n\\[\nn=1214+3003t,\\qquad t\\in\\mathbb Z.\n\\]\n\nFor \\(t=2\\), \\(n=7220\\); for \\(t=3\\), \\(n=10223\\). Therefore the smallest solution greater than \\(10{,}000\\) is \\(10223\\).\n\nANSWER: 10223"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-020", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Smallest number above 10,000 from remainders", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6981, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 498, "reasoning_tokens": 232, "input_tokens": 74, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 560, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "10223", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "10223"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj52dc13c3-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db3146-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:10:45-0500", "answer": "Write \\(n=7a+3\\). The condition modulo \\(11\\) gives\n\\[\n7a+3\\equiv4\\pmod{11}\\implies a\\equiv8\\pmod{11},\n\\]\nso \\(n=77b+59\\).\n\nNext, modulo \\(13\\),\n\\[\n77b+59\\equiv5\\pmod{13}\n\\implies -b+7\\equiv5\\pmod{13}\n\\implies b\\equiv2\\pmod{13}.\n\\]\nThus \\(n=1001c+213\\).\n\nFinally, modulo \\(3\\),\n\\[\n1001c+213\\equiv2\\pmod3\n\\implies2c\\equiv2\\pmod3\n\\implies c\\equiv1\\pmod3.\n\\]\nTherefore all solutions are\n\\[\nn=3003k+1214,\\qquad k\\in\\mathbb Z.\n\\]\n\nFor \\(k=2\\), \\(n=7220\\); for \\(k=3\\), \\(n=10223\\). Hence the latter is the smallest solution greater than \\(10{,}000\\).\n\nANSWER: 10223"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-020", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Smallest number above 10,000 from remainders", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 8642, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1526, "reasoning_tokens": 1018, "input_tokens": 73, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1021, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2411, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "10223", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "10223"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj52dbc59f-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db3146-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:10:47-0500", "answer": "Let the congruences be:\n\n\\[\nn \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7}\n\\]\n\\[\nn \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\\[\nn \\equiv 5 \\pmod{13}\n\\]\n\\[\nn \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}\n\\]\n\nStart with \\(n = 3 + 7a\\).  \nFrom \\(n \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11}\\):\n\n\\[\n3 + 7a \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\\[\n7a \\equiv 1 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\nSince \\(7^{-1} \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}\\),\n\n\\[\na \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\nSo \\(a = 8 + 11b\\), giving:\n\n\\[\nn = 3 + 7(8 + 11b) = 59 + 77b\n\\]\n\nNow use \\(n \\equiv 5 \\pmod{13}\\):\n\n\\[\n59 + 77b \\equiv 5 \\pmod{13}\n\\]\n\\[\n7 - b \\equiv 5 \\pmod{13}\n\\]\n\\[\nb \\equiv 2 \\pmod{13}\n\\]\n\nSo \\(b = 2 + 13c\\), giving:\n\n\\[\nn = 59 + 77(2 + 13c) = 213 + 1001c\n\\]\n\nFinally use \\(n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}\\):\n\n\\[\n213 + 1001c \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}\n\\]\n\\[\n0 + 2c \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}\n\\]\n\\[\nc \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}\n\\]\n\nSo \\(c = 1 + 3d\\), giving:\n\n\\[\nn = 213 + 1001(1 + 3d) = 1214 + 3003d\n\\]\n\nThus all solutions are:\n\n\\[\nn = 1214 + 3003d\n\\]\n\nWe need the smallest \\(n > 10000\\):\n\n\\[\n1214 + 3003d > 10000\n\\]\n\\[\n3003d > 8786\n\\]\n\nThe smallest integer \\(d\\) is \\(3\\):\n\n\\[\nn = 1214 + 3003(3) = 1214 + 9009 = 10223\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 10223"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "reasoning-020", "category": "reasoning", "title": "Smallest number above 10,000 from remainders", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 16370, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 2014, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 79, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 4252, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "expected": "10223", "answer_line_found": true, "extracted": "10223"}, "workflow_id": "0sfj52dbc5a0-d029-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj51db3146-d029-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:10:55-0500", "answer": "Alright, I have this problem:\n\n**Find the smallest integer n greater than 10,000 such that:**\n1. n leaves remainder 3 when divided by 7 (n \u2261 3 mod 7)\n2. n leaves remainder 4 when divided by 11 (n \u2261 4 mod 11)\n3. n leaves remainder 5 when divided by 13 (n \u2261 5 mod 13)\n4. n leaves remainder 2 when divided by 3 (n \u2261 2 mod 3)\n\n### Understanding the Problem\nFirst, I need to find the smallest integer n > 10,000 that satisfies all four congruence conditions. This is a system of congruences, and I think the Chinese Remainder Theorem (CRT) might be applicable here.\n\n### Step 1: Solve the First Three Congruences\nThe first three congruences are:\n1. n \u2261 3 mod 7\n2. n \u2261 4 mod 11\n3. n \u2261 5 mod 13\n\nI recall that CRT can be used to find a common solution to multiple congruences with pairwise coprime moduli. Since 7, 11, and 13 are all primes, they are pairwise coprime.\n\n#### Step 1.1: Solve n \u2261 3 mod 7 and n \u2261 4 mod 11\nFirst, I need to find a number n that satisfies both n \u2261 3 mod 7 and n \u2261 4 mod 11.\n\nLet's express n as:\nn = 7k + 3, for some integer k.\n\nNow, substitute this into the second congruence:\n7k + 3 \u2261 4 mod 11\n=> 7k \u2261 1 mod 11\n\nNow, I need to find the multiplicative inverse of 7 modulo 11, i.e., a number x such that 7x \u2261 1 mod 11.\n\nLet's test:\n7 * 8 = 56 \u2261 1 mod 11 (since 55 is divisible by 11, 56 mod 11 is 1).\n\nThus, the inverse of 7 mod 11 is 8.\n\nNow, multiply both sides of 7k \u2261 1 mod 11 by 8:\nk \u2261 8 mod 11\n\nSo, k can be written as:\nk = 11m + 8, for some integer m.\n\nNow, substitute back into n:\nn = 7k + 3 = 7(11m + 8) + 3 = 77m + 56 + 3 = 77m + 59.\n\nThus, n \u2261 59 mod 77.\n\n#### Step 1.2: Incorporate the Third Congruence n \u2261 5 mod 13\nNow, I have n \u2261 59 mod 77. I need to find n such that n \u2261 5 mod 13.\n\nAgain, express n as:\nn = 77m + 59.\n\nSubstitute into the third congruence:\n77m + 59 \u2261 5 mod 13.\n\nFirst, simplify 77 mod 13 and 59 mod 13:\n- 77 \u00f7 13 = 5 * 13 = 65, remainder 12. So, 77 \u2261 12 mod 13.\n- 59 \u00f7 13 = 4 * 13 = 52, remainder 7. So, 59 \u2261 7 mod 13.\n\nThus:\n12m + 7 \u2261 5 mod 13\n=> 12m \u2261 -2 mod 13\nBut -2 mod 13 is 11, so:\n12m \u2261 11 mod 13.\n\nNow, find the inverse of 12 mod 13. Since 12 * 12 = 144 \u2261 1 mod 13 (because 143 is divisible by 13), the inverse of 12 mod 13 is 12.\n\nMultiply both sides by 12:\nm \u2261 11 * 12 mod 13\n=> m \u2261 132 mod 13.\n\nNow, simplify 132 mod 13:\n132 \u00f7 13 = 10 * 13 = 130, remainder 2. So, 132 \u2261 2 mod 13.\n\nThus, m \u2261 2 mod 13.\n\nSo, m can be written as:\nm = 13p + 2, for some integer p.\n\nNow, substitute back into n:\nn = 77m + 59 = 77(13p + 2) + 59 = 1001p + 154 + 59 = 1001p + 213.\n\nThus, n \u2261 213 mod 1001.\n\n### Step 2: Incorporate the Fourth Congruence n \u2261 2 mod 3\nNow, I have n \u2261 213 mod 1001. I need to find n such that n \u2261 2 mod 3.\n\nAgain, express n as:\nn = 1001p + 213.\n\nSubstitute into the fourth congruence:\n1001p + 213 \u2261 2 mod 3.\n\nFirst, simplify 1001 mod 3 and 213 mod 3:\n- Sum of digits of 1001: 1 + 0 + 0 + 1 = 2 \u2261 2 mod 3.\n- Sum of digits of 213: 2 + 1 + 3 = 6 \u2261 0 mod 3.\n\nThus:\n2p + 0 \u2261 2 mod 3\n=> 2p \u2261 2 mod 3.\n\nNow, find the inverse of 2 mod 3. Since 2 * 2 = 4 \u2261 1 mod 3, the inverse of 2 mod 3 is 2.\n\nMultiply both sides by 2:\np \u2261 4 mod 3\n=> p \u2261 1 mod 3.\n\nThus, p can be written as:\np = 3q + 1, for some integer q.\n\nNow, substitute back into n:\nn = 1001p + 213 = 1001(3q + 1) + 213 = 3003q + 1001 + 213 = 3003q + 1214.\n\n### Step 3: Find the Smallest n > 10,000\nThe general solution is n = 3003q + 1214.\n\nI need the smallest n > 10,000.\n\nLet's find q such that:\n3003q + 1214 > 10,000\n=> 3003q > 10,000 - 1214\n=> 3003q > 8786\n=> q > 8786 / 3003 \u2248 2.9257.\n\nSince q must be an integer, the smallest integer q satisfying this is q = 3.\n\nNow, plug q = 3 into n:\nn = 3003 * 3 + 1214 = 9009 + 1214 = 10223.\n\nBut I need to check if q = 2 gives a value less than 10,000:\nn = 3003 * 2 + 1214 = 6006 + 1214 = 7220 < 10,000.\n\nThus, q = 3 is indeed the smallest integer that gives n > 10,000.\n\n### Verification\nLet's verify n = 10223 against all the original conditions:\n1. 10223 \u00f7 7 = 1460 * 7 = 10220, remainder 3. \u2714\ufe0f\n2. 10223 \u00f7 11 = 929 * 11 = 10219, remain"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-006", "category": "coding", "title": "RFC 6901 JSON Pointer lookup", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2514, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 393, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 322, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1810, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 18, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 18}, "workflow_id": "0sfj13bca393-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138daf49-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:00-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef resolve_pointer(doc, pointer: str):\n    if pointer == \"\":\n        return doc\n\n    if not pointer.startswith(\"/\"):\n        raise ValueError(\"pointer must start with '/'\")\n\n    current = doc\n\n    # Split on '/', dropping the empty piece before the leading '/'\n    tokens = pointer.split(\"/\")[1:]\n\n    for token in tokens:\n        # Decode ~1 before ~0\n        decoded = []\n        i = 0\n        while i < len(token):\n            ch = token[i]\n            if ch == \"~\":\n                if i + 1 >= len(token):\n                    raise ValueError(\"invalid escape: '~' at end of token\")\n                nxt = token[i + 1]\n                if nxt == \"1\":\n                    decoded.append(\"/\")\n                    i += 2\n                elif nxt == \"0\":\n                    decoded.append(\"~\")\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    raise ValueError(\"invalid escape: '~' followed by %r\" % nxt)\n            else:\n                decoded.append(ch)\n                i += 1\n        key = \"\".join(decoded)\n\n        if isinstance(current, dict):\n            if key not in current:\n                raise KeyError(key)\n            current = current[key]\n        elif isinstance(current, list):\n            if key == \"-\":\n                raise KeyError(key)\n            # Must be ASCII digits, no leading zeros unless the token is exactly \"0\"\n            if not key.isascii() or not key.isdigit():\n                raise ValueError(\"invalid array index: %r\" % key)\n            if len(key) > 1 and key[0] == \"0\":\n                raise ValueError(\"invalid array index: %r\" % key)\n            idx = int(key)\n            if idx >= len(current):\n                raise KeyError(key)\n            current = current[idx]\n        else:\n            raise KeyError(key)\n\n    return current\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-005", "category": "coding", "title": "Strict CSV line parser", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2416, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 403, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 244, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1863, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj144b8629-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138daf48-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:00-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef parse_csv_line(line: str, delimiter: str = \",\") -> list[str]:\n    if len(delimiter) != 1 or delimiter == '\"':\n        raise ValueError(\"delimiter must be a single character other than '\\\"'\")\n\n    fields: list[str] = []\n    i = 0\n    n = len(line)\n\n    while True:\n        # Start of a field\n        if i < n and line[i] == '\"':\n            # Quoted field\n            i += 1\n            buf: list[str] = []\n            closed = False\n            while i < n:\n                c = line[i]\n                if c == '\"':\n                    if i + 1 < n and line[i + 1] == '\"':\n                        buf.append('\"')\n                        i += 2\n                    else:\n                        # Closing quote\n                        i += 1\n                        closed = True\n                        break\n                else:\n                    buf.append(c)\n                    i += 1\n            if not closed:\n                raise ValueError(\"unterminated quoted field\")\n            # After closing quote must be delimiter or end of line\n            if i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                raise ValueError(\"characters after closing quote\")\n            fields.append(''.join(buf))\n        else:\n            # Unquoted field\n            start = i\n            while i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                if line[i] == '\"':\n                    raise ValueError(\"quote in unquoted field\")\n                i += 1\n            fields.append(line[start:i])\n\n        # After field: either delimiter or end of line\n        if i < n and line[i] == delimiter:\n            i += 1\n            # If delimiter is last char, we need a trailing empty field\n            if i == n:\n                fields.append(\"\")\n                break\n            continue\n        else:\n            # End of line\n            break\n\n    return fields\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-012", "category": "coding", "title": "Token bucket rate limiter", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1498, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 240, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 249, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1006, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj151bc97e-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138e247f-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:01-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef token_bucket(capacity: int, refill_per_sec: float, requests: list[tuple[float, int]]) -> list[bool]:\n    if capacity < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"capacity must be >= 1\")\n    if refill_per_sec < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"refill_per_sec must be >= 0\")\n\n    tokens = float(capacity)\n    last_time: float | None = None\n    result: list[bool] = []\n\n    for timestamp, cost in requests:\n        if not isinstance(cost, int) or isinstance(cost, bool) or cost < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"cost must be an integer >= 1\")\n        if last_time is not None and timestamp < last_time:\n            raise ValueError(\"timestamps must be non-decreasing\")\n\n        if last_time is not None:\n            elapsed = timestamp - last_time\n            tokens = min(float(capacity), tokens + elapsed * refill_per_sec)\n\n        last_time = timestamp\n\n        if tokens >= cost:\n            tokens -= cost\n            result.append(True)\n        else:\n            result.append(False)\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-005", "category": "coding", "title": "Strict CSV line parser", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3086, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 295, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 245, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1304, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj144bad3b-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138daf48-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:01-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef parse_csv_line(line: str, delimiter: str = \",\") -> list[str]:\n    if not isinstance(delimiter, str) or len(delimiter) != 1 or delimiter == '\"':\n        raise ValueError('delimiter must be a single character other than \\'\"\\'')\n    \n    fields: list[str] = []\n    i = 0\n    n = len(line)\n\n    while True:\n        if i < n and line[i] == '\"':\n            i += 1\n            chars: list[str] = []\n\n            while True:\n                if i == n:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Unterminated quoted field\")\n                if line[i] != '\"':\n                    chars.append(line[i])\n                    i += 1\n                elif i + 1 < n and line[i + 1] == '\"':\n                    chars.append('\"')\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    i += 1\n                    break\n\n            if i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                raise ValueError(\"Unexpected character after closing quote\")\n            fields.append(\"\".join(chars))\n        else:\n            start = i\n            while i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                if line[i] == '\"':\n                    raise ValueError(\"Quote in unquoted field\")\n                i += 1\n            fields.append(line[start:i])\n\n        if i == n:\n            return fields\n        i += 1\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-011", "category": "coding", "title": "Add business days with holidays", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1810, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 309, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 228, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1130, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 15, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 15}, "workflow_id": "0sfj1559e918-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138e247e-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:01-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom datetime import date, timedelta\n\ndef _parse_date(s: str) -> date:\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid date: {s!r}\")\n    if not re.fullmatch(r\"\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\", s):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid date format: {s!r}\")\n    try:\n        return date.fromisoformat(s)\n    except ValueError:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid date: {s!r}\")\n\ndef add_business_days(start: str, days: int, holidays: list[str]) -> str:\n    start_date = _parse_date(start)\n    holiday_set = {_parse_date(h) for h in holidays}\n\n    def is_business_day(d: date) -> bool:\n        return d.weekday() < 5 and d not in holiday_set\n\n    if days == 0:\n        if is_business_day(start_date):\n            return start_date.isoformat()\n        d = start_date + timedelta(days=1)\n        while not is_business_day(d):\n            d += timedelta(days=1)\n        return d.isoformat()\n\n    step = 1 if days > 0 else -1\n    remaining = abs(days)\n    d = start_date\n\n    while remaining > 0:\n        d += timedelta(days=step)\n        if is_business_day(d):\n            remaining -= 1\n\n    return d.isoformat()\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-006", "category": "coding", "title": "RFC 6901 JSON Pointer lookup", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4382, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 396, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 324, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1845, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 18, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 18}, "workflow_id": "0sfj13bca396-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138daf49-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:01-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef resolve_pointer(doc, pointer: str):\n    if not pointer:\n        return doc\n\n    if not pointer.startswith('/'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Pointer must start with '/'\")\n\n    tokens = pointer.split('/')[1:]  # Skip the initial empty string from leading '/'\n\n    current = doc\n    for token in tokens:\n        # Decode ~0 and ~1\n        decoded_token = []\n        i = 0\n        n = len(token)\n        while i < n:\n            if token[i] == '~':\n                if i + 1 >= n:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Invalid escape sequence in pointer\")\n                if token[i+1] == '0':\n                    decoded_token.append('~')\n                    i += 2\n                elif token[i+1] == '1':\n                    decoded_token.append('/')\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Invalid escape sequence in pointer\")\n            else:\n                decoded_token.append(token[i])\n                i += 1\n        decoded_token = ''.join(decoded_token)\n\n        # Handle dict or list\n        if isinstance(current, dict):\n            if decoded_token not in current:\n                raise KeyError(f\"Key not found: {decoded_token}\")\n            current = current[decoded_token]\n        elif isinstance(current, list):\n            if decoded_token == '-':\n                raise KeyError(\"Index '-' refers to non-existent element after last\")\n            if not re.fullmatch(r'0|[1-9][0-9]*', decoded_token):\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid list index: {decoded_token}\")\n            index = int(decoded_token)\n            if index >= len(current):\n                raise KeyError(f\"Index out of range: {index}\")\n            current = current[index]\n        else:\n            raise KeyError(\"Cannot apply token to non-dict and non-list\")\n\n    return current\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-008", "category": "coding", "title": "Subtract IPv4 CIDR blocks", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.3529, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3520, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 289, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 227, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1251, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.3529, "total": 17, "failures": [{"test": "assert cidr_subtract(\"10.0.0.0/24\", [\"10.0.0.0/25\"]) == [\"10.0.0.128/25\"]", "line": 11, "error": "AttributeError: 'IPv4Network' object has no attribute 'is_disjoint'"}, {"test": "assert cidr_subtract(\"10.0.0.0/24\", [\"10.0.0.0/24\"]) == []", "line": 12, "error": "AttributeError: 'IPv4Network' object has no attribute 'is_disjoint'"}, {"test": "assert cidr_subtract(\"10.0.0.0/24\", [\"10.0.0.0/16\"]) == []", "line": 13, "error": "AttributeError: 'IPv4Network' object has no attribute 'is_disjoint'"}, {"test": "assert cidr_subtract(\"10.0.0.0/24\", [\"10.0.0.64/26\"]) == [\"10.0.0.0/26\", \"10.0.0.128/25\"]", "line": 14, "error": "AttributeError: 'IPv4Network' object has no attribute 'is_disjoint'"}, {"test": "assert cidr_subtract(\"10.0.0.0/30\", [\"10.0.0.1/32\"]) == [\"10.0.0.0/32\", \"10.0.0.2/31\"]", "line": 15, "error": "AttributeError: 'IPv4Network' object has no attribute 'is_disjoint'"}], "pass": false, "load_error": null, "passed": 6}, "workflow_id": "0sfj146fb00e-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dd65b-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:02-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport ipaddress\n\ndef cidr_subtract(base: str, remove: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    try:\n        base_net = ipaddress.IPv4Network(base, strict=True)\n    except ValueError as e:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid base CIDR block: {e}\")\n\n    remove_nets = []\n    for cidr in remove:\n        try:\n            net = ipaddress.IPv4Network(cidr, strict=True)\n        except ValueError as e:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid remove CIDR block '{cidr}': {e}\")\n        remove_nets.append(net)\n\n    # Start with the base network\n    remaining = [base_net]\n\n    for net in remove_nets:\n        new_remaining = []\n        for current in remaining:\n            # If the current network is completely outside the remove network, keep it\n            if current.is_disjoint(net):\n                new_remaining.append(current)\n            else:\n                # Otherwise, subtract the remove network from the current network\n                new_remaining.extend(current.address_exclude(net))\n        remaining = new_remaining\n        if not remaining:\n            return []\n\n    # Convert to strings and sort by network address\n    result = [str(net) for net in sorted(remaining, key=lambda n: (n.network_address, n.prefixlen))]\n    return result\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-011", "category": "coding", "title": "Add business days with holidays", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2308, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 264, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 230, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1074, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 15, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 15}, "workflow_id": "0sfj1559c205-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138e247e-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:02-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom datetime import date, timedelta\n\n\ndef add_business_days(start: str, days: int, holidays: list[str]) -> str:\n    def parse_date(value: str) -> date:\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or re.fullmatch(\n            r\"[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}\", value\n        ) is None:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid date: {value!r}\")\n        try:\n            return date.fromisoformat(value)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid date: {value!r}\") from None\n\n    current = parse_date(start)\n    holiday_dates = {parse_date(holiday) for holiday in holidays}\n\n    def is_business_day(value: date) -> bool:\n        return value.weekday() < 5 and value not in holiday_dates\n\n    if days == 0:\n        while not is_business_day(current):\n            current += timedelta(days=1)\n    else:\n        step = timedelta(days=1 if days > 0 else -1)\n        remaining = abs(days)\n        while remaining:\n            current += step\n            if is_business_day(current):\n                remaining -= 1\n\n    return current.isoformat()\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-011", "category": "coding", "title": "Add business days with holidays", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2695, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 253, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 231, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1004, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 15, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 15}, "workflow_id": "0sfj1559e919-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138e247e-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:02-0500", "answer": "```python\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\ndef add_business_days(start: str, days: int, holidays: list[str]) -> str:\n    # Validate input dates\n    try:\n        current = datetime.strptime(start, \"%Y-%m-%d\").date()\n    except ValueError:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid start date format\")\n\n    holiday_dates = set()\n    for h in holidays:\n        try:\n            holiday_dates.add(datetime.strptime(h, \"%Y-%m-%d\").date())\n        except ValueError:\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid holiday date format\")\n\n    if days == 0:\n        # Check if start is a business day\n        if current.weekday() < 5 and current not in holiday_dates:\n            return start\n        # Otherwise find the next business day\n        days = 1\n\n    step = 1 if days > 0 else -1\n    remaining = abs(days)\n\n    while remaining > 0:\n        current += timedelta(days=step)\n        if current.weekday() < 5 and current not in holiday_dates:\n            remaining -= 1\n\n    return current.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-012", "category": "coding", "title": "Token bucket rate limiter", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3524, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 293, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 257, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1240, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj151bf092-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138e247f-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:03-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef token_bucket(capacity: int, refill_per_sec: float, requests: list[tuple[float, int]]) -> list[bool]:\n    if capacity < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Capacity must be at least 1\")\n    if refill_per_sec < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Refill rate must be non-negative\")\n\n    if not requests:\n        return []\n\n    # Validate requests\n    prev_timestamp = requests[0][0]\n    for timestamp, cost in requests:\n        if timestamp < prev_timestamp:\n            raise ValueError(\"Timestamps must be non-decreasing\")\n        if not isinstance(cost, int) or cost < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"Cost must be an integer >= 1\")\n        prev_timestamp = timestamp\n\n    tokens = float(capacity)\n    last_refill_time = requests[0][0]\n    results = []\n\n    for timestamp, cost in requests:\n        # Calculate tokens added since last refill\n        time_elapsed = timestamp - last_refill_time\n        tokens_added = time_elapsed * refill_per_sec\n        tokens = min(tokens + tokens_added, capacity)\n        last_refill_time = timestamp\n\n        # Check if request can be allowed\n        if tokens >= cost:\n            tokens -= cost\n            results.append(True)\n        else:\n            results.append(False)\n\n    return results\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-005", "category": "coding", "title": "Strict CSV line parser", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4700, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 484, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 246, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 2202, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj144bad3c-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138daf48-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:03-0500", "answer": "Here's the Python function `parse_csv_line` that adheres to the specified CSV parsing rules:\n\n```python\ndef parse_csv_line(line: str, delimiter: str = \",\") -> list[str]:\n    if len(delimiter) != 1 or delimiter == '\"':\n        raise ValueError(\"Delimiter must be a single character other than '\\\"'\")\n\n    fields = []\n    current_field = []\n    in_quotes = False\n    i = 0\n    n = len(line)\n\n    while i < n:\n        if not in_quotes:\n            if line[i] == '\"':\n                if current_field:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Unquoted field contains '\\\"'\")\n                in_quotes = True\n                i += 1\n            elif line[i] == delimiter:\n                fields.append(''.join(current_field))\n                current_field = []\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                current_field.append(line[i])\n                i += 1\n        else:\n            if line[i] == '\"':\n                if i + 1 < n and line[i + 1] == '\"':\n                    current_field.append('\"')\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    in_quotes = False\n                    i += 1\n                    # Check what follows the closing quote\n                    if i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                        if line[i] != '\\n' and i != n:  # Not end of line\n                            raise ValueError(\"Closing quote must be followed by delimiter or end of line\")\n            else:\n                current_field.append(line[i])\n                i += 1\n\n    # After loop ends\n    if in_quotes:\n        raise ValueError(\"Unterminated quoted field\")\n\n    fields.append(''.join(current_field))\n\n    # Handle empty line case\n    if not line and not fields:\n        return [\"\"]\n\n    return fields\n```\n\nThis function:\n1. Validates the delimiter is a single character and not a quote\n2. Processes the line character by character, tracking whether we're in a quoted field\n3. Handles escaped quotes (`\"\"`) within quoted fields\n4. Validates proper closing of quoted fields\n5. Handles empty lines and trailing delimiters correctly\n6. Raises ValueError for all invalid cases as specified\n\nThe function follows all the strict rules mentioned in the problem statement."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-010", "category": "coding", "title": "Optimal string alignment distance", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2607, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 449, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 152, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1493, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj15d87ef4-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dfd6d-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:03-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef osa_distance(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the Optimal String Alignment (OSA) distance between two strings.\n\n    OSA distance is the restricted Damerau-Levenshtein distance: the minimum\n    number of insertions, deletions, substitutions, or transpositions of two\n    adjacent characters needed to turn `a` into `b`, with the restriction that\n    no substring is edited more than once (a transposed pair cannot take part\n    in any further edit).\n\n    Comparison is case-sensitive and operates on Python string characters\n    (Unicode code points).\n    \"\"\"\n    m, n = len(a), len(b)\n\n    # dp[i][j] = OSA distance between a[:i] and b[:j]\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(m + 1)]\n\n    # Base cases: transforming empty string to prefix of the other\n    for i in range(m + 1):\n        dp[i][0] = i\n    for j in range(n + 1):\n        dp[0][j] = j\n\n    for i in range(1, m + 1):\n        for j in range(1, n + 1):\n            cost = 0 if a[i - 1] == b[j - 1] else 1\n\n            # Standard Levenshtein operations\n            dp[i][j] = min(\n                dp[i - 1][j] + 1,      # deletion\n                dp[i][j - 1] + 1,      # insertion\n                dp[i - 1][j - 1] + cost  # substitution (or match)\n            )\n\n            # Transposition of two adjacent characters (OSA restriction)\n            if i > 1 and j > 1 and a[i - 1] == b[j - 2] and a[i - 2] == b[j - 1]:\n                dp[i][j] = min(dp[i][j], dp[i - 2][j - 2] + 1)\n\n    return dp[m][n]\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-010", "category": "coding", "title": "Optimal string alignment distance", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2654, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 269, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 155, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 958, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj15d8a608-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dfd6d-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:03-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef osa_distance(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    if a == b:\n        return 0\n\n    # Keep the shorter string in columns to minimize memory usage.\n    if len(a) < len(b):\n        a, b = b, a\n\n    n = len(b)\n    if n == 0:\n        return len(a)\n\n    previous = list(range(n + 1))\n    two_back = None\n\n    for i, char_a in enumerate(a, 1):\n        current = [i] + [0] * n\n        for j, char_b in enumerate(b, 1):\n            current[j] = min(\n                previous[j] + 1,                     # Deletion\n                current[j - 1] + 1,                  # Insertion\n                previous[j - 1] + (char_a != char_b), # Substitution\n            )\n\n            if (\n                i > 1\n                and j > 1\n                and char_a == b[j - 2]\n                and a[i - 2] == char_b\n            ):\n                current[j] = min(current[j], two_back[j - 2] + 1)\n\n        two_back, previous = previous, current\n\n    return previous[n]\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-007", "category": "coding", "title": "Glob matching with character classes", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6482, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1284, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 294, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 5169, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj145a915f-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dd65a-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:05-0500", "answer": "I'll implement this glob matcher using dynamic programming for clean handling of all the pattern features.\n\n```python\ndef glob_match(pattern: str, name: str) -> bool:\n    # Parse pattern into tokens for easier processing\n    # Token types: 'char', 'any' (?), 'star' (*), 'doublestar' (**), 'class' (set)\n    \n    tokens = []\n    i = 0\n    n = len(pattern)\n    \n    while i < n:\n        c = pattern[i]\n        if c == '\\\\':\n            # Escape: next char is literal, or trailing backslash is literal backslash\n            if i + 1 < n:\n                tokens.append(('char', pattern[i + 1]))\n                i += 2\n            else:\n                tokens.append(('char', '\\\\'))\n                i += 1\n        elif c == '?':\n            tokens.append(('any', None))\n            i += 1\n        elif c == '*':\n            if i + 1 < n and pattern[i + 1] == '*':\n                tokens.append(('doublestar', None))\n                i += 2\n            else:\n                tokens.append(('star', None))\n                i += 1\n        elif c == '[':\n            # Try to parse a character class\n            j = i + 1\n            negated = False\n            if j < n and pattern[j] in '!^':\n                negated = True\n                j += 1\n            # Check for literal ] as first char\n            members = []  # list of (start, end) ranges or single chars\n            first = True\n            closed = False\n            while j < n:\n                if pattern[j] == ']' and not first:\n                    closed = True\n                    j += 1\n                    break\n                first = False\n                # Parse one member (could be range)\n                if j + 2 < n and pattern[j + 1] == '-' and pattern[j + 2] != ']':\n                    # Range\n                    start = pattern[j]\n                    end = pattern[j + 2]\n                    members.append((start, end))\n                    j += 3\n                else:\n                    # Single char\n                    members.append((pattern[j], pattern[j]))\n                    j += 1\n            if closed:\n                tokens.append(('class', (negated, members)))\n                i = j\n            else:\n                # No closing ], literal [\n                tokens.append(('char', '['))\n                i += 1\n        else:\n            tokens.append(('char', c))\n            i += 1\n    \n    # DP matching: dp[i][j] = does tokens[i:] match name[j:]?\n    m = len(tokens)\n    k = len(name)\n    \n    # dp[i][j] for i in 0..m, j in 0..k\n    # Use 2D array, fill from bottom-right\n    dp = [[False] * (k + 1) for _ in range(m + 1)]\n    dp[m][k] = True  # empty pattern matches empty name\n    \n    for i in range(m - 1, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(k, -1, -1):\n            tok_type, tok_val = tokens[i]\n            \n            if tok_type == 'char':\n                if j < k and name[j] == tok_val:\n                    dp[i][j] = dp[i + 1][j + 1]\n            elif tok_type == 'any':\n                if j < k and name[j] != '/':\n                    dp[i][j] = dp[i + 1][j + 1]\n            elif tok_type == 'star':\n                # Match zero or more non-/ chars\n                # Option 1: match zero chars\n                if dp[i + 1][j]:\n                    dp[i][j] = True\n                # Option 2: match one more char (if not /)\n                elif j < k and name[j] != '/' and dp[i][j + 1]:\n                    dp[i][j] = True\n            elif tok_type == 'doublestar':\n                # Match zero or more chars (including /)\n                # Option 1: match zero chars\n                if dp[i + 1][j]:\n                    dp[i][j] = True\n                # Option 2: match one more char (any char)\n                elif j < k and dp[i][j + 1]:\n                    dp[i][j] = True\n            elif tok_type == 'class':\n                negated, members = tok_val\n                if j < k and name[j] != '/':\n                    ch = name[j]\n                    matched = False\n                    for star"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-010", "category": "coding", "title": "Optimal string alignment distance", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4265, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 446, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 154, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1478, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj15d8a607-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dfd6d-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:05-0500", "answer": "Here's the Python function `osa_distance` that computes the Optimal String Alignment (OSA) distance between two strings:\n\n```python\ndef osa_distance(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    len_a, len_b = len(a), len(b)\n    # Create a distance matrix with (len_a + 1) rows and (len_b + 1) columns\n    dp = [[0] * (len_b + 1) for _ in range(len_a + 1)]\n\n    # Initialize the first row and column\n    for i in range(len_a + 1):\n        dp[i][0] = i\n    for j in range(len_b + 1):\n        dp[0][j] = j\n\n    for i in range(1, len_a + 1):\n        for j in range(1, len_b + 1):\n            cost = 0 if a[i - 1] == b[j - 1] else 1\n            dp[i][j] = min(\n                dp[i - 1][j] + 1,      # deletion\n                dp[i][j - 1] + 1,      # insertion\n                dp[i - 1][j - 1] + cost  # substitution\n            )\n            # Check for transposition\n            if i > 1 and j > 1 and a[i - 1] == b[j - 2] and a[i - 2] == b[j - 1]:\n                dp[i][j] = min(dp[i][j], dp[i - 2][j - 2] + cost)\n\n    return dp[len_a][len_b]\n```\n\nThis function implements the OSA distance by building a dynamic programming matrix where each cell `dp[i][j]` represents the minimum number of edits required to transform the first `i` characters of string `a` into the first `j` characters of string `b`. The function handles insertions, deletions, substitutions, and transpositions (with the restriction that no substring is edited more than once). The final result is found in `dp[len_a][len_b]`."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-012", "category": "coding", "title": "Token bucket rate limiter", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5984, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 358, "reasoning_tokens": 96, "input_tokens": 252, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1154, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj151bc97f-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138e247f-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:05-0500", "answer": "```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\n\ndef token_bucket(\n    capacity: int,\n    refill_per_sec: float,\n    requests: list[tuple[float, int]],\n) -> list[bool]:\n    if capacity < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"capacity must be at least 1\")\n    if refill_per_sec < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"refill_per_sec must be non-negative\")\n\n    if not requests:\n        return []\n\n    rate = Fraction(refill_per_sec)\n    tokens = Fraction(capacity)\n    previous_time = None\n    results: list[bool] = []\n\n    for timestamp, cost in requests:\n        if not isinstance(cost, int) or cost < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"cost must be an integer >= 1\")\n\n        current_time = Fraction(timestamp)\n        if previous_time is not None:\n            if current_time < previous_time:\n                raise ValueError(\"timestamps must be non-decreasing\")\n            tokens = min(\n                Fraction(capacity),\n                tokens + (current_time - previous_time) * rate,\n            )\n\n        allowed = tokens >= cost\n        if allowed:\n            tokens -= cost\n\n        results.append(allowed)\n        previous_time = current_time\n\n    return results\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-006", "category": "coding", "title": "RFC 6901 JSON Pointer lookup", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 8197, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 443, "reasoning_tokens": 164, "input_tokens": 325, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1217, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 18, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 18}, "workflow_id": "0sfj13bccaa7-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138daf49-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:05-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\n\n\ndef resolve_pointer(doc, pointer: str):\n    if pointer == \"\":\n        return doc\n    if not pointer.startswith(\"/\"):\n        raise ValueError(\"A non-empty JSON Pointer must start with '/'\")\n\n    tokens = []\n    for raw_token in pointer.split(\"/\")[1:]:\n        if re.search(r\"~(?:[^01]|$)\", raw_token):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid escape in token: {raw_token!r}\")\n        tokens.append(raw_token.replace(\"~1\", \"/\").replace(\"~0\", \"~\"))\n\n    current = doc\n    for token in tokens:\n        if isinstance(current, dict):\n            current = current[token]\n        elif isinstance(current, list):\n            if token == \"-\":\n                raise KeyError(token)\n            if re.fullmatch(r\"(?:0|[1-9][0-9]*)\", token) is None:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid list index: {token!r}\")\n\n            # Compare before converting, avoiding limits on huge integer strings.\n            bound = str(len(current))\n            if len(token) > len(bound) or (\n                len(token) == len(bound) and token >= bound\n            ):\n                raise KeyError(token)\n            current = current[int(token)]\n        else:\n            raise KeyError(token)\n\n    return current\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-005", "category": "coding", "title": "Strict CSV line parser", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 7880, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 620, "reasoning_tokens": 313, "input_tokens": 245, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1312, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj144bad3d-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138daf48-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:06-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef parse_csv_line(line: str, delimiter: str = \",\") -> list[str]:\n    if not isinstance(delimiter, str) or len(delimiter) != 1 or delimiter == '\"':\n        raise ValueError('delimiter must be a single character other than \\'\"\\'')\n    \n    fields: list[str] = []\n    n = len(line)\n    i = 0\n\n    while True:\n        if i < n and line[i] == '\"':\n            i += 1\n            chars: list[str] = []\n\n            while i < n:\n                if line[i] != '\"':\n                    chars.append(line[i])\n                    i += 1\n                elif i + 1 < n and line[i + 1] == '\"':\n                    chars.append('\"')\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    i += 1\n                    break\n            else:\n                raise ValueError(\"unterminated quoted field\")\n\n            if i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                raise ValueError(\"closing quote must be followed by delimiter or end of line\")\n\n            fields.append(\"\".join(chars))\n        else:\n            start = i\n            while i < n and line[i] != delimiter:\n                if line[i] == '\"':\n                    raise ValueError(\"quote in unquoted field\")\n                i += 1\n            fields.append(line[start:i])\n\n        if i == n:\n            return fields\n\n        i += 1\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-007", "category": "coding", "title": "Glob matching with character classes", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.75, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 8691, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 859, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 299, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 4771, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.75, "total": 20, "failures": [{"test": "assert glob_match(\"*.py\", \"main.py\")", "line": 1, "error": "AssertionError: "}, {"test": "assert glob_match(\"**/*.py\", \"src/pkg/main.py\")", "line": 3, "error": "AssertionError: "}, {"test": "assert glob_match(\"[]]x\", \"]x\")", "line": 11, "error": "AssertionError: "}, {"test": "assert glob_match(\"[abc\", \"[abc\")", "line": 15, "error": "AssertionError: "}, {"test": "assert not glob_match(\"*\", \"a/b\")", "line": 17, "error": "AssertionError: "}], "pass": false, "load_error": null, "passed": 15}, "workflow_id": "0sfj145a9162-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dd65a-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:07-0500", "answer": "Here's the Python function `glob_match` that implements the specified glob pattern matching:\n\n```python\ndef glob_match(pattern: str, name: str) -> bool:\n    def match_set(pattern_iter, name_char):\n        try:\n            pattern_char = next(pattern_iter)\n        except StopIteration:\n            return False\n\n        negate = False\n        if pattern_char in '!^':\n            negate = True\n            try:\n                pattern_char = next(pattern_iter)\n            except StopIteration:\n                return False\n\n        matched = False\n        while True:\n            if pattern_char == ']':\n                return matched != negate\n\n            if pattern_char == '\\\\':\n                try:\n                    pattern_char = next(pattern_iter)\n                except StopIteration:\n                    return False\n\n            start_char = pattern_char\n            try:\n                pattern_char = next(pattern_iter)\n            except StopIteration:\n                return False\n\n            if pattern_char == '-':\n                try:\n                    end_char = next(pattern_iter)\n                except StopIteration:\n                    return False\n                if end_char == ']':\n                    if start_char == name_char or '-' == name_char:\n                        matched = True\n                    return matched != negate\n                if start_char <= name_char <= end_char:\n                    matched = True\n                try:\n                    pattern_char = next(pattern_iter)\n                except StopIteration:\n                    return False\n            else:\n                if start_char == name_char:\n                    matched = True\n\n    def match(pattern_iter, name_iter):\n        try:\n            pattern_char = next(pattern_iter)\n        except StopIteration:\n            return next(name_iter, None) is None\n\n        if pattern_char == '\\\\':\n            try:\n                pattern_char = next(pattern_iter)\n            except StopIteration:\n                pattern_char = '\\\\'\n            try:\n                name_char = next(name_iter)\n            except StopIteration:\n                return False\n            if pattern_char != name_char:\n                return False\n            return match(pattern_iter, name_iter)\n\n        elif pattern_char == '?':\n            try:\n                name_char = next(name_iter)\n            except StopIteration:\n                return False\n            if name_char == '/':\n                return False\n            return match(pattern_iter, name_iter)\n\n        elif pattern_char == '*':\n            try:\n                next_pattern_char = next(pattern_iter)\n            except StopIteration:\n                next_pattern_char = None\n\n            if next_pattern_char == '*':\n                # Handle **\n                try:\n                    next_next_pattern_char = next(pattern_iter)\n                except StopIteration:\n                    next_next_pattern_char = None\n\n                # Try all possible splits for **\n                name_rest = list(name_iter)\n                for i in range(len(name_rest) + 1):\n                    if match(iter([next_next_pattern_char] if next_next_pattern_char is not None else []),\n                             iter(name_rest[i:])):\n                        return True\n                return False\n            else:\n                # Handle *\n                name_rest = list(name_iter)\n                for i in range(len(name_rest) + 1):\n                    if name_rest[i:] and '/' in name_rest[:i]:\n                        continue\n                    if match(iter([next_pattern_char] if next_pattern_char is not None else []),\n                             iter(name_rest[i:])):\n                        return True\n                return False\n\n        elif pattern_char == '[':\n            try:\n                name_char = next(name_iter)\n            except StopIteration:\n                return False\n            if name_char == '/'"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-008", "category": "coding", "title": "Subtract IPv4 CIDR blocks", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 8372, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 682, "reasoning_tokens": 217, "input_tokens": 224, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1857, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj146f88fd-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dd65b-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:07-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport ipaddress\nimport re\n\n\n_CIDR_PATTERN = re.compile(\n    r\"(?:0|[1-9][0-9]{0,2})\"\n    r\"(?:\\.(?:0|[1-9][0-9]{0,2})){3}/[0-9]+\"\n)\n\n\ndef cidr_subtract(base: str, remove: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    def parse(block: str) -> ipaddress.IPv4Network:\n        if not isinstance(block, str) or _CIDR_PATTERN.fullmatch(block) is None:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Malformed IPv4 CIDR block: {block!r}\")\n\n        address, prefix = block.split(\"/\")\n        # Normalize leading zeros in the prefix without converting an\n        # arbitrarily long decimal string to an integer.\n        prefix = prefix.lstrip(\"0\") or \"0\"\n        if len(prefix) > 2 or int(prefix) > 32:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid prefix length: {block!r}\")\n\n        return ipaddress.IPv4Network(f\"{address}/{prefix}\", strict=True)\n\n    network = parse(base)\n    start = int(network.network_address)\n    end = int(network.broadcast_address)\n\n    intervals = []\n    for block in remove:\n        other = parse(block)  # Validate every entry, even if nothing remains.\n        left = max(start, int(other.network_address))\n        right = min(end, int(other.broadcast_address))\n        if left <= right:\n            intervals.append((left, right))\n\n    intervals.sort()\n    result = []\n\n    def append_range(left: int, right: int) -> None:\n        result.extend(\n            str(block)\n            for block in ipaddress.summarize_address_range(\n                ipaddress.IPv4Address(left),\n                ipaddress.IPv4Address(right),\n            )\n        )\n\n    cursor = start\n    for left, right in intervals:\n        if right < cursor:\n            continue\n        if left > cursor:\n            append_range(cursor, left - 1)\n        cursor = right + 1\n        if cursor > end:\n            break\n\n    if cursor <= end:\n        append_range(cursor, end)\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-009", "category": "coding", "title": "Exact arithmetic expression evaluator", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6576, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 665, "reasoning_tokens": 75, "input_tokens": 355, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 2547, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj15c973e3-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dd65c-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:07-0500", "answer": "```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\n\ndef evaluate(expr: str) -> Fraction:\n    tokens: list[int | str] = []\n    i = 0\n\n    while i < len(expr):\n        ch = expr[i]\n        if ch.isspace():\n            i += 1\n        elif \"0\" <= ch <= \"9\":\n            value = 0\n            while i < len(expr) and \"0\" <= expr[i] <= \"9\":\n                value = value * 10 + ord(expr[i]) - ord(\"0\")\n                i += 1\n            tokens.append(value)\n        elif expr.startswith(\"**\", i):\n            tokens.append(\"**\")\n            i += 2\n        elif ch in \"+-*/()\":\n            tokens.append(ch)\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown character at position {i}: {ch!r}\")\n\n    pos = 0\n\n    def peek() -> int | str | None:\n        return tokens[pos] if pos < len(tokens) else None\n\n    def atom() -> Fraction:\n        nonlocal pos\n        token = peek()\n        if isinstance(token, int):\n            pos += 1\n            return Fraction(token)\n        if token == \"(\":\n            pos += 1\n            value = expression()\n            if peek() != \")\":\n                raise ValueError(\"Expected closing parenthesis\")\n            pos += 1\n            return value\n        raise ValueError(\"Expected an integer or opening parenthesis\")\n\n    def power() -> Fraction:\n        nonlocal pos\n        base = atom()\n        if peek() == \"**\":\n            pos += 1\n            exponent = unary()\n            if exponent.denominator != 1:\n                raise ValueError(\"Exponent must be an integer\")\n            return base ** exponent.numerator\n        return base\n\n    def unary() -> Fraction:\n        nonlocal pos\n        negative = False\n        while peek() in (\"+\", \"-\"):\n            if peek() == \"-\":\n                negative = not negative\n            pos += 1\n        value = power()\n        return -value if negative else value\n\n    def term() -> Fraction:\n        nonlocal pos\n        value = unary()\n        while peek() in (\"*\", \"/\"):\n            operator = peek()\n            pos += 1\n            right = unary()\n            value = value * right if operator == \"*\" else value / right\n        return value\n\n    def expression() -> Fraction:\n        nonlocal pos\n        value = term()\n        while peek() in (\"+\", \"-\"):\n            operator = peek()\n            pos += 1\n            right = term()\n            value = value + right if operator == \"+\" else value - right\n        return value\n\n    result = expression()\n    if pos != len(tokens):\n        raise ValueError(\"Unexpected token\")\n    return result\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-008", "category": "coding", "title": "Subtract IPv4 CIDR blocks", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 9187, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1435, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 221, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 5266, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj146f88fa-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dd65b-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:07-0500", "answer": "I'll write a function that handles CIDR subtraction by converting to integer ranges, subtracting, and converting back.\n\n```python\nimport ipaddress\n\ndef _parse_cidr(s: str) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Parse a strict IPv4 CIDR string, return (network_int, prefix_len). Raise ValueError if malformed.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Not a string: {s!r}\")\n\n    # Must contain exactly one '/'\n    if s.count('/') != 1:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Missing or extra '/': {s!r}\")\n\n    addr_part, prefix_part = s.split('/')\n\n    # Parse prefix length\n    if not prefix_part.isdigit():\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid prefix length: {prefix_part!r}\")\n    prefix_len = int(prefix_part)\n    if prefix_len < 0 or prefix_len > 32:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Prefix length out of range: {prefix_len}\")\n\n    # Parse IPv4 address - must be exactly 4 octets\n    octets = addr_part.split('.')\n    if len(octets) != 4:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Not exactly 4 octets: {addr_part!r}\")\n\n    octet_vals = []\n    for octet in octets:\n        # No leading zeros (except \"0\" itself)\n        if len(octet) > 1 and octet[0] == '0':\n            raise ValueError(f\"Leading zero in octet: {octet!r}\")\n        if not octet.isdigit():\n            raise ValueError(f\"Non-digit octet: {octet!r}\")\n        val = int(octet)\n        if val < 0 or val > 255:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Octet out of range: {val}\")\n        octet_vals.append(val)\n\n    # Reject IPv6 (contains ':')\n    if ':' in s:\n        raise ValueError(f\"IPv6 not allowed: {s!r}\")\n\n    addr_int = (octet_vals[0] << 24) | (octet_vals[1] << 16) | (octet_vals[2] << 8) | octet_vals[3]\n\n    # Check host bits are not set\n    if prefix_len < 32:\n        host_mask = (1 << (32 - prefix_len)) - 1\n        if addr_int & host_mask:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Host bits set: {s!r}\")\n\n    return addr_int, prefix_len\n\ndef _int_to_cidr(addr_int: int, prefix_len: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Convert network integer and prefix length to CIDR string.\"\"\"\n    octets = [\n        (addr_int >> 24) & 0xFF,\n        (addr_int >> 16) & 0xFF,\n        (addr_int >> 8) & 0xFF,\n        addr_int & 0xFF,\n    ]\n    return f\"{octets[0]}.{octets[1]}.{octets[2]}.{octets[3]}/{prefix_len}\"\n\ndef _range_to_cidrs(start: int, end: int) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Convert an inclusive integer range [start, end] to minimal list of CIDR blocks.\"\"\"\n    result = []\n    while start <= end:\n        # Find the largest block starting at 'start' that fits in [start, end]\n        # The block size is limited by: lowest set bit of start, and remaining range\n        max_size_by_start = start & -start if start != 0 else (1 << 32)\n        max_size_by_range = end - start + 1\n\n        # Find largest power of 2 <= min(max_size_by_start, max_size_by_range)\n        size = 1\n        while size * 2 <= max_size_by_start and size * 2 <= max_size_by_range:\n            size *= 2\n\n        # prefix_len = 32 - log2(size)\n        prefix_len = 32\n        temp = size\n        while temp > 1:\n            temp >>= 1\n            prefix_len -= 1\n\n        result.append(_int_to_cidr(start, prefix_len))\n        start += size\n\n    return result\n\ndef cidr_subtract(base: str, remove: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    # Parse base\n    base_addr, base_prefix = _parse_cidr(base)\n    base_size = 1 << (32 - base_prefix)\n    base_start = base_addr\n    base_end = base_addr + base_size - 1\n\n    # Parse all remove blocks, clip to base range, collect as intervals\n    remove_intervals = []\n    for r in remove:\n        r_addr, r_prefix = _parse_cidr(r)\n        r_size = 1 << (32 - r_prefix)\n        r_start = r_addr\n        r_end = r_addr + r_size - 1\n\n        # Clip to base range\n        clip_start = max(r_start, base_start)\n        clip_end = min(r_end, base_end)\n\n        if clip_start <= clip_end:\n            remove_intervals.append((clip_start, clip_end))\n\n    # Sort and merge overlapping/adjacent intervals\n    if not remove_intervals:\n        return [_int_to_cidr(base_start, base_prefix)] if base_size > 0"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-009", "category": "coding", "title": "Exact arithmetic expression evaluator", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.5, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 8955, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 823, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 355, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 4111, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.5, "total": 20, "failures": [{"test": "assert evaluate(\"1 + 2 * 3\") == 7", "line": 11, "error": "ValueError: Unexpected token at end of expression"}, {"test": "assert evaluate(\"(1 + 2) * 3\") == 9", "line": 12, "error": "ValueError: Unexpected token at end of expression"}, {"test": "assert evaluate(\"7 / 2\") == Fraction(7, 2)", "line": 13, "error": "ValueError: Unexpected token at end of expression"}, {"test": "assert isinstance(evaluate(\"6 / 3\"), Fraction)", "line": 14, "error": "ValueError: Unexpected token at end of expression"}, {"test": "assert evaluate(\"-2 ** 2\") == -4", "line": 15, "error": "AssertionError: "}], "pass": false, "load_error": null, "passed": 10}, "workflow_id": "0sfj15c94cd0-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dd65c-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:10-0500", "answer": "Here's a Python function that evaluates arithmetic expressions exactly as specified, without using `eval`, `exec`, `compile`, or the `ast` module:\n\n```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef evaluate(expr: str) -> Fraction:\n    def tokenize(s: str) -> List[str]:\n        tokens = []\n        i = 0\n        n = len(s)\n        while i < n:\n            c = s[i]\n            if c.isspace():\n                i += 1\n                continue\n            if c in '()+-*/**':\n                if c == '*' and i + 1 < n and s[i+1] == '*':\n                    tokens.append('**')\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    tokens.append(c)\n                    i += 1\n            elif c.isdigit():\n                j = i\n                while j < n and s[j].isdigit():\n                    j += 1\n                tokens.append(s[i:j])\n                i = j\n            else:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid character: {c}\")\n        return tokens\n\n    def parse(tokens: List[str]) -> Fraction:\n        def parse_expression() -> Fraction:\n            return parse_binary_op(parse_term, ['+', '-'])\n\n        def parse_term() -> Fraction:\n            return parse_binary_op(parse_factor, ['*', '/'])\n\n        def parse_factor() -> Fraction:\n            token = tokens.pop(0)\n            if token == '(':\n                expr = parse_expression()\n                if not tokens or tokens.pop(0) != ')':\n                    raise ValueError(\"Unbalanced parentheses\")\n                return expr\n            elif token == '+':\n                return parse_factor()\n            elif token == '-':\n                return -parse_factor()\n            else:\n                try:\n                    return Fraction(int(token))\n                except ValueError:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Invalid number: {token}\")\n\n        def parse_binary_op(parse_next: callable, ops: List[str]) -> Fraction:\n            left = parse_next()\n            while tokens and tokens[0] in ops:\n                op = tokens.pop(0)\n                right = parse_next()\n                if op == '+':\n                    left += right\n                elif op == '-':\n                    left -= right\n                elif op == '*':\n                    left *= right\n                elif op == '/':\n                    if right == 0:\n                        raise ZeroDivisionError(\"division by zero\")\n                    left /= right\n            return left\n\n        def parse_exponentiation() -> Fraction:\n            left = parse_factor()\n            while tokens and tokens[0] == '**':\n                tokens.pop(0)\n                right = parse_exponentiation()\n                if right.denominator != 1:\n                    raise ValueError(\"non-integer exponent\")\n                exponent = right.numerator\n                if left == 0 and exponent < 0:\n                    raise ZeroDivisionError(\"0 raised to a negative power\")\n                left **= exponent\n            return left\n\n        # Replace parse_factor with parse_exponentiation in the parsing chain\n        tokens_copy = tokens.copy()\n        tokens = tokens_copy\n        result = parse_exponentiation()\n        if tokens:\n            raise ValueError(\"Unexpected token at end of expression\")\n        return result\n\n    if not expr.strip():\n        raise ValueError(\"Empty expression\")\n\n    tokens = tokenize(expr)\n    if not tokens:\n        raise ValueError(\"Empty expression\")\n\n    return parse(tokens)\n```\n\nThis implementation:\n\n1. Tokenizes the input string into numbers, operators, and parentheses\n2. Parses the tokens according to the specified operator precedence and associativity rules\n3. Handles unary + and - operators correctly\n4. Implements right-associative exponentiation with proper handling of negative exponents\n5. Returns results as exact fractions\n6. Raises appropriate exceptions for syntax errors and division by zero\n\nThe parsing is done using recursive descent with separ"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-009", "category": "coding", "title": "Exact arithmetic expression evaluator", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 10675, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1310, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 349, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 5568, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj15c973e1-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dd65c-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:11-0500", "answer": "I'll write a recursive descent parser for this arithmetic expression evaluator.\n\n```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\ndef evaluate(expr: str) -> Fraction:\n    # Tokenizer\n    tokens = []\n    i = 0\n    n = len(expr)\n    while i < n:\n        c = expr[i]\n        if c.isspace():\n            i += 1\n            continue\n        if c.isdigit():\n            j = i\n            while j < n and expr[j].isdigit():\n                j += 1\n            tokens.append(('NUM', int(expr[i:j])))\n            i = j\n        elif c in '+-*/()':\n            if c == '*':\n                if i + 1 < n and expr[i+1] == '*':\n                    tokens.append(('OP', '**'))\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    tokens.append(('OP', '*'))\n                    i += 1\n            else:\n                tokens.append(('OP', c))\n                i += 1\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown character: {c!r}\")\n    \n    if not tokens:\n        raise ValueError(\"Empty expression\")\n    \n    # Parser using recursive descent\n    pos = [0]  # mutable position\n    \n    def peek():\n        if pos[0] < len(tokens):\n            return tokens[pos[0]]\n        return None\n    \n    def consume():\n        tok = tokens[pos[0]]\n        pos[0] += 1\n        return tok\n    \n    def expect_op(op):\n        tok = peek()\n        if tok is None or tok[0] != 'OP' or tok[1] != op:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Expected {op!r}\")\n        consume()\n    \n    # Grammar:\n    # expr := term (('+' | '-') term)*\n    # term := factor (('*' | '/') factor)*\n    # factor := ('+' | '-') factor | power\n    # power := primary ('**' factor)?    # right-associative, right side can have unary\n    # primary := NUM | '(' expr ')'\n    \n    def parse_expr():\n        result = parse_term()\n        while True:\n            tok = peek()\n            if tok is not None and tok[0] == 'OP' and tok[1] in ('+', '-'):\n                op = consume()[1]\n                right = parse_term()\n                if op == '+':\n                    result = result + right\n                else:\n                    result = result - right\n            else:\n                break\n        return result\n    \n    def parse_term():\n        result = parse_factor()\n        while True:\n            tok = peek()\n            if tok is not None and tok[0] == 'OP' and tok[1] in ('*', '/'):\n                op = consume()[1]\n                right = parse_factor()\n                if op == '*':\n                    result = result * right\n                else:\n                    if right == 0:\n                        raise ZeroDivisionError(\"Division by zero\")\n                    result = result / right\n            else:\n                break\n        return result\n    \n    def parse_factor():\n        tok = peek()\n        if tok is not None and tok[0] == 'OP' and tok[1] in ('+', '-'):\n            op = consume()[1]\n            val = parse_factor()\n            if op == '-':\n                return -val\n            return val\n        return parse_power()\n    \n    def parse_power():\n        base = parse_primary()\n        tok = peek()\n        if tok is not None and tok[0] == 'OP' and tok[1] == '**':\n            consume()\n            # Right side of ** can start with unary operators\n            exponent = parse_factor()\n            # Check for integer exponent\n            if exponent.denominator != 1:\n                raise ValueError(\"Non-integer exponent\")\n            exp_int = exponent.numerator\n            # Handle 0 ** negative\n            if base == 0 and exp_int < 0:\n                raise ZeroDivisionError(\"0 cannot be raised to a negative power\")\n            # Use exact integer power\n            if exp_int >= 0:\n                result = Fraction(base.numerator ** exp_int, base.denominator ** exp_int)\n            else:\n                result = Fraction(base.denominator ** (-exp_int), base.numerator ** (-exp_int))\n            return result\n        return base\n    \n    def parse_primary():\n        tok = peek()\n     "}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-012", "category": "coding", "title": "Token bucket rate limiter", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 14399, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 865, "reasoning_tokens": 592, "input_tokens": 252, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1137, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj151bf091-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138e247f-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:14-0500", "answer": "```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\n\ndef token_bucket(\n    capacity: int,\n    refill_per_sec: float,\n    requests: list[tuple[float, int]],\n) -> list[bool]:\n    if capacity < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"capacity must be at least 1\")\n    if refill_per_sec < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"refill_per_sec must be non-negative\")\n    if not requests:\n        return []\n\n    # Fractions preserve the exact real values represented by input floats.\n    maximum = Fraction(capacity)\n    tokens = maximum\n    rate = Fraction(refill_per_sec)\n    previous = None\n    results: list[bool] = []\n\n    for timestamp, cost in requests:\n        if not isinstance(cost, int) or cost < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"cost must be an integer at least 1\")\n\n        now = Fraction(timestamp)\n        if previous is not None:\n            if now < previous:\n                raise ValueError(\"timestamps must be non-decreasing\")\n            tokens = min(maximum, tokens + (now - previous) * rate)\n        previous = now\n\n        allowed = tokens >= cost\n        if allowed:\n            tokens -= cost\n        results.append(allowed)\n\n    return results\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-006", "category": "coding", "title": "RFC 6901 JSON Pointer lookup", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 16913, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1095, "reasoning_tokens": 746, "input_tokens": 325, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1538, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 18, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 18}, "workflow_id": "0sfj13bca395-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138daf49-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:14-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef resolve_pointer(doc, pointer: str):\n    \"\"\"Return the value referenced by an RFC 6901 JSON Pointer.\"\"\"\n    if pointer == \"\":\n        return doc\n    if not pointer.startswith(\"/\"):\n        raise ValueError(\"A nonempty JSON Pointer must start with '/'\")\n\n    current = doc\n    for raw_token in pointer.split(\"/\")[1:]:\n        for i, char in enumerate(raw_token):\n            if char == \"~\" and (\n                i + 1 == len(raw_token) or raw_token[i + 1] not in \"01\"\n            ):\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid escape in token: {raw_token!r}\")\n\n        token = raw_token.replace(\"~1\", \"/\").replace(\"~0\", \"~\")\n\n        if isinstance(current, dict):\n            current = current[token]\n        elif isinstance(current, list):\n            if token == \"-\":\n                raise KeyError(token)\n\n            if (\n                not token\n                or (len(token) > 1 and token[0] == \"0\")\n                or any(char < \"0\" or char > \"9\" for char in token)\n            ):\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid array index: {token!r}\")\n\n            # Compare before converting, so arbitrarily long valid indices\n            # raise KeyError rather than hitting Python's integer-string limit.\n            length = str(len(current))\n            if len(token) > len(length) or (\n                len(token) == len(length) and token >= length\n            ):\n                raise KeyError(token)\n\n            current = current[int(token)]\n        else:\n            raise KeyError(token)\n\n    return current\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-011", "category": "coding", "title": "Add business days with holidays", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 14442, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1045, "reasoning_tokens": 796, "input_tokens": 230, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 948, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 15, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 15}, "workflow_id": "0sfj1559e917-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138e247e-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:14-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom datetime import date, timedelta\n\n\ndef add_business_days(start: str, days: int, holidays: list[str]) -> str:\n    def parse_date(value: str) -> date:\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or re.fullmatch(\n            r\"[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}\", value\n        ) is None:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid date format: {value!r}\")\n        return date.fromisoformat(value)\n\n    current = parse_date(start)\n    holiday_dates = {parse_date(holiday) for holiday in holidays}\n\n    def is_business_day(day: date) -> bool:\n        return day.weekday() < 5 and day not in holiday_dates\n\n    step = timedelta(days=-1 if days < 0 else 1)\n\n    if days == 0:\n        while not is_business_day(current):\n            current += step\n    else:\n        remaining = abs(days)\n        while remaining:\n            current += step\n            if is_business_day(current):\n                remaining -= 1\n\n    return current.isoformat()\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-007", "category": "coding", "title": "Glob matching with character classes", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 16586, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1088, "reasoning_tokens": 296, "input_tokens": 308, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3536, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj145a9160-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dd65a-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:14-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef glob_match(pattern: str, name: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Match an entire name against a case-sensitive glob pattern.\"\"\"\n    tokens = []\n    i = 0\n\n    while i < len(pattern):\n        ch = pattern[i]\n\n        if ch == \"\\\\\":\n            if i + 1 < len(pattern):\n                tokens.append((\"literal\", pattern[i + 1]))\n                i += 2\n            else:\n                tokens.append((\"literal\", \"\\\\\"))\n                i += 1\n\n        elif ch == \"*\":\n            if i + 1 < len(pattern) and pattern[i + 1] == \"*\":\n                tokens.append((\"globstar\", None))\n                i += 2\n            else:\n                tokens.append((\"star\", None))\n                i += 1\n\n        elif ch == \"?\":\n            tokens.append((\"any\", None))\n            i += 1\n\n        elif ch == \"[\":\n            start = i + 1\n            negated = (\n                start < len(pattern) and pattern[start] in \"!^\"\n            )\n            if negated:\n                start += 1\n\n            # An initial ']' is a member, not the closing delimiter.\n            search_from = start\n            if search_from < len(pattern) and pattern[search_from] == \"]\":\n                search_from += 1\n            end = pattern.find(\"]\", search_from)\n\n            if end == -1:\n                tokens.append((\"literal\", \"[\"))\n                i += 1\n                continue\n\n            members = pattern[start:end]\n            singles = set()\n            ranges = []\n            k = 0\n\n            while k < len(members):\n                # Boundary hyphens are always literal.\n                if members[k] == \"-\" and k in (0, len(members) - 1):\n                    singles.add(\"-\")\n                    k += 1\n                elif (\n                    k + 2 < len(members)\n                    and members[k + 1] == \"-\"\n                    and not (\n                        k + 2 == len(members) - 1\n                        and members[k + 2] == \"-\"\n                    )\n                ):\n                    low, high = ord(members[k]), ord(members[k + 2])\n                    if low <= high:\n                        ranges.append((low, high))\n                    k += 3\n                else:\n                    singles.add(members[k])\n                    k += 1\n\n            tokens.append((\"set\", (negated, singles, ranges)))\n            i = end + 1\n\n        else:\n            tokens.append((\"literal\", ch))\n            i += 1\n\n    # dp[j]: the tokens processed so far match name[:j].\n    dp = [False] * (len(name) + 1)\n    dp[0] = True\n\n    for kind, value in tokens:\n        current = [False] * (len(name) + 1)\n\n        if kind in (\"star\", \"globstar\"):\n            current[0] = dp[0]\n            for j, ch in enumerate(name, 1):\n                current[j] = dp[j] or (\n                    current[j - 1] and (kind == \"globstar\" or ch != \"/\")\n                )\n        else:\n            for j, ch in enumerate(name, 1):\n                if not dp[j - 1]:\n                    continue\n\n                if kind == \"literal\":\n                    matches = ch == value\n                elif kind == \"any\":\n                    matches = ch != \"/\"\n                else:\n                    negated, singles, ranges = value\n                    code = ord(ch)\n                    contained = ch in singles or any(\n                        low <= code <= high for low, high in ranges\n                    )\n                    matches = ch != \"/\" and (contained != negated)\n\n                current[j] = matches\n\n        dp = current\n\n    return dp[-1]\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-010", "category": "coding", "title": "Optimal string alignment distance", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 15555, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 937, "reasoning_tokens": 639, "input_tokens": 155, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1118, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj15d87ef5-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dfd6d-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:17-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef osa_distance(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the optimal string alignment distance using linear space.\"\"\"\n    if a == b:\n        return 0\n\n    # Use the shorter string for the columns.\n    if len(a) < len(b):\n        a, b = b, a\n\n    n = len(b)\n    if n == 0:\n        return len(a)\n\n    previous = list(range(n + 1))\n    previous_previous = previous\n\n    for i, char_a in enumerate(a, start=1):\n        current = [i] + [0] * n\n\n        for j, char_b in enumerate(b, start=1):\n            current[j] = min(\n                previous[j] + 1,                      # Deletion\n                current[j - 1] + 1,                   # Insertion\n                previous[j - 1] + (char_a != char_b),  # Substitution\n            )\n\n            if (\n                i > 1\n                and j > 1\n                and char_a == b[j - 2]\n                and a[i - 2] == char_b\n            ):\n                current[j] = min(\n                    current[j],\n                    previous_previous[j - 2] + 1,\n                )\n\n        previous_previous, previous = previous, current\n\n    return previous[n]\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-008", "category": "coding", "title": "Subtract IPv4 CIDR blocks", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 22851, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 1399, "reasoning_tokens": 1020, "input_tokens": 224, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1533, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 17, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 17}, "workflow_id": "0sfj146f88fc-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dd65b-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:21-0500", "answer": "```python\nimport re\nfrom ipaddress import IPv4Address, IPv4Network, summarize_address_range\n\n\ndef cidr_subtract(base: str, remove: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    def parse(block: str) -> IPv4Network:\n        if not isinstance(block, str) or re.fullmatch(\n            r\"(?:[0-9]{1,3}\\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}/[0-9]+\", block\n        ) is None:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Malformed IPv4 CIDR block: {block!r}\")\n        return IPv4Network(block, strict=True)\n\n    base_network = parse(base)\n    base_start = int(base_network.network_address)\n    base_end = int(base_network.broadcast_address)\n\n    # Validate every removal block, even if an earlier one covers all of base.\n    intervals: list[tuple[int, int]] = []\n    for block in remove:\n        network = parse(block)\n        start = max(base_start, int(network.network_address))\n        end = min(base_end, int(network.broadcast_address))\n        if start <= end:\n            intervals.append((start, end))\n    intervals.sort()\n\n    result: list[str] = []\n\n    def append_range(start: int, end: int) -> None:\n        result.extend(\n            str(network)\n            for network in summarize_address_range(\n                IPv4Address(start), IPv4Address(end)\n            )\n        )\n\n    cursor = base_start\n    for start, end in intervals:\n        if start > cursor:\n            append_range(cursor, start - 1)\n        cursor = max(cursor, end + 1)\n        if cursor > base_end:\n            break\n\n    if cursor <= base_end:\n        append_range(cursor, base_end)\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-007", "category": "coding", "title": "Glob matching with character classes", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 40200, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 2291, "reasoning_tokens": 1536, "input_tokens": 308, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3173, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj145a9161-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dd65a-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:39-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef glob_match(pattern: str, name: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return whether the whole name matches the case-sensitive glob pattern.\"\"\"\n    tokens = []\n    i = 0\n\n    while i < len(pattern):\n        ch = pattern[i]\n\n        if ch == \"\\\\\":\n            if i + 1 < len(pattern):\n                tokens.append((\"literal\", pattern[i + 1]))\n                i += 2\n            else:\n                tokens.append((\"literal\", \"\\\\\"))\n                i += 1\n\n        elif ch == \"*\":\n            end = i + 1\n            while end < len(pattern) and pattern[end] == \"*\":\n                end += 1\n            # Any uninterrupted run of at least two stars is equivalent to **.\n            tokens.append((\"globstar\" if end - i >= 2 else \"star\", None))\n            i = end\n\n        elif ch == \"?\":\n            tokens.append((\"question\", None))\n            i += 1\n\n        elif ch == \"[\":\n            start = i + 1\n            negated = start < len(pattern) and pattern[start] in \"!^\"\n            if negated:\n                start += 1\n\n            # A leading ] belongs to the set, so cannot close it.\n            search_from = start\n            if search_from < len(pattern) and pattern[search_from] == \"]\":\n                search_from += 1\n            end = pattern.find(\"]\", search_from)\n\n            if end == -1:\n                tokens.append((\"literal\", \"[\"))\n                i += 1\n                continue\n\n            members = pattern[start:end]\n            intervals = []\n            k = 0\n            while k < len(members):\n                if k + 2 < len(members) and members[k + 1] == \"-\":\n                    low, high = members[k], members[k + 2]\n                    if low <= high:\n                        intervals.append((low, high))\n                    k += 3\n                else:\n                    intervals.append((members[k], members[k]))\n                    k += 1\n\n            tokens.append((\"set\", (negated, intervals)))\n            i = end + 1\n\n        else:\n            tokens.append((\"literal\", ch))\n            i += 1\n\n    # previous[j] means the processed tokens match name[:j].\n    previous = [False] * (len(name) + 1)\n    previous[0] = True\n\n    for kind, value in tokens:\n        current = [False] * (len(name) + 1)\n\n        if kind in (\"star\", \"globstar\"):\n            current[0] = previous[0]\n            crosses_slashes = kind == \"globstar\"\n            for j, ch in enumerate(name, 1):\n                current[j] = previous[j] or (\n                    current[j - 1] and (crosses_slashes or ch != \"/\")\n                )\n\n        elif kind == \"literal\":\n            for j, ch in enumerate(name, 1):\n                current[j] = previous[j - 1] and ch == value\n\n        elif kind == \"question\":\n            for j, ch in enumerate(name, 1):\n                current[j] = previous[j - 1] and ch != \"/\"\n\n        else:\n            negated, intervals = value\n            for j, ch in enumerate(name, 1):\n                if previous[j - 1] and ch != \"/\":\n                    contained = any(low <= ch <= high for low, high in intervals)\n                    current[j] = contained != negated\n\n        previous = current\n\n    return previous[len(name)]\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-009", "category": "coding", "title": "Exact arithmetic expression evaluator", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 40013, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 2453, "reasoning_tokens": 1646, "input_tokens": 355, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 3634, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 20, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 20}, "workflow_id": "0sfj15c973e4-d02a-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dd65c-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:11:40-0500", "answer": "```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\n\ndef evaluate(expr: str) -> Fraction:\n    \"\"\"Evaluate an arithmetic expression exactly, without executing Python code.\"\"\"\n    precedence = {\"+\": 1, \"-\": 1, \"*\": 2, \"/\": 2,\n                  \"u+\": 3, \"u-\": 3, \"**\": 4}\n    output: list[int | str] = []\n    operators: list[str] = []\n    need_operand = True\n    i = 0\n    n = len(expr)\n\n    # Validate the entire expression and produce postfix notation before\n    # performing arithmetic, so syntax errors always raise ValueError.\n    while i < n:\n        ch = expr[i]\n\n        if ch.isspace():\n            i += 1\n            continue\n\n        if \"0\" <= ch <= \"9\":\n            if not need_operand:\n                raise ValueError(\"Two operands in a row\")\n\n            # Avoid Python's limit on decimal string-to-integer conversion.\n            value = 0\n            while i < n and \"0\" <= expr[i] <= \"9\":\n                value = value * 10 + ord(expr[i]) - ord(\"0\")\n                i += 1\n            output.append(value)\n            need_operand = False\n            continue\n\n        if ch == \"(\":\n            if not need_operand:\n                raise ValueError(\"Missing operator before '('\")\n            operators.append(\"(\")\n            i += 1\n            continue\n\n        if ch == \")\":\n            if need_operand:\n                raise ValueError(\"Missing operand before ')'\")\n            while operators and operators[-1] != \"(\":\n                output.append(operators.pop())\n            if not operators:\n                raise ValueError(\"Unbalanced parentheses\")\n            operators.pop()\n            i += 1\n            continue\n\n        if ch not in \"+-*/\":\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown character: {ch!r}\")\n\n        op = ch\n        i += 1\n        if op == \"*\" and i < n and expr[i] == \"*\":\n            op = \"**\"\n            i += 1\n\n        if need_operand:\n            if op not in (\"+\", \"-\"):\n                raise ValueError(\"Missing operand\")\n            # Prefix operators never pop pending operators. In particular,\n            # this permits a unary operator on the right side of '**'.\n            operators.append(\"u\" + op)\n        else:\n            while operators and operators[-1] != \"(\":\n                top = operators[-1]\n                if (precedence[top] > precedence[op]\n                        or (precedence[top] == precedence[op] and op != \"**\")):\n                    output.append(operators.pop())\n                else:\n                    break\n            operators.append(op)\n            need_operand = True\n\n    if need_operand:\n        raise ValueError(\"Empty expression or missing operand\")\n\n    while operators:\n        op = operators.pop()\n        if op == \"(\":\n            raise ValueError(\"Unbalanced parentheses\")\n        output.append(op)\n\n    values: list[Fraction] = []\n    for token in output:\n        if isinstance(token, int):\n            values.append(Fraction(token))\n        elif token == \"u+\":\n            continue\n        elif token == \"u-\":\n            values[-1] = -values[-1]\n        else:\n            right = values.pop()\n            left = values.pop()\n\n            if token == \"+\":\n                result = left + right\n            elif token == \"-\":\n                result = left - right\n            elif token == \"*\":\n                result = left * right\n            elif token == \"/\":\n                result = left / right\n            else:  # **\n                if right.denominator != 1:\n                    raise ValueError(\"Exponent must be an integer\")\n                result = left ** right.numerator\n\n            values.append(result)\n\n    return values[0]\n```"}
