{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-010", "category": "coding", "title": "Optimal string alignment distance", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 207269, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 31393, "reasoning_tokens": 31076, "input_tokens": 152, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 970, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 93568, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj15d87ef6-d02a-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138dfd6d-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:14:28-0500", "answer": "```python\ndef osa_distance(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the optimal string alignment (OSA) distance between a and b.\"\"\"\n    n, m = len(a), len(b)\n\n    # d[0][j] = j\n    prev1 = list(range(m + 1))\n    prev2 = None  # becomes d[0] after the first iteration; used for i >= 2\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        curr = [0] * (m + 1)\n        curr[0] = i  # d[i][0] = i\n\n        for j in range(1, m + 1):\n            cost = 0 if a[i - 1] == b[j - 1] else 1\n\n            curr[j] = min(\n                prev1[j] + 1,        # deletion\n                curr[j - 1] + 1,     # insertion\n                prev1[j - 1] + cost  # substitution / match\n            )\n\n            if (\n                i > 1\n                and j > 1\n                and a[i - 1] == b[j - 2]\n                and a[i - 2] == b[j - 1]\n            ):\n                curr[j] = min(curr[j], prev2[j - 2] + cost)  # transposition\n\n        prev2 = prev1\n        prev1 = curr\n\n    return prev1[m]\n```"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "coding-012", "category": "coding", "title": "Token bucket rate limiter", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 229985, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 22830, "reasoning_tokens": 22576, "input_tokens": 249, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 1081, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 85391, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "total": 13, "failures": [], "pass": true, "load_error": null, "passed": 13}, "workflow_id": "0sfj151bf090-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj138e247f-d02a-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:14:50-0500", "answer": "```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\ndef token_bucket(capacity: int, refill_per_sec: float, requests: list[tuple[float, int]]) -> list[bool]:\n    if capacity < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"capacity must be at least 1\")\n    if refill_per_sec < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"refill_per_sec must be non-negative\")\n\n    cap = Fraction(capacity)\n    refill = Fraction(refill_per_sec)\n    tokens = cap\n    last_time = None\n    result = []\n\n    for timestamp, cost in requests:\n        if not isinstance(cost, int) or isinstance(cost, bool) or cost < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"cost must be an integer >= 1\")\n        if last_time is not None and timestamp < last_time:\n            raise ValueError(\"timestamps must be non-decreasing\")\n\n        if last_time is not None:\n            elapsed = Fraction(timestamp) - Fraction(last_time)\n            tokens = min(cap, tokens + elapsed * refill)\n\n        if tokens >= cost:\n            result.append(True)\n            tokens -= cost\n        else:\n            result.append(False)\n\n        last_time = timestamp\n\n    return result\n```"}
