{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "agentic-001", "category": "agentic", "title": "Roll back only the service with a fresh deploy", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4627, "turns": 3, "retries": null, "usage": {"search_calls": 0, "output_tokens": 463, "reasoning_tokens": 127, "input_tokens": 2371, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 492}, "answer_chars": 740, "finish_reason": null, "thinking_chars": null, "detail": {"final_include_failed": [], "missing_required": [], "pass": true, "forbidden_made": [], "within_max_turns": true, "final_exclude_failed": []}, "workflow_id": "0sfj74671084-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7429d198-d02b-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:20:54-0500", "answer": "Summary:\n\n- **Checkout** \u2014 confirmed degraded (18% error rate, p95 2400ms, degraded since 13:41 UTC). Its most recent deploy **d-482** (v2.31.0) went out at 13:38 UTC, within the last hour and right before the degradation started. I rolled it back to **v2.30.4** (rollback job `rb-9917`).\n- **Search** \u2014 also degraded (9% error rate, degraded since 13:05 UTC), but its last deploy **d-455** was on 2026-10-23, well over an hour ago. Per your instruction to only roll back a service with a deploy in the last hour, I did **not** touch search.\n\nWorth flagging for follow-up: search is still erroring despite no recent deploy, so its degradation likely has a different cause (dependency, infra, data, etc.) and may need separate investigation."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "agentic-003", "category": "agentic", "title": "Book travel inside the per-diem policy", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5306, "turns": 3, "retries": null, "usage": {"search_calls": 0, "output_tokens": 653, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3819, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 984}, "answer_chars": 813, "finish_reason": null, "thinking_chars": null, "detail": {"final_include_failed": [], "missing_required": [], "pass": true, "forbidden_made": [], "within_max_turns": true, "final_exclude_failed": []}, "workflow_id": "0sfj74b72c7a-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj7429d197-d02b-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:20:55-0500", "answer": "All booked! Here's your summary for the Rocky Mountain Data Summit in Denver:\n\n**\u2708\ufe0f Outbound flight \u2014 booked**\n- Southwest WN-3301 (confirmation **SWK7QX**)\n- Wed, Nov 11, 2026: ORD 2:45 PM \u2192 DEN 4:50 PM (economy)\n- **$189** \u2014 arrives well before the 6:00 PM latest-arrival policy\n\n**\ud83c\udfe8 Hotel \u2014 booked**\n- Union Station Inn (confirmation **USI-44817**)\n- Check-in Nov 11, check-out Nov 13 (2 nights)\n- $184/night \u00d7 2 = **$368 total** \u2014 within the $189/night per diem and 1.1 miles from the Colorado Convention Center\n\n**Not booked (as requested):**\n- Return flight \u2014 you'll arrange that yourself\n\nNote: I skipped the cheaper American flight ($168) because it arrives at 7:40 PM, past the 6:00 PM policy cutoff, and the $149 hotel because it's 14.2 miles from the venue (over the 5-mile limit). Have a great summit!"}
