{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "agentic-008", "category": "agentic", "title": "Triage a failed pipeline run", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6726, "turns": 4, "retries": null, "usage": {"search_calls": 0, "output_tokens": 667, "reasoning_tokens": 75, "input_tokens": 3945, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 1476}, "answer_chars": 927, "finish_reason": null, "thinking_chars": null, "detail": {"final_include_failed": [], "missing_required": [], "pass": true, "forbidden_made": [], "within_max_turns": true, "final_exclude_failed": []}, "workflow_id": "0sfj7455d262-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj742a1fbd-d02b-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:20:57-0500", "answer": "Triage complete for nightly_sales run 2026-10-25:\n\n**Re-ran (transient failure):**\n- `extract_returns` (sales-data-eng) \u2014 failed on a botocore `ReadTimeoutError` reading from S3 after 3 tries. Timeouts are transient, so I cleared and re-ran it (now try #4, queued).\n\n**Ticket opened (non-transient, not re-run):**\n- `transform_sales` (analytics-eng) \u2014 `SchemaValidationError`: `discount_pct` expected `DECIMAL(5,2)` but got STRING in 1,204 rows (e.g. `'12.5%'`). This is a data/schema issue, so per triage rules I did not re-run it and instead opened **ticket DATA-4417** with analytics-eng.\n\n**Left alone (upstream_failed):**\n- `returns_rollup` (analytics-eng) \u2014 blocked by the extract_returns failure; will unblock if the re-run succeeds.\n- `load_warehouse` (data-platform) and `publish_dashboard` (bi-team) \u2014 blocked by upstream failures, including transform_sales, which is pending the ticket fix. No action taken on these."}
