{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-001", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physics", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 14109, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 3, "output_tokens": 1057, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 802, "search_tokens": 12071, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1642, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2113, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Francis Halzen; IceCube Neutrino Observatory", "expected": "Francis Halzen; IceCube Neutrino Observatory", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 4}, "workflow_id": "0sfjd2b948bc-d02b-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjd057c9d2-d02b-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:23:41-0500", "answer": "The 2026 Nobel Prize in Physics was announced on **6 October 2026** by the Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences. It was awarded to **Francis Halzen** (born 1944 in Tienen, Belgium; professor at the University of Wisconsin\u2013Madison, USA) *\"for decisive contributions to the IceCube Neutrino Observatory and the discovery of high-energy neutrinos of astrophysical origin.\"*\n\nThe citation is built around the **IceCube Neutrino Observatory** \u2014 the cubic-kilometre neutrino detector embedded in the glacial ice at the South Pole in Antarctica, which Halzen first proposed in 1988 and which was completed in 2011. IceCube detects high-energy cosmic neutrinos via flashes of light produced when a neutrino collides with an atomic nucleus in the ice, opening a new window on violent astrophysical environments.\n\n**Sources used:**\n1. NobelPrize.org \u2014 official press release, \"Nobel Prize in Physics 2026\" (6 October 2026): https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/physics/2026/press-release/\n2. PBS News \u2014 \"Nobel Prize in physics awarded to Francis Halzen for demystifying neutrinos\" (Oct. 6, 2026): https://www.pbs.org/newshour/science/watch-live-winner-of-the-2026-nobel-prize-in-physics-is\n3. Scientific American \u2014 \"2026 Nobel Prize in Physics awarded to Francis Halzen for discovery of high-energy neutrinos\": https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/2026-nobel-prize-in-physics-awarded-to-francis-halzen-for-discovery-of-high-energy-neutrinos/\n4. AIP \u2014 \"AIP Congratulates 2026 Nobel Prize Winner in Physics\" (Oct. 6, 2026): https://www.aip.org/aip/aip-congratulates-2026-nobel-prize-winner-in-physics\n\nANSWER: Francis Halzen; IceCube Neutrino Observatory", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
