{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-003", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Literature and Peace laureates", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 14126, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 972, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 802, "search_tokens": 15111, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1979, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1344, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay", "expected": "Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 7}, "workflow_id": "0sfjd2f669ec-d02b-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjd057f0e6-d02b-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:23:41-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the 2026 Nobel Prize winners in Literature and Peace.Both searches point to consistent answers. Let me verify directly against the official Nobel Prize press releases.Both winners are confirmed by the official Nobel Prize press releases, with corroboration from major news outlets.\n\n**2026 Nobel Prize in Literature \u2014 Anne Carson**\nThe Swedish Academy announced on 8 October 2026 that the Canadian poet, essayist, classicist, and translator Anne Carson won \"for her bold and inventive oeuvre that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature\" [NobelPrize.org](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/literature/2026/press-release/). This is also reported by [Al Jazeera](https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/8/canadian-anne-carson-wins-2026-nobel-prize-in-literature) and [PBS News](https://www.pbs.org/newshour/arts/watch-live-winner-of-the-2026-nobel-prize-in-literature-is).\n\n**2026 Nobel Peace Prize \u2014 Navi Pillay**\nThe Norwegian Nobel Committee announced on 9 October 2026 that the South African jurist Navanethem \"Navi\" Pillay won \"for her efforts to promote peace and international law.\" Pillay, born in Durban under apartheid, defended Nelson Mandela and other anti-apartheid activists, served as a judge on South Africa's High Court, the International Criminal Tribunal for Rwanda, and the International Criminal Court, was UN High Commissioner for Human Rights (2008\u20132014), and is now an ad hoc judge at the International Court of Justice in the Myanmar genocide case [NobelPrize.org](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/peace/2026/press-release/). This is corroborated by [Al Jazeera](https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/9/2026-nobel-peace-prize-awarded-to-navi-pillay), [PBS News](https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-live-winner-of-the-2026-nobel-peace-prize-is), and [Britannica](https://www.britannica.com/topic/2026-Nobel-Prize-winners).\n\nANSWER: Literature: Anne Carson; Peace: Navi Pillay", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-002", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4862, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 1, "output_tokens": 165, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 828, "search_tokens": 6820, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 411, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; optogenetics and light-gated ion channels", "expected": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; optogenetics (light-gated ion channels)", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 7}, "workflow_id": "0sfjd408bc2c-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjd057f0e5-d02b-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:23:41-0500", "answer": "The 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine was awarded jointly to **Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, and Georg Nagel** for their discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics, a method that allows researchers to control the activity of individual nerve cells in the living brain using light.\n\nANSWER: Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; optogenetics and light-gated ion channels", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
