{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-002", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 7683, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 2, "output_tokens": 227, "reasoning_tokens": 88, "input_tokens": 13058, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 4497}, "answer_chars": 791, "finish_reason": "completed", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; light-gated ion channels and optogenetics", "expected": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; optogenetics (light-gated ion channels)", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 2}, "workflow_id": "0sfjd408bc29-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjd057f0e5-d02b-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:23:46-0500", "answer": "The **2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine** was awarded jointly to **Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, and Georg Nagel** for their discoveries concerning **light-gated ion channels and optogenetics**. ([physiology.org](https://www.physiology.org/detail/news/2026/10/05/karl-deisseroth--peter-hegemann-and-georg-nagel-named-2026-nobel-laureates-in-physiology-or-medicine?SSO=Y&utm_source=openai))\n\nThe recognized research enables scientists to control nerve-cell activity with light, helping reveal how neurons shape memories, feelings, and behaviours. ([ki.se](https://ki.se/en/about-ki/prizes-and-ceremonies/prizes-and-awards/the-nobel-prize-in-physiology-or-medicine?utm_source=openai))\n\nANSWER: Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; light-gated ion channels and optogenetics", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-004", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 US Open men's singles final", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 15477, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 1188, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 805, "search_tokens": 17619, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1380, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2529, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton", "expected": "Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 4}, "workflow_id": "0sfjd3e14e3b-d02b-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjd05817f7-d02b-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:23:52-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the 2026 US Open men's singles champion.The search results are consistent across multiple sources. Let me verify with the official US Open website and the ATP Tour to confirm the details.**Alexander Zverev** won the men's singles title at the 2026 US Open. He defeated American **Ben Shelton** in the final on Sunday, September 13, 2026, with a score of **6\u20133, 7\u20136(2), 5\u20137, 6\u20132**.\n\nThe win marked Zverev's second Grand Slam title of 2026 (following his French Open victory earlier in the year) and his first US Open title \u2014 making him the first German man to win the US Open since Boris Becker in 1989. Shelton was playing in his first-ever major final and was bidding to become the first American man to win a major since Andy Roddick in 2003.\n\n**Sources used:**\n1. Official US Open website \u2014 \"Alexander Zverev defeats Ben Shelton to win 2026 US Open\" (September 13, 2026): https://www.usopen.org/en_US/news/articles/2026-09-13/alexander_zverev_defeats_ben_shelton_to_win_2026_us_open.html\n2. Wikipedia \u2014 \"2026 US Open \u2013 Men's singles\": https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_US_Open_%E2%80%93_Men%27s_singles\n3. ATP Tour \u2014 \"What were the US Open results?\" (us-open-2026-results): https://www.atptour.com/en/news/us-open-2026-results\n4. USOpenTennisInfo.com \u2014 \"US Open Tennis 2026 Results\": https://usopentennisinfo.com/results/\n\nANSWER: Alexander Zverev; Ben Shelton", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-002", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 17258, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 3, "output_tokens": 975, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 807, "search_tokens": 15370, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 2351, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1220, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics", "expected": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; optogenetics (light-gated ion channels)", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 5}, "workflow_id": "0sfjd408bc2d-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjd057f0e5-d02b-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:23:55-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine laureates.The search results are consistent across multiple sources. Let me verify with the official Nobel Prize press release.The 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine was announced on 5 October 2026 by the Nobel Assembly at Karolinska Institutet. It was awarded jointly to three laureates [TiO7SAUN][jeM77fhK][YRoH777o]:\n\n1. **Karl Deisseroth** \u2014 Howard Hughes Medical Institute and Stanford University, USA (born 1971)\n2. **Peter Hegemann** \u2014 Humboldt University of Berlin, Germany (born 1954)\n3. **Georg Nagel** \u2014 University of W\u00fcrzburg, Germany (born 1953)\n\n**Research area recognized:** The prize was awarded *\"for their discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics.\"* Hegemann and Nagel discovered the protein channelrhodopsin in the single-celled alga *Chlamydomonas*, which opens an ion channel when illuminated by blue light. Deisseroth then introduced the channelrhodopsin gene into nerve cells, creating a light-controlled \"switch\" that lets researchers activate or silence individual neurons in the living brain \u2014 the technique now known as **optogenetics**. This method has revolutionized neuroscience, enabling scientists to map the neural circuits underlying memories, feelings, and behaviors [TiO7SAUN][jeM77fhK][YRoH777o]. The prize amount of 12 million Swedish kronor is shared equally among the three laureates [jeM77fhK].\n\n**Sources:**\n- NobelPrize.org \u2014 Official press release: https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/press-release/ [jeM77fhK][YRoH777o]\n- NobelPrize.org \u2014 Prize summary: https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/summary/ [TiO7SAUN]\n- Nature \u2014 \"Medicine Nobel awarded for brain 'switch' that controls neurons with light\": https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03091-2 [RNAOdDjw]\n- C&EN \u2014 \"Optogenetics researchers win Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine\": https://cen.acs.org/people/nobel-prize/nobel-2026-physiology-medicine/104/web/2026/10 [znK1ld0Z]\n- NBC News \u2014 \"Three scientists just won the 2026 Nobel Prize in medicine for pioneering optogenetics\": https://www.nbcnews.com/world/europe/nobel-prize-medicine-2026-karl-deisseroth-peter-hegemann-georg-nagel-rcna601564 [onsuqH0F]\n\nANSWER: Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-002", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 21117, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 3, "output_tokens": 602, "reasoning_tokens": 454, "input_tokens": 29511, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 4497}, "answer_chars": 756, "finish_reason": "completed", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics", "expected": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; optogenetics (light-gated ion channels)", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 2}, "workflow_id": "0sfjd408bc2b-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjd057f0e5-d02b-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:23:58-0500", "answer": "The **2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine** was awarded jointly to **Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, and Georg Nagel**, announced on October 5, 2026. ([lindau-nobel.org](https://www.lindau-nobel.org/news-nobel-prize-in-physiology-or-medicine-2026/))\n\nThe prize recognized their **\u201cdiscoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics.\u201d** This research enabled scientists to use light-sensitive proteins to control nerve-cell activity and investigate how neural circuits govern brain function. ([nsf.gov](https://www.nsf.gov/bio/updates/nsf-bio-congratulates-winners-2026-nobel-prize-physiology-or?utm_source=openai))\n\nANSWER: Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-002", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 23758, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 621, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 807, "search_tokens": 24657, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1668, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics", "expected": "Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; optogenetics (light-gated ion channels)", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 3}, "workflow_id": "0sfjd408bc2a-d02b-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfjd057f0e5-d02b-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:24:01-0500", "answer": "The 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine was announced on 5 October 2026 by the Nobel Assembly at Karolinska Institutet. It was awarded jointly to three laureates, each receiving one-third of the prize:\n\n- **Karl Deisseroth** \u2014 Howard Hughes Medical Institute and Stanford University, USA\n- **Peter Hegemann** \u2014 Humboldt University of Berlin, Germany (prize-winning work done at the Max Planck Institute for Biochemistry, Martinsried, Germany)\n- **Georg Nagel** \u2014 University of W\u00fcrzburg, Germany (prize-winning work done at the Max Planck Institute for Biophysics, Frankfurt, Germany)\n\nThe prize recognized **\u201ctheir discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics.\u201d** In brief: Hegemann and Nagel discovered the light-sensitive protein channelrhodopsin in the single-celled alga *Chlamydomonas*, and Deisseroth turned that protein into a light-controlled switch for nerve cells, creating optogenetics \u2014 a method that lets researchers switch individual neurons on or off in the living brain and has opened a new era in neuroscience.\n\nSources:\n- NobelPrize.org \u2014 Press release: Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine 2026 (https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/press-release/)\n- NobelPrize.org \u2014 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine 2026, Summary (https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/summary/)\n- Chemical & Engineering News (C&EN) \u2014 \u201cOptogenetics researchers win Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine,\u201d 5 October 2026 (https://cen.acs.org/people/nobel-prize/nobel-2026-physiology-medicine/104/web/2026/10)\n\nANSWER: Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann, Georg Nagel; discoveries concerning light-gated ion channels and optogenetics", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
