{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-011", "category": "grounding", "title": "US 2025 median household income and poverty rate", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 5031, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 1, "output_tokens": 119, "reasoning_tokens": 41, "input_tokens": 12861, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 4435}, "answer_chars": 320, "finish_reason": "completed", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "$87,460; 10.2%", "expected": "$87,460; 10.2%", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 1}, "workflow_id": "0sfj32b6f2b9-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2ff195ba-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:26:24-0500", "answer": "According to the U.S. Census Bureau\u2019s September 15, 2026 release, **real median household income in 2025 was $87,460**, and the **official poverty rate was 10.2%**. ([census.gov](https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/income-poverty-health-insurance-coverage.html?utm_source=openai))\n\nANSWER: $87,460; 10.2%", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-011", "category": "grounding", "title": "US 2025 median household income and poverty rate", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 7185, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 2, "output_tokens": 184, "reasoning_tokens": 78, "input_tokens": 21148, "search_tokens": 0, "cached_input_tokens": 4435}, "answer_chars": 432, "finish_reason": "completed", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "$87,460; 10.2%", "expected": "$87,460; 10.2%", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 2}, "workflow_id": "0sfj32b719cc-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2ff195ba-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:26:26-0500", "answer": "The U.S. Census Bureau\u2019s September 15, 2026 release reported that **real median household income in 2025 was $87,460**. ([census.gov](https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/income-poverty-health-insurance-coverage.html)) Its *Poverty in the United States: 2025* report put the **official poverty rate at 10.2%**. ([census.gov](https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2026/demo/p60-290.html))\n\nANSWER: $87,460; 10.2%", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
