{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-006", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Asian Games medal table leader", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 36760, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 15, "output_tokens": 1300, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 814, "search_tokens": 91316, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 2545, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "China; 169", "expected": "China; 169", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 7}, "workflow_id": "0sfj3200df46-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2ff14794-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:26:44-0500", "answer": "Based on my web searches, I found consistent reporting across multiple major news sources about the final medal table at the 2026 Asian Games in Aichi-Nagoya, Japan.\n\n**China** finished at the top of the medal table for the 12th consecutive Asian Games, winning **169 gold medals** (along with 89 silver and 83 bronze, for a total of 341 medals).\n\nThis figure is confirmed by multiple independent and authoritative sources:\n\n- **Xinhua News Agency** (China's official state news agency): \"China topping the gold medal table for the 12th consecutive edition, and finishing with **169 gold**, 89 silver and 83 bronze medals\" ([english.news.cn](https://english.news.cn/20261004/0d5d63d5f50a41a28f9cf40229426dcf/c.html))\n- **Kyodo News** (Japan): \"China once again finished comfortably atop the medal standings with 341 medals, including **169 golds**\" ([english.kyodonews.net](https://english.kyodonews.net/articles/-/87151))\n- **The Mainichi** (Japan, via Kyodo): \"China finished comfortably atop the medal standings with 341 medals, including **169 golds**\" ([mainichi.jp](https://mainichi.jp/english/articles/20261005/p2g00m0sp002000c))\n- **PTI/The Times of India**: \"China topped the medal tally with 341 medals, including **169 gold**\" ([timesofindia.indiatimes.com](https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/asian-games-2026/asian-games-2026-closing-ceremony-live-updates-mizuho-park-athletic-stadium-date-time-india-flag-bearer/liveblog/134671578.cms))\n- **The Economic Times**: \"China topped the table for the 12th consecutive edition, finishing with **169 gold**, 89 silver and 83 bronze for a total of 341 medals\" ([economictimes.indiatimes.com](https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/sports/other-sports/sayonara-nagoya-asian-games-2026-come-to-a-close-with-a-dazzling-light-and-musical-show-come-2030-aap-qatar-mein-hain/articleshow/134680232.cms))\n- **Olympics.com**: Final medal table coverage confirming China's top position ([olympics.com](https://www.olympics.com/en/news/20th-asian-games-aichi-nagoya-2026-medal-table-live-updates))\n- **Khel Now**: \"China topped the final medal standings with **169 gold**, 89 silver and 83 bronze medals, for a total of 341 medals\" ([khelnow.com](https://khelnow.com/asian-games/final-medal-tally-asian-games-202610))\n\nNote: One source (insidethegames.biz) reported \"189 gold\" which appears to be a typographical error, as it is contradicted by the overwhelming consensus of all other major news agencies including Xinhua, Kyodo, and multiple Indian and Japanese outlets.\n\nANSWER: China; 169", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-009", "category": "grounding", "title": "Latest stable Conductor OSS release (Oct 2026)", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 50747, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": 5, "output_tokens": 3738, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 816, "search_tokens": 26283, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1784, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 10462, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "v3.32.5", "expected": "v3.32.5", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 3}, "workflow_id": "0sfj30217a27-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2ff16ea9-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:26:54-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the latest stable Conductor OSS release.The search shows the releases list is dominated by `v3.33.0-rc*` prereleases with `v3.32.5` as the newest non-RC. I need exact dates and prerelease flags to confirm what was latest stable as of Oct 20, 2026. Let me pull the GitHub API and releases page.I have the key data. Let me confirm via GitHub's dedicated \"latest release\" endpoint (which returns the newest non-prerelease, non-draft release).As of October 20, 2026, the most recent **stable (non\u2011prerelease)** release of Conductor OSS was **v3.32.5**.\n\nReasoning from the sources:\n- GitHub\u2019s releases page for `conductor-oss/conductor` lists the newest entries as the `v3.33.0-rc*` series (rc5 \u2192 rc13), with **`v3.32.5` explicitly badged \u201cLatest\u201d** (published 25 Sep) \u2014 i.e., the project\u2019s designated latest stable release. No GA `v3.33.0` exists; that line is only release candidates. ([github.com/conductor-oss/conductor/releases](https://github.com/conductor-oss/conductor/releases))\n- The GitHub releases API confirms the timeline: `v3.32.5` (`prerelease:false`, `draft:false`, published `2026-09-25T04:58:15Z`), while every newer tag up through Oct 14 (`v3.33.0-rc11/rc12/rc13`) is an `-rc` prerelease, so none qualify as stable. ([api.github.com/repos/conductor-oss/conductor/releases?per_page=40](https://api.github.com/repos/conductor-oss/conductor/releases?per_page=40))\n- GitHub\u2019s \u201clatest release\u201d endpoint (newest non\u2011draft, non\u2011prerelease) returns `tag_name: \"v3.32.5\"` (`prerelease:false`, published `2026-09-25`), which was already out before Oct 20, 2026 and remained the latest stable through that date. ([api.github.com/repos/conductor-oss/conductor/releases/latest](https://api.github.com/repos/conductor-oss/conductor/releases/latest))\n\nANSWER: v3.32.5", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
