{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-007", "category": "grounding", "title": "Python 3.15.0 release date and release manager", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 12465, "turns": 1, "retries": 2, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 570, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 814, "search_tokens": 20442, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1427, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "2026-10-09; Hugo van Kemenade", "expected": "2026-10-09; Hugo van Kemenade", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 3}, "workflow_id": "0sfj30e3d655-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2ff14795-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:24-0500", "answer": "Based on my web search, here's what I found:\n\n**Final Python 3.15.0 release date:** The official Python.org download page for Python 3.15.0 states \"**Release date:** Oct. 9, 2026\" and confirms \"This is the stable release of Python 3.15.0\" [1]. PEP 790 (the official Python 3.15 Release Schedule) also lists \"3.15.0 final: Friday, 2026-10-09\" under the \"Actual\" schedule [3]. The Python Insider blog announcement \"Python 3.15.0 (final) is here!\" was published on October 9, 2026 [2].\n\nNote: The release was originally planned for October 1, 2026, but was postponed by one week due to last-minute lazy-import release blockers, which led to an additional release candidate (3.15.0rc3) on October 2, 2026 [1][3].\n\n**Release manager:** PEP 790 explicitly states \"3.15 release manager: Hugo van Kemenade\" [3]. The Python.org release page also thanks \"the Sovereign Tech Agency for supporting Hugo van Kemenade's work as release manager for Python 3.14 and 3.15\" [1], and the Python Insider announcement is signed by \"Your release team, Hugo van Kemenade, Ned Deily, Steve Dower\" [2].\n\n**Sources:**\n- [1] Python.org \u2013 Python Release Python 3.15.0: https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3150/\n- [2] Python Insider \u2013 Python 3.15.0 (final) is here!: https://blog.python.org/2026/10/python-3150-final-is-here/\n- [3] PEP 790 \u2013 Python 3.15 Release Schedule: https://peps.python.org/pep-0790/\n\nANSWER: 2026-10-09; Hugo van Kemenade", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-010", "category": "grounding", "title": "Vega-C flight VV30 payloads", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 13422, "turns": 1, "retries": 2, "usage": {"search_calls": 5, "output_tokens": 831, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 798, "search_tokens": 23068, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1964, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Copernicus Sentinel-3C; FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer)", "expected": "FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer); Copernicus Sentinel-3C", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 5}, "workflow_id": "0sfj321ca4b5-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2ff16ea6-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:24-0500", "answer": "Europe's Vega-C rocket launched two satellites on flight VV30 in September 2026:\n\n1. **Copernicus Sentinel-3C** \u2014 the third satellite of the EU's Copernicus Sentinel-3 mission, dedicated to monitoring oceans, land, ice and the atmosphere (managed by EUMETSAT, built by Thales Alenia Space).\n\n2. **FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer)** \u2014 ESA's eighth Earth Explorer mission, designed to monitor vegetation health from space by detecting the faint fluorescence emitted by plants during photosynthesis.\n\nThe VV30 mission lifted off on **15 September 2026 at 03:21 CEST** (14 September at 22:21 local time) from Europe's Spaceport in Kourou, French Guiana. It was the second Vega-C launch operated solely by Avio (rather than jointly with Arianespace) and the eighth Vega-C flight overall. Both satellites were deployed into Sun-synchronous orbit, with Sentinel-3C separating first, followed by FLEX about an hour later.\n\n**Sources:**\n- ESA: \"FLEX and Sentinel-3C launched\" \u2014 https://www.esa.int/Applications/Observing_the_Earth/FLEX_and_Sentinel-3C_launched\n- ESA Multimedia: \"Vega-C flight VV30 with FLEX and Sentinel-3C\" \u2014 https://www.esa.int/ESA_Multimedia/Images/2026/09/Vega-C_flight_VV30_with_FLEX_and_Sentinel-3C\n- Avio press release: \"AVIO TO LAUNCH COPERNICUS SENTINEL-3C AND FLEX SATELLITES ON SEPTEMBER 14th 2026 ON VEGA C\" \u2014 https://www.avio.com/press-release/avio-to-launch-copernicus-sentinel-3-c-and-flex-satellites-on-september-14th-2026-on-vega-c\n- Spaceflight Now: \"Avio launches pair of climate monitoring European spacecraft to study plants, oceans and atmospheric changes\" \u2014 https://spaceflightnow.com/2026/09/15/avio-launches-pair-of-climate-monitoring-european-spacecraft-to-study-plants-oceans-and-atmospheric-changes/\n- NASASpaceFlight.com: \"Vega C set to launch the ESA Sentinel-3C and FLEX missions from Kourou\" \u2014 https://www.nasaspaceflight.com/2026/09/vega-c-launch-sentinel-3c-flex/\n\nANSWER: Copernicus Sentinel-3C; FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer)", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-008", "category": "grounding", "title": "Kubernetes v1.37 release name and date", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 12364, "turns": 1, "retries": 2, "usage": {"search_calls": 5, "output_tokens": 530, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 804, "search_tokens": 19323, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1458, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Garhwal; 2026-08-26", "expected": "Garhwal; 2026-08-26", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 3}, "workflow_id": "0sfj328be167-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2ff16ea7-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:28-0500", "answer": "Based on my web search and verification from official sources:\n\n**Release name:** Kubernetes v1.37 is codenamed **\"Garhwal\"** (\u0917\u0922\u093c\u0935\u093e\u0932, pronounced *ga\u1e5bhv\u0101l*), named after the Himalayan region of Uttarakhand, India. This is confirmed by the official Kubernetes blog post titled \"Kubernetes v1.37: Garhwal\" [kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release/](https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release/) and the SIG Release repository README [github.com/kubernetes/sig-release/tree/master/releases/release-1.37](https://github.com/kubernetes/sig-release/tree/master/releases/release-1.37).\n\n**Release date:** Kubernetes v1.37.0 was released on **Wednesday, August 26, 2026**. This is confirmed by:\n- The official Kubernetes blog post dated \"Wednesday, August 26, 2026\" [kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release/](https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release/)\n- The GitHub release page for v1.37.0 showing \"k8s-release-robot released this 26 Aug\" with source code assets timestamped \"2026-08-26T10:44:20Z\" [github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/releases/tag/v1.37.0](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/releases/tag/v1.37.0)\n- The SIG Release timeline showing \"Wednesday 26th August 2026: Week 15 \u2014 Kubernetes v1.37.0 released\" [github.com/kubernetes/sig-release/tree/master/releases/release-1.37](https://github.com/kubernetes/sig-release/tree/master/releases/release-1.37)\n\nANSWER: Garhwal; 2026-08-26", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-007", "category": "grounding", "title": "Python 3.15.0 release date and release manager", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 17031, "turns": 1, "retries": 2, "usage": {"search_calls": 4, "output_tokens": 1221, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 814, "search_tokens": 15873, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1825, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2300, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "2026-10-09; Hugo van Kemenade", "expected": "2026-10-09; Hugo van Kemenade", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 4}, "workflow_id": "0sfj30e3d654-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2ff14795-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:28-0500", "answer": "I'll search the web for this information.The search results strongly indicate the answer. Let me verify against the official python.org pages directly.I found and verified the information from official Python sources.\n\n**Final release date:** The official Python 3.15.0 download page (python.org) states \"Release date: Oct. 9, 2026\" and identifies it as \"the stable release of Python 3.15.0.\" This followed a surprise third release candidate (3.15.0rc3, released Oct 2, 2026) that pushed the final release back about a week from the originally planned date in PEP 790. The Python Insider announcement \"Python 3.15.0 (final) is here!\" confirms this is the final (non-release-candidate) release, containing 5,643 commits from 1,012 contributors.\n\n**Release manager:** The release announcement is signed by the release team \u2014 Hugo van Kemenade, Ned Deily, and Steve Dower \u2014 with Hugo van Kemenade explicitly thanking the Sovereign Tech Agency \"for supporting my work as release manager for Python 3.14 and 3.15.\" This is corroborated by the Python Steering Council announcement on discuss.python.org (\"Python 3.14/3.15 Release Manager\") naming @hugovk (Hugo van Kemenade) as the release manager, and by his own release-day blog post \"Releasing Python 3.15.0.\"\n\n**Sources:**\n- https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3150/ \u2014 official release page: \"Release date: Oct. 9, 2026\"\n- https://blog.python.org/2026/10/python-3150-final-is-here/ \u2014 official final release announcement, signed by release manager Hugo van Kemenade\n- https://discuss.python.org/t/python-3-14-3-15-release-manager/51812 \u2014 Steering Council announcement of Hugo van Kemenade as 3.14/3.15 release manager\n- https://hugovk.dev/blog/2026/releasing-python-3-15-0/ \u2014 release manager's own account of the 3.15.0 release\n\nANSWER: 2026-10-09; Hugo van Kemenade", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-010", "category": "grounding", "title": "Vega-C flight VV30 payloads", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 13275, "turns": 1, "retries": 2, "usage": {"search_calls": 2, "output_tokens": 1200, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 798, "search_tokens": 17394, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1982, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2245, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Sentinel-3C; FLEX", "expected": "FLEX (Fluorescence Explorer); Copernicus Sentinel-3C", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 0}, "workflow_id": "0sfj321ccbc6-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2ff16ea6-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:30-0500", "answer": "Europe's Vega-C rocket flew mission VV30 on 15 September 2026 (03:21 CEST / 01:21 UTC, which was the evening of 14 September local time in French Guiana), lifting off from Europe's Spaceport in Kourou, French Guiana. It was a dual launch operated by Avio, carrying two Earth-observation satellites stacked with a Vespa secondary payload adapter, with Sentinel-3C deployed first.\n\nThe two satellites were:\n\n1. **Copernicus Sentinel-3C** \u2014 the third satellite of the EU Copernicus programme's Sentinel-3 mission (managed by EUMETSAT), for ocean and atmosphere monitoring, built by Thales Alenia Space.\n2. **FLEX (FLuorescence EXplorer)** \u2014 ESA's eighth Earth Explorer mission, which maps vegetation fluorescence to quantify photosynthetic activity and plant health, also built by Thales Alenia Space.\n\nSources:\n- ESA \u2014 \"Vega-C flight VV30 with FLEX and Sentinel-3C\": \"ESA's FLEX and the Copernicus Sentinel-3C satellite are flying to space on Vega-C flight VV30 from Europe's Spaceport in French Guiana. A dual launch, the two satellites are fitted inside Vega-C's fairing with a secondary payload adapter called Vespa and are deployed into orbit in turn with Sentinel-3C deploying first.\" [search-result://qc5AXrmP]\n- Spaceflight Now \u2014 \"Onboard the launch with the designation VV30 were two spacecraft: the ocean- and atmosphere-monitoring Copernicus Sentinel-3C, managed by EUMETSAT, and the plant health-monitoring Fluorescence Explorer (FLEX), managed by ESA.\" [search-result://WgZFZ9nK, search-result://pMfih46U]\n- Wikipedia (FLEX satellite) \u2014 \"FLEX and Sentinel-3C satellite launched together aboard a Vega-C rocket... on 15 September 2026.\" [search-result://RyhI7L9S]\n- Gunter's Space Page (Vega-C launch list) \u2014 \"Vega-C VV30 15.09.2026 ... Sentinel 3C / FLEX.\" [search-result://G6qIeE5j]\n- GlobeNewswire / S\u00f2phia High Tech \u2014 \"VV30 carried two European Earth observation satellites... Copernicus Sentinel-3C... and FLEX...\" [search-result://kBm1atvW]\n\nANSWER: Sentinel-3C; FLEX", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-008", "category": "grounding", "title": "Kubernetes v1.37 release name and date", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 16350, "turns": 1, "retries": 2, "usage": {"search_calls": 5, "output_tokens": 1193, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 804, "search_tokens": 20413, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1645, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 2123, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "Garhwal; 2026-08-26", "expected": "Garhwal; 2026-08-26", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 3}, "workflow_id": "0sfj328be16a-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2ff16ea7-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:32-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the Kubernetes v1.37 release name and date.The search results point clearly to the official sources. Let me open the authoritative Kubernetes blog post and the sig-release page to confirm the codename and exact release date.I have confirmed the details from authoritative Kubernetes sources.\n\n**Findings:**\n\n- **Release name:** Kubernetes v1.37 is codenamed **Garhwal** (\u0917\u0922\u093cETTOVAL, pronounced *ga\u1e5bhv\u0101l*), named after the Himalayan region of Uttarakhand, India. The official announcement is titled \"Kubernetes v1.37: Garhwal\" and states: \"The theme for Kubernetes v1.37 is **Garhwal** ... a Himalayan region of Uttarakhand, India.\" [kubernetes.io blog](https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release/)\n- **v1.37.0 release date:** The Kubernetes sig-release schedule lists \"**Wednesday 26th August 2026**: Week 15 \u2014 Kubernetes v1.37.0 released,\" and the GitHub release page for tag `v1.37.0` shows it was published on **26 Aug 2026** (assets timestamped 2026-08-26T10:44:20Z). [kubernetes/sig-release](https://github.com/kubernetes/sig-release/tree/master/releases/release-1.37) \u00b7 [kubernetes/kubernetes release v1.37.0](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/releases/tag/v1.37.0)\n\n**Sources cited:**\n1. Kubernetes Blog \u2014 \"Kubernetes v1.37: Garhwal\" (Aug 26, 2026): https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release/\n2. kubernetes/sig-release \u2014 release-1.37 README & timeline: https://github.com/kubernetes/sig-release/tree/master/releases/release-1.37\n3. kubernetes/kubernetes \u2014 Release v1.37.0 (tag page): https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/releases/tag/v1.37.0\n\nANSWER: Garhwal; 2026-08-26", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-011", "category": "grounding", "title": "US 2025 median household income and poverty rate", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 16130, "turns": 1, "retries": 2, "usage": {"search_calls": 3, "output_tokens": 1091, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 822, "search_tokens": 15001, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1646, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1986, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "$87,460; 10.2%", "expected": "$87,460; 10.2%", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 3}, "workflow_id": "0sfj32b6f2bb-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2ff195ba-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:35-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the U.S. Census Bureau's September 2026 income and poverty report to find these figures.The search results are consistent across multiple sources. Let me verify by opening the official Census Bureau press release directly.I've confirmed the figures directly from the official U.S. Census Bureau press release (Press Release CB26-151, released Tuesday, September 15, 2026), titled \"Income, Poverty and Health Insurance Coverage in the United States: 2025.\"\n\n**Key findings from the report** (based on the 2026 Current Population Survey Annual Social and Economic Supplement, covering calendar year 2025):\n\n1. **Real median household income in 2025: $87,460** \u2014 an increase of 2.6% from the 2024 estimate of $85,210, and the highest on record dating back to 1967.\n2. **Official poverty rate in 2025: 10.2%** \u2014 a decline of 0.5 percentage points from 2024, representing 34.5 million people in poverty. (The Supplemental Poverty Measure rate was 13.1%, not statistically different from 2024.)\n\n**Sources cited:**\n- U.S. Census Bureau press release, \"Income, Poverty and Health Insurance Coverage in the United States: 2025\" (Sept. 15, 2026): https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/income-poverty-health-insurance-coverage.html\n- U.S. Census Bureau report, \"Income in the United States: 2025\" (P60-289): https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2026/demo/p60-289.html\n- U.S. Census Bureau report, \"Poverty in the United States: 2025\" (P60-290): https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2026/demo/p60-290.html\n- Corroborating coverage: CNBC (Sept. 15, 2026) and WBIW/Stateline (Sept. 15, 2026)\n\nANSWER: $87,460; 10.2%", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-011", "category": "grounding", "title": "US 2025 median household income and poverty rate", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 18770, "turns": 1, "retries": 2, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 527, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 822, "search_tokens": 23885, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1124, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "$87,460; 10.2%", "expected": "$87,460; 10.2%", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 3}, "workflow_id": "0sfj32b6cba8-d02c-11f1-ba7a-56adf5b8ca14", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2ff195ba-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:38-0500", "answer": "According to the U.S. Census Bureau's September 15, 2026 release of the 2025 income and poverty data (based on the 2026 Current Population Survey Annual Social and Economic Supplement):\n\n- **Real median household income in 2025 was $87,460** \u2014 an increase of 2.6% from the 2024 estimate of $85,210, and the highest on record dating back to 1967. [Source: Census Bureau press release CB26-151](https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/income-poverty-health-insurance-coverage.html); [Income in the United States: 2025 (P60-289)](https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2026/demo/p60-289.html)\n- **The official poverty rate in 2025 was 10.2%** \u2014 down 0.5 percentage points from 2024, with 34.5 million people in poverty. (For reference, the Supplemental Poverty Measure rate was 13.1%, not statistically different from 2024.) [Source: Census Bureau press release CB26-151](https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/income-poverty-health-insurance-coverage.html); [Poverty in the United States: 2025 (P60-290)](https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2026/demo/p60-290.html)\n\nANSWER: $87,460; 10.2%", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "grounding-006", "category": "grounding", "title": "2026 Asian Games medal table leader", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 30491, "turns": 1, "retries": 2, "usage": {"search_calls": 6, "output_tokens": 1867, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 814, "search_tokens": 18542, "cached_input_tokens": null}, "answer_chars": 1361, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 4596, "detail": {"pass": true, "score": 1.0, "extracted": "China; 169", "expected": "China; 169", "answer_line_found": true, "pattern_misses": [], "cited": true, "citation_count": 0}, "workflow_id": "0sfj3200df44-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj2ff14794-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:42-0500", "answer": "I'll search for the 2026 Asian Games medal table results.**China** finished top of the medal table at the 20th Asian Games in Aichi\u2013Nagoya, Japan (held 19 September \u2013 4 October 2026), winning **169 gold medals** (along with 89 silver and 83 bronze, 341 total) \u2014 its 12th consecutive Asian Games medal-table title and its best haul at an overseas Asiad.\n\nThis is confirmed by multiple independent sources:\n- **Xinhua** (4 Oct 2026): \"China topping the gold medal table for the 12th consecutive edition, and finishing with 169 gold, 89 silver and 83 bronze medals\" [search-result://FH7lpTBD]\n- **CCTV English**: \"topping the gold medal table for a record 12th straight Asian Games, securing 169 gold, 89 silver and 83 bronze medals\" [search-result://zPIopMYK]\n- **Wikipedia \u2013 2026 Asian Games medal table**: rank 1 shows 169 gold, 89 silver, 83 bronze, 341 total [search-result://DbeORJ3Q]\n- **Times of India medal tally**: \"China: 169 Gold | 89 Silver | 83 Bronze | Total: 341\" [search-result://IpVF6SdY]\n- **Rediff Sports** and **Mathrubhumi**: both report China topped the table with 169 gold, 89 silver, 83 bronze (341 total) [search-result://Dlt2niha] [search-result://95YdI9Ol]\n\n(Note: one outlet, insidethegames.biz, reported 189 gold, but this conflicts with the official-style tally and all other sources, and appears to be an error.)\n\nANSWER: China; 169", "rescored": "grounding citation rule v3 (URL, website or provider reference link)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-005", "category": "your_data", "title": "Time in lieu for overnight incidents", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1650, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 93, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4151, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 347, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 60, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4438, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly awards 8 hours for the two overnight incidents exceeding 45 minutes and states that the time must be used within 30 days of each incident.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c04ade1-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d54-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:48-0500", "answer": "Based on section 5 of the handbook:\n\n**Time in lieu owed: 8 hours** (4 hours for each overnight incident lasting more than 45 minutes)\n\n- 30-minute incident: no time in lieu (under 45 minutes)\n- 70-minute incident: 4 hours\n- 2-hour incident: 4 hours\n\n**Deadline:** You must take the time in lieu within **30 days of each incident**, or it expires."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-005", "category": "your_data", "title": "Time in lieu for overnight incidents", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1313, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 73, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4094, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4040}, "answer_chars": 276, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 60, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4417, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly awards 8 hours for the two overnight incidents lasting more than 45 minutes and states that each allotment expires 30 days after its incident.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c04addf-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d54-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:48-0500", "answer": "You\u2019re owed **8 hours of time in lieu**: 4 hours each for the 70-minute and 2-hour overnight incidents. The 30-minute incident doesn\u2019t qualify; incidents must last **more than 45 minutes**.\n\nYou must use each 4-hour allotment **within 30 days of its incident**, or it expires."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-005", "category": "your_data", "title": "Time in lieu for overnight incidents", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1333, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 67, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4321, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 263, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 90, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4410, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": ["re:\\b8\\s*(hours|hrs|h)\\b"], "pass": false}, "judge": {"score": 2, "reason": "The answer gives the correct 30-day deadline but incorrectly totals the entitlement as 4 hours instead of 8 hours for the two qualifying incidents.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": ["The claim that only 4 hours of time in lieu are owed is unsupported; both the 70-minute and 2-hour incidents qualify, totaling 8 hours."], "faithful": false}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c04ade2-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d54-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:48-0500", "answer": "You are owed **4 hours of time in lieu** for the overnight incident that lasted **70 minutes** (the 30-minute incident does not qualify, and the 2-hour incident only counts as one 4-hour block).\n\nThis time in lieu must be taken **within 30 days** of the incident."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-003", "category": "your_data", "title": "Platinum downtime budget", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2209, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 130, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4085, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4040}, "answer_chars": 503, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 55, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4491, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates the Platinum downtime allowance and credit thresholds, and its additional request deadline and contract precedence statements are supported by the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c17729f-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d52-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:48-0500", "answer": "For a Platinum customer, the monthly API uptime commitment is **99.95%**. In a 30-day month (43,200 minutes), that allows **21.6 minutes of downtime** before a service credit applies.\n\n- **More than 21.6 minutes:** credit of **10% of that month\u2019s fees**.\n- **More than 432 minutes** (uptime below 99.0%): credit of **25% of that month\u2019s fees**.\n\nThe customer must request the credit within **30 days after the affected month ends**. A signed customer contract overrides the handbook if its terms differ."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-003", "category": "your_data", "title": "Platinum downtime budget", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2959, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 255, "reasoning_tokens": 119, "input_tokens": 4085, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4040}, "answer_chars": 527, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 58, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4491, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates 21.6 minutes of allowed downtime, states both credit thresholds and amounts, and accurately includes the request deadline and contract precedence.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c1772a1-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d52-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:50-0500", "answer": "For Platinum, the API uptime commitment is **99.95% per calendar month**.\n\n- In a **30-day month**, that allows **21.6 minutes of downtime (21 minutes, 36 seconds)**. More downtime puts uptime below the commitment.\n- The credit is **10% of that month\u2019s fees** if uptime falls below 99.95%.\n- If uptime falls below **99.0%**, the credit is **25% of that month\u2019s fees**.\n\nThe customer must request the credit within **30 days after the affected month ends**. A signed customer contract overrides the handbook if its terms differ."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-003", "category": "your_data", "title": "Platinum downtime budget", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2665, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 120, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4312, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 367, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 78, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4470, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates the 21.6-minute downtime allowance and states the 10% monthly-fee credit, rising to 25% when uptime falls below 99.0%, though it leaves the exactly 99.0% boundary implicit.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c1772a2-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d52-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:50-0500", "answer": "For a Platinum customer in a 30-day month, the API downtime threshold before owing a service credit is **21.6 minutes** (calculated as 0.05% of 30 days).\n\nIf monthly uptime falls below 99.95% (but above 99.0%), the service credit is **10% of that month's fees**. If uptime falls below 99.0%, the credit increases to **25% of that month's fees**. (Section 8.2 and 8.3)"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2331, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 144, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4040}, "answer_chars": 499, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 96, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4538, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 4, "reason": "The answer correctly rejects 15:00 and calculates the 90-minute rollout, but gives a latest start strictly before 14:30 rather than the rubric's required 14:30, consistent with a literal reading of the document's 'before 16:00' wording.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c54f999-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdccb79-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:51-0500", "answer": "No. Friday deploys must reach **100% of traffic before 16:00 UTC**. The Normal rollout requires 30 minutes at 5%, then 60 minutes at 25%\u201490 minutes before reaching 100%.\n\nA 15:00 start would reach 100% at 16:30, so it is not allowed. You would need to start **before 14:30 UTC** (14:30 exactly reaches 100% at 16:00, not before). Friday deploys may start no earlier than 14:00 UTC, so the available start window is **14:00 to before 14:30 UTC**, assuming required approvals and no applicable freeze."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3098, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 193, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4141, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 681, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 115, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4584, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 3, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates the 90-minute rollout, 16:30 completion, and reference latest start of 14:30, but contradicts those conclusions by initially saying the 15:00 start is allowed.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": ["The opening claim that starting this Normal deploy at 15:00 UTC on Friday is allowed contradicts the required rollout duration and Friday cutoff."], "faithful": false}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c54f99a-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdccb79-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:51-0500", "answer": "Yes, starting at 15:00 UTC on Friday is allowed \u2014 but with a condition.\n\nPer section 7.2, Friday production deploys may start from 14:00 UTC, **and the change must reach 100% of traffic before 16:00 UTC**.\n\nSince your change is a Normal change, it must follow the progressive rollout in section 7.3:\n1. Canary at 5% for 30 minutes\n2. 25% for 60 minutes\n3. 100%\n\nThat's a minimum of **90 minutes** of rollout stages. Starting at 15:00 UTC means you'd reach 100% at 16:30 UTC \u2014 which violates the Friday rule.\n\n**The latest you could start is 14:30 UTC**, which would get you to 100% traffic by 16:00 UTC (assuming each stage takes its full minimum duration and there are no delays)."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-001", "category": "your_data", "title": "SEV-1 status page cadence", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1290, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 37, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4080}, "answer_chars": 156, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 56, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4337, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4334}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer matches the documented SEV-1 cadence: first update within 20 minutes of declaration, then every 30 minutes until resolved.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c431697-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d53-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:52-0500", "answer": "The first status page update must go out **within 20 minutes of declaration**. After that, post updates **every 30 minutes until the incident is resolved**."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-001", "category": "your_data", "title": "SEV-1 status page cadence", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1244, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 47, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4308, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 176, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 65, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4348, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states the SEV-1 status update deadlines of within 20 minutes of declaration and every 30 minutes thereafter until resolved, as specified in Section 2.1.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c433da9-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d53-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:53-0500", "answer": "The first status page update for a SEV-1 must go out **within 20 minutes of declaration**. After that, updates must be posted **every 30 minutes until resolved** (Section 2.1)."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-005", "category": "your_data", "title": "Time in lieu for overnight incidents", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6873, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 559, "reasoning_tokens": 461, "input_tokens": 4151, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 353, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1862, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 63, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4444, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly awards 8 hours for the two overnight incidents exceeding 45 minutes and states that the time must be used within 30 days of each incident or it expires.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c0486ce-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d54-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:53-0500", "answer": "You\u2019re owed **8 hours** of time in lieu.\n\nPer section 5, you get 4 hours for each **overnight incident lasting more than 45 minutes**:\n\n- 30-minute incident: **0 hours** \u2014 it does not exceed 45 minutes.\n- 70-minute incident: **4 hours**.\n- 2-hour incident: **4 hours**.\n\nYou must take the time in lieu **within 30 days of each incident**, or it expires."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-003", "category": "your_data", "title": "Platinum downtime budget", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4630, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 246, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4143, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 886, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 69, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4602, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates 21.6 minutes of permitted downtime in a 30-day month and states the documented 10% and 25% credit tiers, along with the supported request and processing deadlines.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c1799b3-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d52-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:53-0500", "answer": "I can answer this from the handbook.\n\n**Platinum uptime commitment:** 99.95% per calendar month (section 8.2).\n\n**Allowed downtime in a 30-day month:** 30 days \u00d7 24 hours \u00d7 60 minutes = 43,200 minutes. At 99.95% uptime, the maximum allowable downtime is 0.05% of that:\n\n43,200 \u00d7 0.0005 = **21.6 minutes** of API downtime per month.\n\nSo if a Platinum customer's API is down for more than **21.6 minutes** in a calendar month, their monthly uptime falls below the 99.95% commitment.\n\n**Service credit if missed (section 8.3):**\n- If monthly uptime falls below 99.95% (but at or above 99.0%): a credit of **10% of that month's fees**.\n- If monthly uptime falls below 99.0%: the credit increases to **25% of that month's fees**.\n\nNote that the customer must request the credit within 30 days of the end of the affected month, and Customer Success processes requests within 10 business days."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2210, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 160, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4309, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 658, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 63, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4535, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the holiday freeze exception for CVSS 9.0+ patches, VP of Engineering approval, progressive rollout, and CAB register logging within one business day.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c9b39a3-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca465-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:53-0500", "answer": "The document states:\n\n- During the **Holiday freeze** (December 18 through January 4), only **Standard and Emergency changes** are allowed.\n- An exception is made for a patch for a security vulnerability rated **CVSS 9.0 or higher**, which may ship as a **Normal change** with approval from the **VP of Engineering**.\n- The patch must still follow the **progressive rollout** in section 7.3.\n- Every freeze exception must be logged in the **CAB register** within 1 business day.\n\nSince the vulnerability is CVSS 9.3 (above the 9.0 threshold), you may ship the patch on December 22 as a **Normal change**, but you need **approval from the VP of Engineering**."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-001", "category": "your_data", "title": "SEV-1 status page cadence", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 3024, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 248, "reasoning_tokens": 148, "input_tokens": 4139, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 424, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 624, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 58, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4400, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer gives the correct SEV-1 status update cadence, and its additional statements about role separation and Platinum customer notification are supported by the document.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c431695-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d53-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:54-0500", "answer": "For a SEV-1, the first status page update must go out **within 20 minutes of declaration**, and subsequent updates must be posted **every 30 minutes until resolved** (section 2.1).\n\nAlso note: for a SEV-1, the Communications Lead must be a different person from the Incident Commander (section 3), and each affected Platinum customer must receive a direct email from their TAM within 60 minutes of declaration (section 8.4)."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-006", "category": "your_data", "title": "Incident chat log retention", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1035, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 18, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4063, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4040}, "answer_chars": 81, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 44, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4269, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer matches the documented retention period of 400 days followed by automatic deletion.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6cadd759-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca467-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:54-0500", "answer": "Incident channel chat logs are kept for **400 days**, then deleted automatically."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2020, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 118, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4040}, "answer_chars": 522, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 63, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4494, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the holiday-freeze exception, required VP approval, Normal-change rollout and CAB logging deadline, and adds supported owning-team, conditional CAB and deploy-window requirements.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c9b39a4-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca465-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:55-0500", "answer": "Yes. December 22 is during the holiday freeze, but a CVSS 9.3 patch qualifies for the exception for vulnerabilities rated **9.0 or higher**.\n\nShip it as a **Normal change** with:\n- **VP of Engineering approval** for the freeze exception.\n- **One approval from the owning team**; also CAB approval if the change is high-risk (schema, network/ACL, or authentication changes).\n\nIt must follow the Normal progressive rollout and applicable deploy window. Log the freeze exception in the **CAB register within 1 business day**."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-006", "category": "your_data", "title": "Incident chat log retention", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1263, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 18, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4063, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4040}, "answer_chars": 81, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 45, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4269, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4266}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer exactly matches the documented retention period of 400 days followed by automatic deletion.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6cadd758-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca467-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:55-0500", "answer": "Incident channel chat logs are kept for **400 days**, then deleted automatically."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-003", "category": "your_data", "title": "Platinum downtime budget", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 8262, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 732, "reasoning_tokens": 609, "input_tokens": 4143, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 432, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 1989, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 71, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4479, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly calculates the 21.6-minute downtime allowance from Platinum's 99.95% commitment and states the documented 10% credit, increasing to 25% below 99.0% uptime.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c1772a0-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d52-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:55-0500", "answer": "For a Platinum customer, the monthly uptime commitment is **99.95%** (section 8.2).\n\nIn a 30-day month (43,200 minutes), that allows **21.6 minutes** of API downtime before the commitment is breached.\n\nIf monthly uptime falls below 99.95%, the service credit is **10% of that month's fees**. If uptime falls below 99.0% (432 minutes of downtime in a 30-day month), the credit increases to **25%** of that month's fees (section 8.3)."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-005", "category": "your_data", "title": "Time in lieu for overnight incidents", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2108, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 72, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4094, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4040}, "answer_chars": 285, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 61, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4416, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly awards 8 hours for the two overnight incidents lasting more than 45 minutes and states that each allotment expires 30 days after its respective incident.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c04ade0-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d54-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:55-0500", "answer": "You\u2019re owed **8 hours of time in lieu**: 4 hours each for the 70-minute and 2-hour overnight incidents. The 30-minute incident doesn\u2019t qualify because incidents must last **more than 45 minutes**.\n\nUse each 4-hour allotment **within 30 days of its respective incident**, or it expires."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-006", "category": "your_data", "title": "Incident chat log retention", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1251, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 27, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4119, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 124, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 49, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4280, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer accurately states the section 10.1 retention policy of 400 days followed by automatic deletion.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6cadd757-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca467-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:55-0500", "answer": "According to section 10.1 of the handbook, incident channel chat logs are kept for **400 days**, then deleted automatically."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-002", "category": "your_data", "title": "Escalating an unmitigated API error spike", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2012, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 156, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4092, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4089}, "answer_chars": 639, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 71, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4617, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies SEV-2, explains primary and Tier 2 paging with declaration-based timing, and gives both documented Director of Reliability escalation triggers.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6da93f3a-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca466-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:57-0500", "answer": "This meets **SEV-2** criteria: API errors above 5% for 10 consecutive minutes.\n\nEscalation timers run **from declaration**, not from when errors began. If it has been at least 45 minutes since declaration:\n- **On-call primary:** paged at declaration; the secondary is automatically paged if the primary hasn\u2019t acknowledged within 15 minutes.\n- **Owning team\u2019s service owner:** paged after 45 minutes without mitigation.\n\nPage the **Director of Reliability** if either:\n- The SEV-2 lasts **more than 3 hours from declaration to resolution**, even if it has been mitigated; or\n- This is the **third SEV-2 on the same service within 7 days**."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4128, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 294, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4139, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 1182, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 123, "reasoning_tokens": 34, "input_tokens": 4660, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the holiday-freeze exception for CVSS 9.0+ patches, VP of Engineering approval, Normal-change progressive rollout, and CAB-register logging deadline, with additional requirements consistent with the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c9b39a2-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca465-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:57-0500", "answer": "Yes \u2014 you can ship it on December 22. December 18 through January 4 is the holiday freeze, during which only Standard and Emergency changes are normally allowed. However, there's an explicit exception: **a patch for a security vulnerability rated CVSS 9.0 or higher may ship as a Normal change with approval from the VP of Engineering.**\n\nSo for your CVSS 9.3 patch on the warehouse sync service:\n\n- **Approval needed:** VP of Engineering (Tobias Renwick)\n- **Change class:** Normal (not Standard, not Emergency \u2014 it's a planned patch, not an active incident mitigation)\n- **Rollout:** It must still follow the progressive rollout in section 7.3 (canary at 5% for 30 min \u2192 25% for 60 min \u2192 100%), with a tested rollback completing within 15 minutes\n- **Logging:** The freeze exception must be logged in the CAB register within 1 business day\n\nOne note: since it's a Normal change, if it's also high-risk (e.g., it involves schema, network/ACL, or authentication changes), it would additionally need CAB approval \u2014 but the CAB meets Tuesdays and Thursdays at 16:00 UTC, and December 22, 2026 is a Tuesday, so you'd need to submit by 12:00 UTC that day to be reviewed in that meeting."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-001", "category": "your_data", "title": "SEV-1 status page cadence", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1269, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 36, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4080}, "answer_chars": 151, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 56, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4336, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states the SEV-1 first-update deadline of 20 minutes from declaration and subsequent updates every 30 minutes until resolution.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c431696-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d53-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:57-0500", "answer": "The first status page update is due **within 20 minutes of declaration**. After that, post updates **every 30 minutes until the incident is resolved**."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2298, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 152, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4312, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4224}, "answer_chars": 502, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 70, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4529, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": ["16:30"], "pass": false}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly rejects a 15:00 UTC start, explains the 90-minute progressive rollout and Friday 16:00 UTC cutoff, and gives the reference's latest start of 14:30 UTC.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c54f998-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdccb79-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:58-0500", "answer": "The document states:\n\n- **Friday**: production deploys may start from **14:00 UTC**, and the change must reach **100% of traffic before 16:00 UTC**.\n- **Progressive rollout** (for Normal changes) takes at least **90 minutes** (30 min canary + 60 min 25% stage).\n\nSince your deploy is a **Normal change**, you must complete the rollout by **16:00 UTC**, meaning the latest you could start is **14:30 UTC** (not 15:00 UTC). Starting at **15:00 UTC** would not allow enough time to finish by the deadline."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-007", "category": "your_data", "title": "Postmortem draft vs customer RCA deadlines", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1435, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 57, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4079, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4040}, "answer_chars": 236, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 48, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4383, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states both deadlines from resolution and accurately defines business days as excluding weekends and company holidays.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6dd78a77-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca468-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:58-0500", "answer": "For a SEV-1, measured from **resolution**:\n\n- **Internal postmortem draft:** due within **3 business days**.\n- **Customer-facing RCA:** published within **5 business days**.\n\nBusiness days exclude weekends and Ferngate company holidays."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-001", "category": "your_data", "title": "SEV-1 status page cadence", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 997, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 47, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4139, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 176, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 56, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4352, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4349}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states the SEV-1 status page cadence: within 20 minutes of declaration, then every 30 minutes until resolved.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c433da8-d02c-11f1-9071-46362399c705", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdc7d53-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:58-0500", "answer": "Per the handbook (section 2.1), for a SEV-1:\n\n- **First status page update**: within **20 minutes of declaration**\n- **Subsequent updates**: **every 30 minutes** until resolved"}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-006", "category": "your_data", "title": "Incident chat log retention", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6029, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 143, "reasoning_tokens": 109, "input_tokens": 4119, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 147, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 529, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 59, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4285, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly states that incident channel chat logs are retained for 400 days and then deleted automatically, matching section 10.1 and the reference answer.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6cadd756-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca467-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:59-0500", "answer": "According to the Retention table in section 10.1 of the handbook, incident channel chat logs are kept for **400 days**, then deleted automatically."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-007", "category": "your_data", "title": "Postmortem draft vs customer RCA deadlines", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1420, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 70, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4136, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 285, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 72, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4399, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly gives the postmortem draft deadline as 3 business days and the SEV-1 customer-facing RCA deadline as 5 business days after resolution, with the optional review deadline also supported by the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6dd76363-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca468-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:59-0500", "answer": "Based on the handbook:\n\n- **Internal postmortem draft**: due within **3 business days of resolution** (section 9). The review meeting happens within 7 business days of resolution.\n- **Customer-facing RCA**: published within **5 business days of resolution** (section 8.4, for a SEV-1)."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-002", "category": "your_data", "title": "Escalating an unmitigated API error spike", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_off", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning off)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "none", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 4513, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 438, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4149, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 1584, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 60, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4892, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies SEV-2, the primary and service-owner paging requirements, and both Director escalation triggers, with additional escalation details supported by the handbook.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6da93f3e-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca466-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:59-0500", "answer": "Based on the handbook, here's the situation:\n\n**What severity this is:** An API error rate above 5% for 10 consecutive minutes is a **SEV-2 (Major)** \u2014 and at 50 minutes unmitigated, it's well past that threshold.\n\n**Who should have been paged by now:**\n\n| Tier | Who | Trigger | Status at 50 min unmitigated |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Tier 1 | On-call primary (secondary as backup) | Every incident, at declaration | \u2705 Paged at declaration |\n| Tier 2 | Owning team's service owner | SEV-2 with no mitigation after **45 minutes** | \u2705 **Should have been paged at 45 minutes** \u2014 you're at 50 |\n| Tier 3 | Director of Reliability | SEV-2 lasting more than **3 hours** | \u23f3 Not yet \u2014 at 3 hours from declaration |\n| Tier 4 | VP of Engineering and CTO | SEV-1 > 2 hours, or suspected data exposure | \u274c Not applicable (this is a SEV-2, no data exposure indicated) |\n\nAlso note: Beacon auto-escalates if a page isn't acknowledged \u2014 after 15 minutes for a SEV-2, the next person in the chain gets re-paged (section 6.2).\n\n**What would escalate this to the Director of Reliability (Tier 3):**\n- The SEV-2 **lasting more than 3 hours** (measured from declaration to resolution, not mitigation), **or**\n- This being the **third SEV-2 on the same service within 7 days**\n\n**One more thing:** If the error rate or impact worsens \u2014 e.g., a full outage of the customer API in any region, or more than 25% of active customers impacted \u2014 this would become a **SEV-1**, which changes the escalation clock significantly (Tier 2 at 20 min unmitigated, Director of Reliability at 60 minutes, VP/CTO at 2 hours)."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6148, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 282, "reasoning_tokens": 152, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4040}, "answer_chars": 561, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 75, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4500, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the holiday-freeze exception, required VP approval, progressive rollout, and CAB logging deadline, while accurately including the applicable Normal-change approvals and deploy-window constraints.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c9b60b5-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca465-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:27:59-0500", "answer": "**Yes.** December 22 falls within the holiday freeze, but a CVSS 9.3 patch qualifies for the exception for vulnerabilities rated **9.0 or higher**.\n\nShip it as a **Normal change** with:\n- **VP of Engineering approval** for the freeze exception.\n- **One approval from the owning team**.\n- **CAB approval as well** if it involves schema migrations, network/ACL changes, or authentication changes.\n\nYou must still follow the Normal-change progressive rollout and applicable deploy window, and log the freeze exception in the CAB register within **1 business day**."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-007", "category": "your_data", "title": "Postmortem draft vs customer RCA deadlines", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_low", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning low)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "low", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1472, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 53, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4079, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4040}, "answer_chars": 227, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 67, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4379, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly gives both deadlines from resolution\u20143 business days for the internal postmortem draft and 5 business days for the SEV-1 customer-facing RCA\u2014and accurately defines business days.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6dd76366-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca468-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:28:00-0500", "answer": "Both deadlines run from **resolution**:\n\n- **Internal postmortem draft:** within **3 business days**.\n- **Customer-facing RCA:** within **5 business days**.\n\nBusiness days are Monday\u2013Friday, excluding Ferngate company holidays."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-007", "category": "your_data", "title": "Postmortem draft vs customer RCA deadlines", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 2745, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 312, "reasoning_tokens": 218, "input_tokens": 4136, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 402, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 923, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 66, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4420, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly gives the postmortem draft deadline as 3 business days and the SEV-1 customer-facing RCA deadline as 5 business days from resolution, with supported additional details.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6dd76364-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca468-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:28:00-0500", "answer": "Per the handbook:\n\n- **Internal postmortem draft**: due within **3 business days of resolution** (Section 9). The review meeting follows within 7 business days, and the IC owns the postmortem.\n- **Customer-facing RCA**: must be published within **5 business days of resolution** (Section 8.4).\n\nBoth clocks start from resolution, so since you resolved it this afternoon, count business days from today."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": false, "score": 0.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 6033, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 275, "reasoning_tokens": 155, "input_tokens": 4083, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4040}, "answer_chars": 379, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 0.0, "pass": false, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 129, "reasoning_tokens": 35, "input_tokens": 4508, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 3, "reason": "The answer correctly rejects 15:00 and calculates the 90-minute rollout, but gives a start strictly before 14:30 rather than the rubric's required 14:30 latest start, although its stricter interpretation is supported by the document's wording 'before 16:00 UTC'.", "correct": false, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c54f997-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdccb79-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:28:00-0500", "answer": "No. The standard Normal rollout takes **90 minutes** before reaching 100%: 30 minutes at 5%, then 60 minutes at 25%.\n\nStarting at 15:00 UTC would reach 100% at 16:30, but Friday changes must reach 100% **before 16:00 UTC**.\n\nYou must therefore start **before 14:30 UTC**, and no earlier than 14:00 UTC. Starting exactly at 14:30 would reach 100% at 16:00\u2014not before the deadline."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-006", "category": "your_data", "title": "Incident chat log retention", "difficulty": "easy", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 885, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 25, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4288, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "answer_chars": 110, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 51, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4275, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer matches the document and reference: incident channel chat logs are retained for 400 days and then deleted automatically.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6cadfe6a-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca467-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:28:01-0500", "answer": "The document states that **incident channel chat logs** are kept for **400 days**, then deleted automatically."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-002", "category": "your_data", "title": "Escalating an unmitigated API error spike", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "sol_high", "config_label": "GPT-6.1 Sol (reasoning high)", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 8071, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 406, "reasoning_tokens": 172, "input_tokens": 4092, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4089}, "answer_chars": 901, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 103, "reasoning_tokens": 22, "input_tokens": 4689, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies SEV-2, the primary and conditional backup paging, the 45-minute Tier 2 threshold, and both Tier 3 triggers, while accurately clarifying that escalation timing starts at declaration rather than symptom onset.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6da93f3d-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca466-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:28:02-0500", "answer": "This meets **SEV-2** criteria: API errors above 5% for 10 consecutive minutes.\n\nWho should be paged:\n- **On-call primary:** at declaration.\n- **Secondary/next person in the chain:** automatically if the primary hasn\u2019t acknowledged within 15 minutes.\n- **Owning team\u2019s service owner (Tier 2):** if there is still no mitigation **45 minutes after declaration**.\n\n**The clock starts at declaration, not when errors first rose.** If you declared after the first 10 minutes of errors, you\u2019re about 40 minutes into the incident\u2014Tier 2 would be due in about 5 minutes if still unmitigated.\n\nPage **Director of Reliability Imogen Achterberg (Tier 3)** when:\n- This SEV-2 lasts **more than 3 hours**, measured from declaration to resolution\u2014even if mitigated; or\n- It is the **third SEV-2 on this service within 7 days**.\n\nIf it becomes SEV-1, Tier 3 is due once it lasts more than 60 minutes from declaration."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-002", "category": "your_data", "title": "Escalating an unmitigated API error spike", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 9131, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 948, "reasoning_tokens": 753, "input_tokens": 4149, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4076}, "answer_chars": 761, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 3167, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 66, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4658, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer matches the rubric by identifying SEV-2, the primary and Tier 2 service-owner paging requirements, and both Director of Reliability escalation triggers with the correct declaration-to-resolution timing.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6da93f3c-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca466-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:28:03-0500", "answer": "Assuming the incident was declared when the API error rate first stayed above 5% for 10 consecutive minutes, this is a **SEV-2**.\n\n- **At declaration:** page **Tier 1** \u2014 the on-call primary, with the secondary as backup. Beacon re-pages the next person if a SEV-2 page is unacknowledged after **15 minutes**.\n- **After 45 minutes without mitigation:** page **Tier 2** \u2014 the owning team\u2019s **service owner**. At about 50 minutes, the service owner should have been paged.\n\nIt escalates to the **Director of Reliability (Tier 3)** if either:\n\n- The SEV-2 lasts **more than 3 hours** from declaration to resolution, or\n- This is the **third SEV-2 on the same service within 7 days**.\n\n\u201cLasting\u201d is measured from declaration to resolution, not merely to mitigation."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-004", "category": "your_data", "title": "Security patch during the holiday freeze", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 17785, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 2255, "reasoning_tokens": 1988, "input_tokens": 4139, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 1057, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 8032, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 70, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4638, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly identifies the holiday-freeze exception for CVSS 9.0+ patches, requires VP of Engineering approval and progressive rollout, includes timely CAB logging, and accurately adds the applicable Normal-change requirements.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c9b60b6-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca465-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:28:09-0500", "answer": "Yes. December 22 falls inside the **holiday freeze** (December 18 through January 4, section 7.4), during which only Standard and Emergency changes are normally allowed. However, the freeze has an explicit exception: **a patch for a security vulnerability rated CVSS 9.0 or higher may ship as a Normal change with approval from the VP of Engineering** (section 7.4). CVSS 9.3 qualifies.\n\nApprovals/requirements:\n- **VP of Engineering approval** for the freeze exception.\n- As a **Normal change**, it also needs **one approval from the owning team** (Warehouse Sync) per section 7.1. If the patch is a schema migration, network/ACL change, or authentication change, it would additionally need CAB approval.\n- It must still follow the **progressive rollout** in section 7.3: canary at 5% for 30 minutes \u2192 25% for 60 minutes \u2192 100%, with a tested rollback completing within 15 minutes.\n- **Log the freeze exception in the CAB register within 1 business day.**\n- The deploy must still respect the deploy window in section 7.2 (Monday\u2013Thursday, 14:00\u201320:00 UTC)."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-002", "category": "your_data", "title": "Escalating an unmitigated API error spike", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 1957, "turns": 1, "retries": 1, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 132, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4320, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4224}, "answer_chars": 499, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 69, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4595, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly classifies the incident as SEV-2, identifies Tier 1 and the service owner as required pages, and gives both documented SEV-2 escalation triggers for the Director of Reliability.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6da93f3b-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca466-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:28:15-0500", "answer": "Based on the document:\n\n- **Who should have been paged by now**:\n  - **Tier 1**: On-call primary (and secondary as backup) at declaration (SEV-2).\n  - **Tier 2**: The owning team's service owner, since this is a SEV-2 with no mitigation after 45 minutes.\n\n- **What would escalate this to the Director of Reliability (Tier 3)**:\n  - The incident lasting more than 3 hours from declaration (measured to resolution, not mitigation).\n  - Or, this being the third SEV-2 on the same service within 7 days."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-007", "category": "your_data", "title": "Postmortem draft vs customer RCA deadlines", "difficulty": "medium", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l3", "config_label": "Mistral Large 3 (baseline)", "model": "mistral-large-2512", "reasoning_effort": null, "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 788, "turns": 1, "retries": 1, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 34, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4304, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 4224}, "answer_chars": 163, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 0, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 64, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4362, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer correctly gives both SEV-1 deadlines measured from resolution: 3 business days for the internal postmortem draft and 5 business days for the customer-facing RCA.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6dd76365-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdca468-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:28:20-0500", "answer": "The internal postmortem draft is due within **3 business days** of resolution.\n\nThe customer-facing RCA must be published within **5 business days** of resolution."}
{"run_id": "full-r1", "item_id": "your_data-008", "category": "your_data", "title": "Friday deploy with the standard canary", "difficulty": "hard", "repeat": 1, "config_id": "l4_high", "config_label": "Mistral Large 4 (reasoning high)", "model": "mistral-large-4", "reasoning_effort": "high", "pass": true, "score": 1.0, "api_ok": true, "error": null, "latency_ms": 33465, "turns": 1, "retries": 0, "usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 5032, "reasoning_tokens": 4862, "input_tokens": 4141, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 3564}, "answer_chars": 580, "finish_reason": "stop", "thinking_chars": 16229, "detail": {"score": 1.0, "pass": true, "judge_usage": {"search_calls": null, "output_tokens": 77, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4564, "search_tokens": null, "cached_input_tokens": 0}, "programmatic": {"missing_facts": [], "pass": true}, "judge": {"score": 5, "reason": "The answer matches the required 90-minute calculation, rejects the 15:00 start, and gives 14:30 UTC as the latest start, while appropriately noting the document's strict 'before 16:00' wording and freeze restrictions.", "correct": true, "parsed": true, "hallucinations": [], "faithful": true}}, "workflow_id": "0sfj6c54f996-d02c-11f1-89ad-1a5d2f4e051b", "parent_workflow_id": "0sfj6bdccb79-d02c-11f1-aff9-321d2204384c", "recorded_at": "2026-10-24T23:28:22-0500", "answer": "No. Under **section 7.2**, Friday production deploys must reach 100% of traffic **before 16:00 UTC**. A Normal change using the standard progressive rollout (**section 7.3**) takes **90 minutes**: 30 minutes at 5% (canary), then 60 minutes at 25%, before reaching 100%.\n\nStarting at 15:00 UTC would reach 100% at **16:30 UTC**, which violates the Friday rule.\n\nThe **latest you could start is 14:30 UTC** (reaching 100% at 16:00 UTC). If \"before 16:00\" is interpreted strictly, you should start by **14:29 UTC**.\n\n*(Also verify the date isn't in a change freeze per section 7.4.)*"}
